COLLDATA("qencen","en",[[246,"§Noon\nSee: ‘Alif-Laam-Meem’."],[247,"§Nuh(as)\nNuh(as) has been described forty-three times in the Holy Quran. Nuh(as) is one of the prophets whose description has been given in great detail in the Holy Quran. In fact after Ibraheem(as), Nuh(as) is the prophet who has been described in great detail. He was born in a city in Iraq. It is narrated in a Sahih Bukhari hadith that he was born thousand years after Adam(as). All these years the people were following the religion of God, that is monotheism. By the time Nuh(as) was born they had strayed to idolatry. The idols which have been mentioned in the Holy Quran are Wadd, Suwa’, Yaghuth, Ya’uq and Nasr. We come to know from the Sahih Hadith that Nuh(as) was the first prophet to be sent to earth. And as soon as he was sent, he started calling people towards Allah(swt). The Holy Quran says:\n﴿لَقَدْ أَرْسَلْنَا نُوحًا إِلَىٰ قَوْمِهِ فَقَالَ يَا قَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللَّـهَ مَا لَكُم مِّنْ إِلَـٰهٍ غَيْرُهُ إِنِّي أَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ عَظِيمٍ ٥٩﴾\nWe had certainly sent Noah to his people, and he said, \"O my people, worship Allah; you have no deity other than Him. Indeed, I fear for you the punishment of a tremendous Day.\n(Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-59)\n﴿وَلَقَدْ أَرْسَلْنَا نُوحًا إِلَىٰ قَوْمِهِ إِنِّي لَكُمْ نَذِيرٌ مُّبِينٌ ٢٥ أَن لَّا تَعْبُدُوا إِلَّا اللَّـهَ ۖ إِنِّي أَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ أَلِيمٍ ٢٦﴾\nAnd We had certainly sent Noah to his people, [saying], \"Indeed, I am to you a clear warner. That you not worship except Allah. Indeed, I fear for you the punishment of a painful day.\"\n(Quran, Surah-11, Hud, Verses-25,26)\n﴿وَلَقَدْ أَرْسَلْنَا نُوحًا إِلَىٰ قَوْمِهِ فَقَالَ يَا قَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللَّـهَ مَا لَكُم مِّنْ إِلَـٰهٍ غَيْرُهُ ۖ أَفَلَا تَتَّقُونَ ٢٣﴾\nAnd We had certainly sent Noah to his people, and he said, \"O my people, worship Allah; you have no deity other than Him; then will you not fear Him?\"\n(Quran, Surah-23, Al-Mu’minun, Verse-23)\nIn this way Nuh(as) called the people towards Allah(swt) for nine hundred and fifty years(See : Surah-29, Ankaboot, Verse-14); but his people did not heed to his call.\n﴿كَذَّبَتْ قَوْمُ نُوحٍ الْمُرْسَلِينَ ١٠٥﴾\nThe people of Noah denied the messengers.\n(Quran, Surah-26, Ash-Shu’ara, Verse-105)\nقَالُوا أَنُؤْمِنُ لَكَ وَاتَّبَعَكَ الْأَرْذَلُونَ\nThey said, \"Should we believe you while you are followed by the lowest [class of people]?\"\n(Quran, Surah-26, Ash-Shu’ara, Verse-111)\n﴿كَذَّبَتْ قَبْلَهُمْ قَوْمُ نُوحٍ فَكَذَّبُوا عَبْدَنَا وَقَالُوا مَجْنُونٌ وَازْدُجِرَ ٩﴾\nThe people of Noah denied before them, and they denied Our servant and said, \"A madman,\" and he was repelled.\n(Quran, Surah-54, Al-Qamar, Verse-9)\n﴿وَلَقَدْ أَرْسَلْنَا نُوحًا إِلَىٰ قَوْمِهِ فَلَبِثَ فِيهِمْ أَلْفَ سَنَةٍ إِلَّا خَمْسِينَ عَامًا فَأَخَذَهُمُ الطُّوفَانُ وَهُمْ ظَالِمُونَ ١٤﴾\nAnd We certainly sent Noah to his people, and he remained among them a thousand years minus fifty years, and the flood seized them while they were wrongdoers.\n(Quran, Surah-29, Al-Ankaboot, Verse-14)\nNuh(as) strove day and night for leading his people to the right path, but they did not heed his message.\n﴿قَالَ رَبِّ إِنِّي دَعَوْتُ قَوْمِي لَيْلًا وَنَهَارًا ٥ فَلَمْ يَزِدْهُمْ دُعَائِي إِلَّا فِرَارًا ٦﴾\nHe said, \"My Lord, indeed I invited my people [to truth] night and day. But my invitation increased them not except in flight.\n(Quran, Surah-71, Nuh, Verses-5,6)\n﴿قَالَ نُوحٌ رَّبِّ إِنَّهُمْ عَصَوْنِي وَاتَّبَعُوا مَن لَّمْ يَزِدْهُ مَالُهُ وَوَلَدُهُ إِلَّا خَسَارًا ٢١﴾\nNoah said, \"My Lord, indeed they have disobeyed me and followed him whose wealth and children will not increase him except in loss.\n(Quran, Surah-71, Nuh, Verse-21)\nIn the end when Nuh(as) was frustrated, he cursed his tribe:\n﴿وَقَالَ نُوحٌ رَّبِّ لَا تَذَرْ عَلَى الْأَرْضِ مِنَ الْكَافِرِينَ دَيَّارًا ٢٦ إِنَّكَ إِن تَذَرْهُمْ يُضِلُّوا عِبَادَكَ وَلَا يَلِدُوا إِلَّا فَاجِرًا كَفَّارًا ٢٧﴾\nAnd Noah said, \"My Lord, do not leave upon the earth from among the disbelievers an inhabitant. Indeed, if You leave them, they will mislead Your servants and not beget except [every] wicked one and [confirmed] disbeliever.\n(Quran, Surah-71, Nuh, Verses-26,27)\nAllah(swt) drowned them for their sins.\n﴿مِّمَّا خَطِيئَاتِهِمْ أُغْرِقُوا فَأُدْخِلُوا نَارًا فَلَمْ يَجِدُوا لَهُم مِّن دُونِ اللَّـهِ أَنصَارًا ٢٥﴾\nBecause of their sins they were drowned and put into the Fire, and they found not for themselves besides Allah [any] helpers.\n(Quran, Surah-71, Nuh, Verse-25)\nWhen the people of his tribe had crossed all limits and Nuh(as) was convinced that they would never come to the right path and turn believers, Allah(swt) commanded Nuh(as) to build a huge Ark:\n﴿فَأَوْحَيْنَا إِلَيْهِ أَنِ اصْنَعِ الْفُلْكَ بِأَعْيُنِنَا وَوَحْيِنَا فَإِذَا جَاءَ أَمْرُنَا وَفَارَ التَّنُّورُ ۙ فَاسْلُكْ فِيهَا مِن كُلٍّ زَوْجَيْنِ اثْنَيْنِ وَأَهْلَكَ إِلَّا مَن سَبَقَ عَلَيْهِ الْقَوْلُ مِنْهُمْ ۖ وَلَا تُخَاطِبْنِي فِي الَّذِينَ ظَلَمُوا ۖ إِنَّهُم مُّغْرَقُونَ ٢٧﴾\nSo We inspired to him,\"Construct the ship under Our observation, and Our inspiration, and when Our command comes and the oven overflows, put into the ship from each [creature] two mates and your family, except those for whom the decree [of destruction] has proceeded. And do not address Me concerning those who have wronged; indeed, they are to be drowned.\n(Quran, Surah-23, Al-Mu’minun, Verse-27)\nAfter the Ark was built there was a great flood and all the creatures who had not boarded the Ark drowned in the water and after that Allah(swt) populated the earth again with the creatures present in the Ark. That is why Nuh(as) is called the second Adam. It is said that Nuh(as)’s wife and son Yam did not join him and perished in the flood. The sons who survived were Ham, Shem and Japheth. Europeans are the descendants of Ham, Asians the descendants of Shem and Africans are the descendants of Japheth. But this cannot be proved conclusively as we do not have any historical evidence. After everything had perished in the flood, Allah(swt) commanded:\n﴿وَقِيلَ يَا أَرْضُ ابْلَعِي مَاءَكِ وَيَا سَمَاءُ أَقْلِعِي وَغِيضَ الْمَاءُ وَقُضِيَ الْأَمْرُ وَاسْتَوَتْ عَلَى الْجُودِيِّ ۖ وَقِيلَ بُعْدًا لِّلْقَوْمِ الظَّالِمِينَ ٤٤﴾\nAnd it was said, \"O earth, swallow your water, and O sky, withhold [your rain].\" And the water subsided, and the matter was accomplished, and the ship came to rest on the [mountain of] Judiyy. And it was said, \"Away with the wrongdoing people.\"\n(Quran, Surah-11, Hud, Verse-44)\nThen the tribe of Nuh(as) came out of Iraq and started spreading throughout the earth. And wherever these people went, they carried the tale of the great flood with them. That is why the story of this great flood is told in every part of the world. It is mentioned in the Bible that this flood lasted for forty days and all the living creatures who were not on the Ark perished in it. The only ones who were saved were Nuh(as), his three sons and their wives and pairs of creatures which were put in the Ark. After forty days, when the flood waters had subsided, Nuh(as) came out onto the land and he and his sons populated the earth. Then Allah(swt) blessed Nuh(as) and his sons and commanded them to go forth and multiply on the earth. In this way Nuh(as) came to be called the second father of humans after Adam(as).( See: Genesis : 6-8)\nIn Verse-15 of Surah-Qamar of the Holy Quran, it says about the Ark:\nAnd We left it as a sign, so is there any who will remember?\nBy ‘sign’ is not meant the Ark, but the entire tale of Nuh(as); how he built the Ark following the command of Allah(swt), how the believers were saved and the disbelievers drowned and how the earth again came to be populated with the pious people – all these should be a lesson for every human being. And if some day the Ark is also found as is being said in the media that the remains of a huge boat have been found on a mountain in Armenia, then even that should serve as a sign and reminder for the discerning and pious people."],[248,"§Nuh(as)’s son\nIt is said in the Bible that Nuh(as) had three sons – Shem, Ham and Japheth( Genesis, 6:10). And then it has been said that it was the descendants of these three sons who again populated the earth after all the other humans had perished in the flood. An error seems to have been committed by the writers of Bible in this regard and some facts have been missed. But, as the Holy Quran is the last and final divine book of revelation, it corrects this error and completes the tale of Nuh(as). It is that the disbeliever son of Nuh(as) was left behind and was drowned. He refused to board the Ark and said that he would climb atop a high mountain and thus escape the flood. But, he could not escape the wrath of Allah(swt) and was drowned in the great flood:\n﴿وَهِيَ تَجْرِي بِهِمْ فِي مَوْجٍ كَالْجِبَالِ وَنَادَىٰ نُوحٌ ابْنَهُ وَكَانَ فِي مَعْزِلٍ يَا بُنَيَّ ارْكَب مَّعَنَا وَلَا تَكُن مَّعَ الْكَافِرِينَ ٤٢ قَالَ سَآوِي إِلَىٰ جَبَلٍ يَعْصِمُنِي مِنَ الْمَاءِ ۚ قَالَ لَا عَاصِمَ الْيَوْمَ مِنْ أَمْرِ اللَّـهِ إِلَّا مَن رَّحِمَ ۚ وَحَالَ بَيْنَهُمَا الْمَوْجُ فَكَانَ مِنَ الْمُغْرَقِينَ ٤٣﴾\nAnd it sailed with them through waves like mountains, and Noah called to his son who was apart [from them], \"O my son, come aboard with us and be not with the disbelievers.\" [But] he said, \"I will take refuge on a mountain to protect me from the water.\" [Noah] said, \"There is no protector today from the decree of Allah, except for whom He gives mercy.\" And the waves came between them, and he was among the drowned.\n(Quran, Surah-11, Hud, Verses-42,43)\nThis was the fourth son of Nuh(as) who is not mentioned in the Bible as he was drowned in the flood and did not have any children. Bible only mentions the three sons who survived the flood and whose descendants populated the earth again. The Holy Quran describes how as a father Nuh(as) pleads with Allah(swt) to save his son:\n﴿وَنَادَىٰ نُوحٌ رَّبَّهُ فَقَالَ رَبِّ إِنَّ ابْنِي مِنْ أَهْلِي وَإِنَّ وَعْدَكَ الْحَقُّ وَأَنتَ أَحْكَمُ الْحَاكِمِينَ ٤٥ قَالَ يَا نُوحُ إِنَّهُ لَيْسَ مِنْ أَهْلِكَ ۖ إِنَّهُ عَمَلٌ غَيْرُ صَالِحٍ ۖ فَلَا تَسْأَلْنِ مَا لَيْسَ لَكَ بِهِ عِلْمٌ ۖ إِنِّي أَعِظُكَ أَن تَكُونَ مِنَ الْجَاهِلِينَ ٤٦﴾\nAnd Noah called to his Lord and said, \"My Lord, indeed my son is of my family; and indeed, Your promise is true; and You are the most just of judges!\" He said, \"O Noah, indeed he is not of your family; indeed, he is [one whose] work was other than righteous, so ask Me not for that about which you have no knowledge. Indeed, I advise you, lest you be among the ignorant.\"\n(Quran, Surah-11, Hud, Verses-45,46)\nHere the Holy Quran describes the disbeliever son as one whose work was other than righteous. We learn an important lesson from this that the reward and punishment we get is based on our deeds and not on the family or tribe we belong to. Here we also need to deny what some scholars of Quran say about the name of this son being ‘Canaan’. This is neither confirmed by the Bible nor by any sahih hadith. In fact, we come to know from the Bible that ‘Canaan’ was the fourth son of ‘Ham’; that is the grandson of Nuh(as)( Genesis, 10:6) He survived the flood and his descendants settled on the west coast of Jordan and that is why it is called the country of Canaan and then later on they were engaged in battles with the Bani-Israel."],[249,"§Onion\nIn the desert of Sina, Allah(swt) sent down Manna and Salwa for the sustenance of the Bani-Israel. But after a few days they wanted to eat other things. So, they said to Musa(as):\nوَإِذْ قُلْتُمْ يَا مُوسَىٰ لَن نَّصْبِرَ عَلَىٰ طَعَامٍ وَاحِدٍ فَادْعُ لَنَا رَبَّكَ يُخْرِجْ لَنَا مِمَّا تُنبِتُ الْأَرْضُ مِن بَقْلِهَا وَقِثَّائِهَا وَفُومِهَا وَعَدَسِهَا وَبَصَلِهَا ۖ قَالَ أَتَسْتَبْدِلُونَ الَّذِي هُوَ أَدْنَىٰ بِالَّذِي هُوَ خَيْرٌ\nAnd [recall] when you said, \"O Moses, we can never endure one [kind of] food. So call upon your Lord to bring forth for us from the earth its green herbs and its cucumbers and its garlic and its lentils and its onions.\" [Moses] said, \"Would you exchange what is better for what is less?\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-61)\nThe rabble with them began to crave other food, and again the Israelites started wailing and said, “If only we had meat to eat! We remember the fish we ate in Egypt at no cost—also the cucumbers, melons, leeks, onions and garlic. But now we have lost our appetite; we never see anything but this manna!”\n(Bible, Numbers, 11:4-6)\nMoses heard the people of every family wailing at the entrance to their tents.\n(Bible, Numbers, 11:10)\nEating onion, garlic and gandna(leek)(a vegetable with leaves like the onion which is eaten raw in Arabia) is not forbidden, but as these leave a foul smell in the mouth, it is forbidden to eat them and enter the mosque.\nIt is narrated in a sahih hadith:\n“Whoever has eaten garlic or onion need not come even near our mosque but sit at home.”\nOnce a few vegetables were placed in front of the Holy Prophet(saws), but he(saws) detected a foul smell and said,\n“You eat (I won’t) for I converse with those whom you do not converse with.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 855, Sahih Muslim, 561,564)\nHearing this some of the companions said that now these things have become unlawful. When the Holy Prophet(saws) came to know of this, he(saws) said:\n“O people how can I make unlawful something which Allah(swt) has made lawful! But I hate foul smell.”( Sahih Muslim, 565)\nBut there is no objection if these are cooked and eaten as the second Caliph Umar-bin-Khattab said in his Friday sermon:\n“During the time of Nabi(saws), if someone came to him after eating onion or garlic, he would send him away from the Masjid to Al-Baqi. But if someone wishes to eat them, he should cook them till there is no more foul odour.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 567)"],[250,"§Orphan\nAn orphan is one whose father has passed away. Orphans have to face a lot of social and financial problems in this world. Islam addresses these problems in a wonderful way.\nThere are basically two situations in which the orphans find themselves:\nFirst category:\nThe father of the orphan has left behind some wealth. In this situation somebody is appointed to look after the wealth. It becomes obligatory for this guardian to try to increase this wealth and not to take any amount exceeding that which has been designated as fee for his services.\nوَلَا تَقْرَبُوا مَالَ الْيَتِيمِ إِلَّا بِالَّتِي هِيَ أَحْسَنُ حَتَّىٰ يَبْلُغَ أَشُدَّهُ\nAnd do not approach the orphan's property except in a way that is best until he reaches maturity.\n(Quran, Surah-6, Al-An’am, Verse-152 and Surah-17, Bani-Israel, Verse-34)\nThat is, the guardian should take care of the orphan’s wealth till he reaches maturity. He should invest the money wisely so that there is an increase in the wealth. The orphan’s wealth may be combined with the guardian’s own wealth for trade purposes.\nIt becomes imperative for the guardian that he should have the best interests of the orphan uppermost in his mind. If he feels that it is more profitable to mix his capital with that of the orphan’s, then it is not forbidden for him:\nوَيَسْأَلُونَكَ عَنِ الْيَتَامَىٰ ۖ قُلْ إِصْلَاحٌ لَّهُمْ خَيْرٌ ۖ وَإِن تُخَالِطُوهُمْ فَإِخْوَانُكُمْ ۚ وَاللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ الْمُفْسِدَ مِنَ الْمُصْلِحِ ۚ وَلَوْ شَاءَ اللَّهُ لَأَعْنَتَكُمْ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ\nAnd they ask you about orphans. Say, \"Improvement for them is best. And if you mix your affairs with theirs - they are your brothers. And Allah knows the corrupter from the amender. And if Allah had willed, He could have put you in difficulty. Indeed, Allah is Exalted in Might and Wise.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-220)\nHere ‘mix the affairs’ means to combine the wealth of the orphan along with the guardian’s own wealth with the aim of increasing the orphan’s profit and not incurring loss for him. This is what is meant by ‘Allah knows the corrupter from the amender’. If the guardian is rich then he should not take anything from the orphan’s wealth; but if he is poor he should take only as much as has been permitted. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَلَا تُؤْتُوا السُّفَهَاءَ أَمْوَالَكُمُ الَّتِي جَعَلَ اللَّـهُ لَكُمْ قِيَامًا وَارْزُقُوهُمْ فِيهَا وَاكْسُوهُمْ وَقُولُوا لَهُمْ قَوْلًا مَّعْرُوفًا ٥ وَابْتَلُوا الْيَتَامَىٰ حَتَّىٰ إِذَا بَلَغُوا النِّكَاحَ فَإِنْ آنَسْتُم مِّنْهُمْ رُشْدًا فَادْفَعُوا إِلَيْهِمْ أَمْوَالَهُمْ ۖ وَلَا تَأْكُلُوهَا إِسْرَافًا وَبِدَارًا أَن يَكْبَرُوا ۚ وَمَن كَانَ غَنِيًّا فَلْيَسْتَعْفِفْ ۖ وَمَن كَانَ فَقِيرًا فَلْيَأْكُلْ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ ۚ فَإِذَا دَفَعْتُمْ إِلَيْهِمْ أَمْوَالَهُمْ فَأَشْهِدُوا عَلَيْهِمْ ۚ وَكَفَىٰ بِاللَّـهِ حَسِيبًا ٦﴾\nAnd do not give the weak-minded your property, which Allah has made a means of sustenance for you, but provide for them with it and clothe them and speak to them words of appropriate kindness. And test the orphans [in their abilities] until they reach marriageable age. Then if you perceive in them sound judgement, release their property to them. And do not consume it excessively and quickly, [anticipating] that they will grow up. And whoever, [when acting as guardian], is self-sufficient should refrain [from taking a fee]; and whoever is poor - let him take according to what is acceptable. Then when you release their property to them, bring witnesses upon them. And sufficient is Allah as Accountant.\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verses-5,6)\nThat is, Allah(swt) will take to task the people who cunningly consume the orphan’s wealth. So, they have been warned against even approaching the orphan’s wealth. The punishment for those who take away this forbidden wealth is described in the Holy Quran as under:\n﴿إِنَّ الَّذِينَ يَأْكُلُونَ أَمْوَالَ الْيَتَامَىٰ ظُلْمًا إِنَّمَا يَأْكُلُونَ فِي بُطُونِهِمْ نَارًا ۖ وَسَيَصْلَوْنَ سَعِيرًا ١٠﴾\nIndeed, those who devour the property of orphans unjustly are only consuming into their bellies fire. And they will be burned in a Blaze.\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-10)\nAnd when they reach maturity, their wealth should be handed over to them without any deception or foul play. As the Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَآتُوا الْيَتَامَىٰ أَمْوَالَهُمْ ۖ وَلَا تَتَبَدَّلُوا الْخَبِيثَ بِالطَّيِّبِ ۖ وَلَا تَأْكُلُوا أَمْوَالَهُمْ إِلَىٰ أَمْوَالِكُمْ ۚ إِنَّهُ كَانَ حُوبًا كَبِيرًا ٢﴾\nAnd give to the orphans their properties and do not substitute the defective [of your own] for the good [of theirs]. And do not consume their properties into your own. Indeed, that is ever a great sin.\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-2)\nMarriage of the orphan girls:\nIt is permitted to marry orphan girls. In fact it is the best option in certain cases. But it should be borne in mind that justice is done to the girl. Some people marry girls taking advantage of their helplessness and just for the sake of their wealth. The Holy Quran says about these people:\n﴿وَإِنْ خِفْتُمْ أَلَّا تُقْسِطُوا فِي الْيَتَامَىٰ فَانكِحُوا مَا طَابَ لَكُم مِّنَ النِّسَاءِ مَثْنَىٰ وَثُلَاثَ وَرُبَاعَ ۖ فَإِنْ خِفْتُمْ أَلَّا تَعْدِلُوا فَوَاحِدَةً أَوْ مَا مَلَكَتْ أَيْمَانُكُمْ ۚ ذَٰلِكَ أَدْنَىٰ أَلَّا تَعُولُوا ٣﴾\nAnd if you fear that you will not deal justly with the orphan girls, then marry those that please you of [other] women, two or three or four. But if you fear that you will not be just, then [marry only] one or those your right hand possesses. That is more suitable that you may not incline [to injustice].\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-3)\nSecond category:\nInto this category fall the orphans whose father has not left behind anything. In this case the responsibility of taking care of these orphans is that of the society. In this regard clear instructions are given in the Holy Quran. When one companion asked the Holy Prophet(saws) as to how to spend the excess wealth, the following verse was revealed:\n﴿يَسْأَلُونَكَ مَاذَا يُنفِقُونَ ۖ قُلْ مَا أَنفَقْتُم مِّنْ خَيْرٍ فَلِلْوَالِدَيْنِ وَالْأَقْرَبِينَ وَالْيَتَامَىٰ وَالْمَسَاكِينِ وَابْنِ السَّبِيلِ ۗ وَمَا تَفْعَلُوا مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَإِنَّ اللَّـهَ بِهِ عَلِيمٌ ٢١٥﴾\nThey ask you, [O Muhammad], what they should spend. Say, \"Whatever you spend of good is [to be] for parents and relatives and orphans and the needy and the traveler. And whatever you do of good - indeed, Allah is Knowing of it.\"\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-215)\nOne of the qualities of the pious is:\n﴿وَيُطْعِمُونَ الطَّعَامَ عَلَىٰ حُبِّهِ مِسْكِينًا وَيَتِيمًا وَأَسِيرًا ٨﴾\nAnd they give food in spite of love for it to the needy, the orphan, and the captive\n(Quran, Surah-76, Ad-Dhahr, Verse-8)\nThe disbelievers of Mecca who do not believe in the Day of Judgement and drive away the orphans are criticized in the Holy Quran:\n﴿فَذَٰلِكَ الَّذِي يَدُعُّ الْيَتِيمَ ٢ وَلَا يَحُضُّ عَلَىٰ طَعَامِ الْمِسْكِينِ ٣﴾\nFor that is the one who drives away the orphan. And does not encourage the feeding of the poor.(Quran, Surah-107, Al-Ma’un, Verses-2-3)\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) was himself an orphan; but Allah(swt) had mercy on him. That is why he is being commanded to behave in a kindly manner with the orphans:\n﴿فَأَمَّا الْيَتِيمَ فَلَا تَقْهَرْ ٩ وَأَمَّا السَّائِلَ فَلَا تَنْهَرْ ١٠﴾\nSo as for the orphan, do not oppress [him]. And as for the petitioner, do not repel [him].\n(Quran, Surah-93, Ad-Dhuha, Verses-9-10)\nThat is why the Holy Prophet(saws) was very generous to the beggars and the needy and some or the other orphan would always be living with him. His companion Anas(ra) says that the Holy Prophet(saws) never refused anybody who asked him for something. He(saws) has given glad tidings to those who took care of orphans:\n“Me and the one who takes care of orphans will be like this in paradise.” Saying this the Holy Prophet(saws) showed his two fingers.\n(Sahih Bukhari, 6005)\nAccording to another hadith:\n“The one who takes care of the orphan, whether he is his close one or not and myself will be like this.” Saying this the Holy Prophet(saws) showed his two fingers.\n(Sahih Muslim, 2983)\nThat is, irrespective of whether the orphan is from one's family or an outsider, taking care of orphans is an act which is very noble and has huge rewards in the Hereafter. According to one hadith, when one person complained about his being very hard-hearted, the Holy Prophet(saws) advised him:\n“Pat the head of the orphan and feed the poor.”\n(Musnad Ahmad, 7576)\nThat is, take care of some orphan. One other meaning of this is to marry the mother of the orphan so that the orphan gets a permanent home. This will cause your heart to soften up and the hardness will disappear.\nIn this way Islam beautifully addresses the issue of orphans along with that of widows.\nIf one is unable to do all this he should help the children living in orphanages. But this should be done only after making sure that the people who run these institutions are in fact serving the orphans and not running a business for their own profit. This would amount to the same thing as directly taking care of the orphans."],[251,"§Pomegranate\nPomegranate is called ‘Rumman’ in Arabic. There will be many delights in heaven, of which pomegranate is one. This is also mentioned in the Holy Quran:\nفِيهِمَا فَاكِهَةٌ وَنَخْلٌ وَرُمَّانٌ\nIn both of them are fruit and palm trees and pomegranates.\n(Quran, Surah-55, Ar-Rahman, Verse-68)\nPomegranate is among the things which Allah(swt) in His Infinite mercy has provided for us humans to lead a comfortable life in this world."],[252,"§Pride\nPride is ‘Takabbur’ in Arabic. Pride is a disease which afflicts people in such a way that they cannot distinguish between right and wrong. That is why Allah(swt) does not like a person who is proud. The Holy Quran says:\nإِنَّهُ لَا يُحِبُّ الْمُسْتَكْبِرِينَ\nIndeed, He does not like the arrogant.\n(Quran, Surah-16, An-Nahl, Verse-23)\nAs against them, the people who do not have any pride are praised. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿لَتَجِدَنَّ أَشَدَّ النَّاسِ عَدَاوَةً لِّلَّذِينَ آمَنُوا الْيَهُودَ وَالَّذِينَ أَشْرَكُوا ۖ وَلَتَجِدَنَّ أَقْرَبَهُم مَّوَدَّةً لِّلَّذِينَ آمَنُوا الَّذِينَ قَالُوا إِنَّا نَصَارَىٰ ۚ ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّ مِنْهُمْ قِسِّيسِينَ وَرُهْبَانًا وَأَنَّهُمْ لَا يَسْتَكْبِرُونَ ٨٢﴾\nYou will surely find the most intense of the people in animosity toward the believers [to be] the Jews and those who associate others with Allah; and you will find the nearest of them in affection to the believers those who say, \"We are Christians.\" That is because among them are priests and monks and because they are not arrogant.\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verse-82)\nThat is, when the truth is explained to them, they accept it.\nBut this does not mean that there were no Jews who did not accept the truth. In fact there were many among the Jews who embraced the truth. A Jewish scholar Abdullah-bin-Salam is praised in the Holy Quran:\nقُلْ أَرَأَيْتُمْ إِن كَانَ مِنْ عِندِ اللَّهِ وَكَفَرْتُم بِهِ وَشَهِدَ شَاهِدٌ مِّن بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ عَلَىٰ مِثْلِهِ فَآمَنَ وَاسْتَكْبَرْتُمْ\nSay, \"Have you considered: if the Qur'an was from Allah, and you disbelieved in it while a witness from the Children of Israel has testified to something similar and believed while you were arrogant...?\"\n(Quran, Surah-46, Al-Ahqaf, Verse-10)\nAccording to a sahih hadith, Saad-bin-AbiWaqqas says:\n“There is no one who walks the earth about whom the Holy Prophet(saws) has said that he is a dweller of paradise except for Abdullah-bin-Salam.”\nRegarding him this verse of surah-46, Al-Ahqaf was revealed. ( See Sahih Bukhari, 3812 and Sahih Muslim, 2483)\nAllah(swt) has admonished the arrogant people severely.\nThe first arrogant being was ‘Iblees’ when he refused to prostrate in front of Adam(as) along with the other angels. He was the only one who was disobedient and the reason was his arrogance.\n(See:Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-34)\nAnd this arrogance was the reason for his being insulted and being expelled from paradise.(See: Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-13)\nThat is, wherever the arrogant people exist, they will have to face insult. The best people are those who are humble for the sake of Allah(swt) as is explained in the sahih hadith:\n“The people who adopt humility for the sake of Allah(swt) shall be given a high status by Allah(swt).”\n(Sahih Muslim, 2588)\nAccording to another Sahih Hadith:\n“It has been revealed to me that O people! Cultivate humility, do not be arrogant with each other and do not commit excesses against anybody” ( Sahih Muslim, 2865)\nMany arrogant people have been described in the Holy Quran; Pharaoh(Firaun) being one of them:\n﴿وَاسْتَكْبَرَ هُوَ وَجُنُودُهُ فِي الْأَرْضِ بِغَيْرِ الْحَقِّ وَظَنُّوا أَنَّهُمْ إِلَيْنَا لَا يُرْجَعُونَ ٣٩ فَأَخَذْنَاهُ وَجُنُودَهُ فَنَبَذْنَاهُمْ فِي الْيَمِّ ۖ فَانظُرْ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الظَّالِمِينَ ٤٠﴾\nAnd he was arrogant, he and his soldiers, in the land, without right, and they thought that they would not be returned to Us. So We took him and his soldiers and threw them into the sea. So see how was the end of the wrongdoers.\n(Quran, Surah-28, Al-Qasas, Verses-39,40)\nIn the Holy Quran, three arrogant people have been described in one verse itself and then their ultimate end has been explained:\n﴿وَقَارُونَ وَفِرْعَوْنَ وَهَامَانَ ۖ وَلَقَدْ جَاءَهُم مُّوسَىٰ بِالْبَيِّنَاتِ فَاسْتَكْبَرُوا فِي الْأَرْضِ وَمَا كَانُوا سَابِقِينَ ٣٩ فَكُلًّا أَخَذْنَا بِذَنبِهِ ۖ فَمِنْهُم مَّنْ أَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِ حَاصِبًا وَمِنْهُم مَّنْ أَخَذَتْهُ الصَّيْحَةُ وَمِنْهُم مَّنْ خَسَفْنَا بِهِ الْأَرْضَ وَمِنْهُم مَّنْ أَغْرَقْنَا ۚ وَمَا كَانَ اللَّـهُ لِيَظْلِمَهُمْ وَلَـٰكِن كَانُوا أَنفُسَهُمْ يَظْلِمُونَ ٤٠﴾\nAnd [We destroyed] Qarun and Pharaoh and Haman. And Moses had already come to them with clear evidences, and they were arrogant in the land, but they were not outrunners [of Our punishment]. So each We seized for his sin; and among them were those upon whom We sent a storm of stones, and among them were those who were seized by the blast [from the sky], and among them were those whom We caused the earth to swallow, and among them were those whom We drowned. And Allah would not have wronged them, but it was they who were wronging themselves.\n(Quran, Surah-29, Al-Ankaboot, Verses-39,40)\nIn the same way when the Holy Prophet(saws) was inviting people towards the path of Allah(swt), there was a very proud Arab chieftain named Walid-bin-Mughira. The following verse was revealed about him:\n﴿ذَرْنِي وَمَنْ خَلَقْتُ وَحِيدًا ١١﴾\nLeave Me with the one I created alone.\n(Quran, Surah-74, Al-Muddathir, Verse-11)\nAnd then after enumerating His various favours, Allah(swt) says:\n﴿ثُمَّ أَدْبَرَ وَاسْتَكْبَرَ ٢٣ فَقَالَ إِنْ هَـٰذَا إِلَّا سِحْرٌ يُؤْثَرُ ٢٤ إِنْ هَـٰذَا إِلَّا قَوْلُ الْبَشَرِ ٢٥ سَأُصْلِيهِ سَقَرَ ٢٦ وَمَا أَدْرَاكَ مَا سَقَرُ ٢٧ لَا تُبْقِي وَلَا تَذَرُ ٢٨ لَوَّاحَةٌ لِّلْبَشَرِ ٢٩﴾\nThen he turned back and was arrogant. And said, \"This is not but magic imitated [from others]. This is not but the word of a human being.\" I will drive him into Saqar. And what can make you know what is Saqar? It lets nothing remain and leaves nothing [unburned], Blackening the skins.\n(Quran, Surah-74, Al-Muddathir, Verses-23-29)\nThis Walid-bin-Mughira was one of the Arab chieftains who made fun of the Holy Prophet(saws) and the following verse was revealed about him:\n﴿إِنَّا كَفَيْنَاكَ الْمُسْتَهْزِئِينَ ٩٥﴾\nIndeed, We are sufficient for you against the mockers.\n(Quran, Surah-15, Al-Hijr, Verse-95)\nHe was once injured by an arrow in his leg. Two years later the wound festered and the poison caused his death and he is not remembered by anyone after his death. In fact some of his sons even embraced Islam. One among them was Khalid-bin-Walid who was appointed the head of the Muslim army and he led many expeditions against the enemies of Islam and defeated them. His name has been written in golden letters in the annals of the history of Islam while his arrogant father is despised."],[253,"§Prison\nPrison is called ‘Sijn’ in Arabic. It means a jail. This word has been used in two places in the Holy Quran:\nWhen Musa(as) invited the Pharaoh(Firaun) towards ‘Tawheed’ or monotheism, he threatened him and said:\n﴿قَالَ لَئِنِ اتَّخَذْتَ إِلَـٰهًا غَيْرِي لَأَجْعَلَنَّكَ مِنَ الْمَسْجُونِينَ ٢٩﴾\nHe said,\"If thou dost put forward any god other than me, I will certainly put thee in prison!\"\n(Quran, Surah-26, Ash-Shu’araa, Verse-29)\nIn the story of Yusuf(as), the prison is described again and again; for example when the Egyptian lady says:\nقَالَتْ مَا جَزَاءُ مَنْ أَرَادَ بِأَهْلِكَ سُوءًا إِلَّا أَن يُسْجَنَ أَوْ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ\nShe said: \"What is the (fitting) punishment for one who formed an evil design against thy wife, but prison or a grievous chastisement?\"\n(Quran, Surah-12, Yusuf, Verse-25)\n﴿قَالَتْ فَذَٰلِكُنَّ الَّذِي لُمْتُنَّنِي فِيهِ ۖ وَلَقَدْ رَاوَدتُّهُ عَن نَّفْسِهِ فَاسْتَعْصَمَ ۖ وَلَئِن لَّمْ يَفْعَلْ مَا آمُرُهُ لَيُسْجَنَنَّ وَلَيَكُونًا مِّنَ الصَّاغِرِينَ ٣٢﴾\nShe said: \"There before you is the man about whom ye did blame me! I did seek to seduce him from his (true) self but he did firmly save himself guiltless!....and now, if he doth not my bidding, he shall certainly be cast into prison, and (what is more) be of the company of the vilest!\"\n(Quran, Surah-12, Yusuf, Verse-32)\nYusuf(as) said:\nقَالَ رَبِّ السِّجْنُ أَحَبُّ إِلَيَّ مِمَّا يَدْعُونَنِي إِلَيْهِ\nHe said: \"O my Lord! the prison is more to my liking than that to which they invite me.\n(Quran, Surah-12,Yusuf, Verse-33)\n﴿ثُمَّ بَدَا لَهُم مِّن بَعْدِ مَا رَأَوُا الْآيَاتِ لَيَسْجُنُنَّهُ حَتَّىٰ حِينٍ ٣٥﴾\nThen it occurred to the men, after they had seen the signs, (that it was best) to imprison him for a time.\n(Quran, Surah-12, Yusuf, Verse-35)\nYusuf(as) continued preaching monotheism even in prison:\n﴿يَا صَاحِبَيِ السِّجْنِ أَأَرْبَابٌ مُّتَفَرِّقُونَ خَيْرٌ أَمِ اللَّـهُ الْوَاحِدُ الْقَهَّارُ ٣٩﴾\n\"O my two companions of the prison! (I ask you): are many lords differing among themselves better, or the One Allah, Supreme and Irresistible?\n(Quran, Surah-12, Yusuf,Verse-39)\nThe first instance of prison in recorded history is found in Egypt.\nDuring the time of the Holy Prophet(saws), there were no prisons in the Arab countries but murderers and people not returning their loans were put under arrest.( Abu Dawood 3630, Tirmizi 1417, Nasai 4876)\nThen the second caliph Umar-bin-Khattab bought the house of Safwan-bin-Umayya in Makka and converted it into a prison.\nIn the same way he made a prison in Madina in which the poet Hutayya was kept because he would write poems criticizing people. It is said that nobody was immune from his poems. The third caliph Usman-bin-Affan imprisoned Zaabi-bin-Hatis who was a notorious dacoit.\nIn this way began the policy of imprisoning the criminals in the Islamic regime.\nThis was in fact necessary because there was no other way of protecting the society from the criminals. All the Islamic religious scholars are unanimous in their support of the policy of imprisoning the criminals."],[254,"§Purity\nPurity is called ‘Taharat’ in Arabic and because Allah(swt) loves purity and pure people, Islam gives great importance to purity. It is narrated in a sahih hadith:\n“Purity is half of faith.”( Sahih Muslim, 233)\nThis purity is both of the body and mind.\nPurity of the body:\nThe Holy Quran and the sahih hadith give instructions to keep ourselves clean and pure the whole day and night and all through our lives:\n1.A person should first wash his hands as soon as he gets up because he is not aware where all his hands have been while he was asleep.(Sahih Bukhari,162 and Sahih Muslim, 278)\n2.After urinating, shake the organ thrice to dislodge any urine and then wash the private parts with water.\n3.It is forbidden to face the Qibla while relieving oneself and the left hand should be used for cleaning after that. Three clods of mud or three pebbles can also be used for cleaning after relieving oneself and these pebbles or mud should not have bones or dung.(Sahih Muslim 262). After that it is better to wash with water.\n4.In case of intercourse, with or without discharge, a bath is compulsory.\n5.In case of nocturnal ejaculation or wet dream, a bath is compulsory both for men and women.(See Sahih Bukhari 13 and Sahih Muslim, 31)\n6.If a woman has her hair in a plait or braid, then it is not necessary to unbraid her hair for having a bath.(Sahih Muslim, 33)\n7.But if she has to have a bath at the end of her menstruation, then she should unbraid her hair and then have a bath.( Sahih Bukhari, 317 and Sahih Muslim, 1211)\n8.It is necessary to shield or cover oneself while having a bath.( Sahih Bukhari, 28 and Sahih Muslim, 336)\n9.It is better not to be naked while having a bath because we need to be ashamed in front of Allah(swt).\n10.Women should not use the toilets which are common.( Musnad Ahmad, 28041)\n11.Care should be taken to keep the drops of urine from splashing onto the clothes.( Sahih Bukhari 218 and Sahih Muslim, 292)\n12.For cleaning the mouth, miswak should be used.( Sahih Bukhari, 887 and Sahih Muslim, 252)\n13.Always try to be in the state of ablution because only a believer can be in this condition.(Musnad Ahmad 5:282)\n14.Circumcision should be done, the hair of the private parts and underarms should be shaved, moustache should be shaved and the nails should be trimmed as these are in the nature of human beings.( Sahih Bukhari, 5889 and Sahih Muslim, 257)\n15.Before entering the toilet this supplication should be recited:\nAllahumma inni Aoozubika minal khubsi wal khabaiz.\n(O Allah(swt)! I seek refuge in You from male and female satans)\n(Abu Dawood, 6 and Ibn-Majah, 296)\n16.It is forbidden to have intercourse with one’s wife while she is menstruating, till she purifies herself.( See: Quran,Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-222)\n17.Anal intercourse with one’s wife is forbidden.\n18.Sodomising boys is forbidden. In Islam such a person is to be severely punished. This was reason why Allah(swt) had punished the tribe of Lut(as).(See:Quran, Surah-27, An-Naml, Verse-57,58)\n19.We should sit while urinating so that the drops do not splash on the clothes. But in case of necessity, it can be done standing also.(Sahih Bukhari, 224 and Sahih Muslim, 273)\n20.We should not relieve ourselves in stagnant water.(Sahih Bukhari, 289, Sahih Muslim, 272)\n21.We should beware of two things which cause others to curse – one is urinating on the pathways used by people and the second is to do so in shady places where people take rest.(Sahih Muslim, 289)\n22.If the clothes are stained with semen, then the area should be washed off. If it has dried up, then it can also be scraped away.(Sahih Muslim, 29)\n23.If someone urinates in a mosque by mistake, then it should be cleaned with water.(Sahih Bukhari, 221, Sahih Muslim, 284)\n24.No man or woman should see the private parts of other men or women. And two men should not sleep in one quilt and two women should not sleep in one quilt.\n25.We should always keep our clothes pure and clean,(See:Quran, Surah-74, Al-Mudassir, Verse-4)\n26.The Holy Quran should not be recited in an impure state.(See:Quran, Surah-56, Al-Waaqia, Verse-79)\nOn special occasions, a bath is compulsory:\n1.A complete bath should be taken at least once a week on Friday and perfume should be used.\n2.Bath should be taken on Eid-ul-Fitr and Eid-ul-Azha.\n3.Bath should be taken before donning the Ihram for Umra and Hajj.\n4.After coming from Arafat, stoning the Jamarat, offering the sacrifice and shaving the hair, a bath should be taken.\nIn this way, a Muslim can keep himself pure his whole life and offer the five prayers from dawn to dusk. It is narrated in a sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) once questioned one companion that if a person bathes five times everyday in a flowing river, will he still remain unclean? The companion replied,”No.” Then the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n\"That is the example of the five prayers with which Allah(swt) blots out (annuls) evil deeds.\"\n(Sahih Bukhari, 528 and Sahih Muslim, 667)\nPurity of heart:\nPurity of heart means that the concept of ‘Tawheed’ should be deeply embedded in our hearts and we should hate every form of ‘shirk’ just as we hate a dirty thing because ‘shirk’ is a great injustice.(See:Quran, Surah-31, Luqman, Verse-13)\nAnyone who has anyone other than Allah(swt) in his heart is definitely impure.\nAllah(swt) had commanded Ibraheem(as) to keep His house(Kaaba) clean from such unclean people:\n﴿وَإِذْ بَوَّأْنَا لِإِبْرَاهِيمَ مَكَانَ الْبَيْتِ أَن لَّا تُشْرِكْ بِي شَيْئًا وَطَهِّرْ بَيْتِيَ لِلطَّائِفِينَ وَالْقَائِمِينَ وَالرُّكَّعِ السُّجُودِ ٢٦﴾\nAnd [mention, O Muhammad], when We designated for Abraham the site of the House, [saying], \"Do not associate anything with Me and purify My House for those who perform Tawaf and those who stand [in prayer] and those who bow and prostrate.\n(Quran, Surah-22, Al-Hajj, Verse-26)\nThat is, clean My house of such impure people who believe in other gods and goddesses other than me and worship them. These people are indeed unclean. Their impurity is the impurity of their hearts. That is why after the victory over Makka, the Holy Prophet(saws) removed all the idols which had been placed in the Holy Kaaba and the following verse was revealed by Allah(swt):\nيَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِنَّمَا الْمُشْرِكُونَ نَجَسٌ فَلَا يَقْرَبُوا الْمَسْجِدَ الْحَرَامَ بَعْدَ عَامِهِمْ هَٰذَا ۚ\nO you who have believed, indeed the polytheists are unclean, so let them not approach al-Masjid al-Haram after this, their [final] year.\n(Quran, Surah-9, At-Tawba, Verse-28)\nPurity of heart is when we do pious deeds, we should do it for Allah(swt) alone.\n(See: Sahih Bukhari, 3465 and Sahih Muslim, 2743)\nIf someone does pious deeds just to make a show of it in front of others, then they will not be acceptable to Allah(swt). But the doer will go to hell.( See: Sahih Muslim, 1905)\nIslam gives more importance to the purity of heart than to the purity of body because the acceptance or non-acceptance of good deeds depends on the purity of the heart.\n﴿يَوْمَ لَا يَنفَعُ مَالٌ وَلَا بَنُونَ ٨٨ إِلَّا مَنْ أَتَى اللَّهَ بِقَلْبٍ سَلِيمٍ ٨٩﴾\nThe Day when there will not benefit [anyone] wealth or children. But only one who comes to Allah with a sound heart.\"\n(Quran, Surah-26, Ash-Shu’ara, Verses-88,89)\nThat is, the heart which is free from shirk, kufr, desires, pride etc. and is content with the remembrance of Allah(swt).\nThere were two doors for the shirk of the heart and both of them were closed with just one verse:\nإِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ\nIt is You we worship and You we ask for help.\n(Quran, Surah-1, Al-Fatiha, Verse-4)"],[255,"§Qasr\nQasr is a special word of the Holy Quran which means ‘to shorten’.\nIn the Quranic terminology, when on a journey a person can Qasr(shorten) his prayers. Instead of the four rakats of the Zuhur, Asr and Isha prayers, two rakats can be offered. But there is no shortening of prayers in case of the three rakats of the Magrib prayer and the two rakats of the Fajr prayer.\nIt is actually mentioned in the Holy Quran with regard to the prayer during war:\n﴿وَإِذَا ضَرَبْتُمْ فِي الْأَرْضِ فَلَيْسَ عَلَيْكُمْ جُنَاحٌ أَن تَقْصُرُوا مِنَ الصَّلَاةِ إِنْ خِفْتُمْ أَن يَفْتِنَكُمُ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا ۚ إِنَّ الْكَافِرِينَ كَانُوا لَكُمْ عَدُوًّا مُّبِينًا ١٠١﴾\nWhen ye travel through the earth, there is no blame on you if ye shorten your prayers, for fear the Unbelievers May attack you: For the Unbelievers are unto you open enemies.\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-101)\nThen, when the war came to an end the companions of the Holy Prophet(saws) thought that the Qasr prayers were no longer allowed. Upon which the Holy Prophet(saws) said,\n“This is a gift from Allah(swt), accept it.”\n(Sahih Muslim, 686)\nThat is, even during the times of peace, offer Qasr prayers.\nAfter what distance are the Qasr prayers to be offered? It is narrated in one sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) said,\n“No woman who believes in Allah(swt) and the Last Day may travel without a mehram for one day plus one night.”\n(Bukhari 1088 and Muslim 1339)\nA travel lasting for one day plus one night was termed a journey by the Holy Prophet(saws) which works out to approximately 80 kms when the journey is on a camel. If the distance is less than this, the rules of journey do not apply.\nThe period of journey:\nThe journey should last for at least four days. But if the duration of the journey has not been decided, then the person is considered a traveler till his return. During the entire journey, he should Qasr his prayers. In addition to shortening the prayers, a person while on a journey can also combine two prayers; that is, he can offer the Zuhur and Asr prayers together and the Magrib and Isha prayers together and the Fajr prayer at the time of the Fajr prayer as was done by the Holy Prophet(saws) during the battle of ‘Tabuk’.(Abu Dawood 1208 and Tirmizi 553)"],[256,"§Qibla\nQibla means the direction of worship. What is meant is the Holy Kaaba. All the Muslims of this world turn their face towards the Kaaba when they offer the salah. We come to know from the life-history of the Holy Prophet(saws) that when he was in Makka, both the Holy Kaaba and the ‘Baitul Muqaddas’ were considered the Qibla. He(saws) would stand between the ‘Yemeni corner’ and the ‘Hajr-e-Aswad’ corner. In this way both the Kaaba and the ‘Baitul Muqaddas’ were in front of him because ‘Baitul Muqaddas’ is to the north of Mecca. But when he migrated to Madina, it was not possible for him to face both the Qiblas while offering salah. So, with the permission of Allah(swt), he started offering salah facing the ‘Baitul Muqaddas’. The Holy Prophet(saws) offered salah in this way for some sixteen to seventeen months. After namaz, he would look towards the sky and pray to Allah(swt), “O Allah(swt), give me permission to face the Kaaba.”( Sahih Bukhari, 4486 and Muslim, 525)\nThen one day, the command came that the Muslims should offer salah facing the Holy Kaaba wherever in the world they are. From the records of the life of the Holy Prophet(saws) and the hadith we come to know that the Holy Prophet(saws) was offering the Zuhur salah when the following verse was revealed:\nفَوَلِّ وَجْهَكَ شَطْرَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ ۚ\nTurn then Thy face in the direction of the sacred Mosque.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-144)\nThe Holy Prophet(saws), while offering the salah turned his face from Baitul Muqaddas which is to the north of Madina towards Masjid-e-Haram (Kaaba) which is to the south of Madina. In the same way, when the news reached the tribe of Banu-Salma, they changed their direction from Baitul Muqaddas to Kaaba in the state of namaz itself. At that place is built a beautiful and vast mosque which is called ‘Masjid-e-Qiblatain’ which means the masjid in which namaz was offered facing the two qiblas. It is said that even in the Masjid-e-Quba, the qibla was changed in the state of namaz itself. This was in fact a test for them as the Holy Quran says:\nوَكَذَٰلِكَ جَعَلْنَاكُمْ أُمَّةً وَسَطًا لِّتَكُونُوا شُهَدَاءَ عَلَى النَّاسِ وَيَكُونَ الرَّسُولُ عَلَيْكُمْ شَهِيدًا ۗ وَمَا جَعَلْنَا الْقِبْلَةَ الَّتِي كُنتَ عَلَيْهَا إِلَّا لِنَعْلَمَ مَن يَتَّبِعُ الرَّسُولَ مِمَّن يَنقَلِبُ عَلَىٰ عَقِبَيْهِ\nThus, have We made of you an Ummat justly balanced, that ye might be witnesses over the nations, and the Messenger a witness over yourselves; and We appointed the Qibla to which thou wast used, only to test those who followed the Messenger from those who would turn on their heels (From the Faith).\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-143)\nToday not only do we offer namaz facing the Kaaba, but the dead body is laid in the grave with the face towards the Kaaba. While sacrificing an animal, its face is turned towards the Holy Kaaba. It is compulsory for every Muslim to respect the Holy Kaaba. We should not attend the call of nature facing the Kaaba. That is why in the homes of Muslims, the toilet does not face the Kaaba. It is not right for a Muslim to offer salah in any other direction other than the Holy Kaaba as the namaz will not be accepted by Allah(swt).\nNow let us look at the verses revealed in connection with the qibla:\n﴿سَيَقُولُ السُّفَهَاءُ مِنَ النَّاسِ مَا وَلَّاهُمْ عَن قِبْلَتِهِمُ الَّتِي كَانُوا عَلَيْهَا ۚ قُل لِّلَّـهِ الْمَشْرِقُ وَالْمَغْرِبُ ۚ يَهْدِي مَن يَشَاءُ إِلَىٰ صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيمٍ ١٤٢﴾\nThe fools among the people will say: \"What hath turned them from the Qibla to which they were used?\" Say: To Allah belong both east and West: He guideth whom He will to a Way that is straight.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-142)\nThe Holy Quran first mentions what the Jews and Christians would say when the qibla was changed as was mentioned previously that for about sixteen to seventeen months, the Holy Prophet(saws) offered salah facing the Baitul Muqaddas which was sacred to all the three – Jews, Christians and the Muslims and which was built by Dawood(as) and his son Sulaiman(as); but the Holy Prophet(saws) was in favour of facing the Kaaba which was built by Ibraheem(as). The Holy Quran says:\n﴿نَرَىٰ تَقَلُّبَ وَجْهِكَ فِي السَّمَاءِ ۖ فَلَنُوَلِّيَنَّكَ قِبْلَةً تَرْضَاهَا ۚ فَوَلِّ وَجْهَكَ شَطْرَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ ۚ وَحَيْثُ مَا كُنتُمْ فَوَلُّوا وُجُوهَكُمْ شَطْرَهُ ۗ وَإِنَّ الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتَابَ لَيَعْلَمُونَ أَنَّهُ الْحَقُّ مِن رَّبِّهِمْ ۗ وَمَا اللَّـهُ بِغَافِلٍ عَمَّا يَعْمَلُونَ ١٤٤﴾\nWe see the turning of thy face (for guidance to the heavens: now Shall We turn thee to a Qibla that shall please thee. Turn then Thy face in the direction of the sacred Mosque: Wherever ye are, turn your faces in that direction. The people of the Book know well that that is the truth from their Lord. Nor is Allah unmindful of what they do.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-144)\nThese verses made the truth clear that the prophet whose coming was predicted by Ibraheem(as) in the books was none other than Muhammad(saws), and ‘Baitullah’ is one of the signs of Ibraheem(as) which was built by him along with his son Ismael(as). It was to welcome this prophet that the Jews had settled in Arabia. But when the Holy Prophet(saws) arrived, the ‘people of the Book’ refused to accept him as a messenger because he was from Bani-Ismael when in their heart of hearts they recognized him as the prophet whose advent they were waiting for. They should have known that Allah(swt) is not unaware of what they do.\nFrom the above verses it is also clear that the Holy Prophet(saws) wished that Allah(swt) would make Kaaba the qibla of the Muslims because it was one of the signs of Ibraheem(as) and Islam was in fact an extension of the religion of Ibraheem(as). It is surprising that even though the ‘people of the Book’(namely the Jews and Christians) also knew this they made the Baitul Muqaddas the qibla instead of the Kaaba and when following the command of Allah(swt), the Holy Prophet again changed the qibla to Kaaba, they became his(saws) bitter enemies and they were so far gone that they refused to accept any proof. Referring to this, the Holy Quran says:\nوَلَئِنْ أَتَيْتَ الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتَابَ بِكُلِّ آيَةٍ مَّا تَبِعُوا قِبْلَتَكَ ۚ وَمَا أَنتَ بِتَابِعٍ قِبْلَتَهُمْ ۚ وَمَا بَعْضُهُم بِتَابِعٍ قِبْلَةَ بَعْضٍ\nEven if thou wert to bring to the people of the Book all the Signs (together), they would not follow Thy Qibla; nor art thou going to follow their Qibla; nor indeed will they follow each other's Qibla.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-145)\nWhen such is the case, it is not right for the Holy Prophet(saws) to follow the Jews and Christians in order to please them when the Almighty Allah(swt) has given him knowledge through His(swt) revelations. The Holy Quran says:\nوَلَئِنِ اتَّبَعْتَ أَهْوَاءَهُم مِّن بَعْدِ مَا جَاءَكَ مِنَ الْعِلْمِ ۙ إِنَّكَ إِذًا لَّمِنَ الظَّالِمِينَ\nIf thou after the knowledge hath reached thee, Wert to follow their (vain) desires,-then wert thou Indeed (clearly) in the wrong.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-145)\nThat is, just as the ‘people of the Book’ who even though they had knowledge would not accept the Kaaba as their qibla and thus became transgressors, O Muhammad! if even you after knowledge has come to you follow their vain desires, you will become a transgressor. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَمِنْ حَيْثُ خَرَجْتَ فَوَلِّ وَجْهَكَ شَطْرَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ ۖ وَإِنَّهُ لَلْحَقُّ مِن رَّبِّكَ ۗ وَمَا اللَّـهُ بِغَافِلٍ عَمَّا تَعْمَلُونَ ١٤٩﴾\nFrom whencesoever Thou startest forth, turn Thy face in the direction of the sacred Mosque; that is indeed the truth from the Lord. And Allah is not unmindful of what ye do.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-149)\nSo, the namaz of a Muslim is not valid till he offers it facing the Holy Kaaba. But if he is on a journey or in a place where the qibla cannot be determined accurately, then he should first try his level best to try to determine it and then face the direction which he thinks is the most probable. Under these conditions, if he commits a mistake, that is, faces some other direction other than the Kaaba and offers namaz, then Allah(swt) is the Most Merciful and Most Forgiving."],[257,"§Qisaas\nThe literal meaning of Qisaas is ‘to take revenge’. This is of two types:\nTaking revenge when a person kills somebody. That is, according to Islamic law, the court can give the guilty person the death sentence for killing somebody so that he is prevented from further such acts.\nBefore the advent of Islam, no proper law existed in this regard and so the powerful tribes generally committed atrocities on the powerless ones and in retaliation sometimes killed the entire tribe along with the one guilty person and the war went on for many years as can still be seen in some countries.\nSo, Allah(swt) laid down the law in this matter. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْقِصَاصُ فِي الْقَتْلَى ۖ الْحُرُّ بِالْحُرِّ وَالْعَبْدُ بِالْعَبْدِ وَالْأُنثَىٰ بِالْأُنثَىٰ ۚ فَمَنْ عُفِيَ لَهُ مِنْ أَخِيهِ شَيْءٌ فَاتِّبَاعٌ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ وَأَدَاءٌ إِلَيْهِ بِإِحْسَانٍ ۗ ذَٰلِكَ تَخْفِيفٌ مِّن رَّبِّكُمْ وَرَحْمَةٌ ۗ فَمَنِ اعْتَدَىٰ بَعْدَ ذَٰلِكَ فَلَهُ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ ١٧٨ وَلَكُمْ فِي الْقِصَاصِ حَيَاةٌ يَا أُولِي الْأَلْبَابِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَّقُونَ ١٧٩﴾\nO ye who believe! the law of equality is prescribed to you in cases of murder: the free for the free, the slave for the slave, the woman for the woman. But if any remission is made by the brother of the slain, then grant any reasonable demand, and compensate him with handsome gratitude, this is a concession and a Mercy from your Lord. After this whoever exceeds the limits shall be in grave penalty. In the Law of Equality there is (saving of) Life to you, o ye men of understanding; that ye may restrain yourselves.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verses-178-179)\nFrom the above verses, the following rules can be deduced:\nAllah(swt) has laid down the Qisaas for saving the lives of many because with the Qisaas of one person, the lives of many others will be saved.\nIf the heir of the person killed decides to take blood-money instead, then it is allowed as is narrated in one sahih hadith. The Holy Prophet(saws) said,\n“The heir of the person killed can either kill the murderer, accept blood-money or forgive the killer.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 4290 and Sahih Muslim, 1354)\nIf the blood-money has been taken or the killer has been forgiven, then do not again kill the person else it will be considered an excess on your part.\nLetting go of one’s rights and forgiving has been praised in the Holy Quran:\nوَأَن تَعْفُوا أَقْرَبُ لِلتَّقْوَىٰ\nremission is the nearest to righteousness.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-237)\nIt is important to understand that killings are of two types which are described in the Holy Quran and Sahih Hadith:\nKilling somebody accidentally:\nThat is, the intention was not to kill but it happened by mistake. For instance instead of the bullet hitting the animal aimed at, hit a person or a small child or an insane person kills somebody unintentionally. Under Islamic law these are called as ‘Katl-e-Qata’ (killing by mistake) and the repentance for it is:\nThe murderer should free a believing slave and if he is unable to do so, he should fast continuously for two months and keep begging Allah(swt) for forgiveness.\nThe relatives of the killed person should be given the blood-money, which has been mentioned in the sahih hadith as a hundred camels or the equivalent amount in gold or silver or money.\nThe Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَمَا كَانَ لِمُؤْمِنٍ أَن يَقْتُلَ مُؤْمِنًا إِلَّا خَطَأً ۚ وَمَن قَتَلَ مُؤْمِنًا خَطَأً فَتَحْرِيرُ رَقَبَةٍ مُّؤْمِنَةٍ وَدِيَةٌ مُّسَلَّمَةٌ إِلَىٰ أَهْلِهِ إِلَّا أَن يَصَّدَّقُوا ۚ فَإِن كَانَ مِن قَوْمٍ عَدُوٍّ لَّكُمْ وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ فَتَحْرِيرُ رَقَبَةٍ مُّؤْمِنَةٍ ۖ وَإِن كَانَ مِن قَوْمٍ بَيْنَكُمْ وَبَيْنَهُم مِّيثَاقٌ فَدِيَةٌ مُّسَلَّمَةٌ إِلَىٰ أَهْلِهِ وَتَحْرِيرُ رَقَبَةٍ مُّؤْمِنَةٍ ۖ فَمَن لَّمْ يَجِدْ فَصِيَامُ شَهْرَيْنِ مُتَتَابِعَيْنِ تَوْبَةً مِّنَ اللَّـهِ ۗ وَكَانَ اللَّـهُ عَلِيمًا حَكِيمًا ٩٢﴾\nNever should a believer kill a believer; but (If it so happens) by mistake, (Compensation is due): If one (so) kills a believer, it is ordained that he should free a believing slave, and pay compensation to the deceased's family, unless they remit it freely. If the deceased belonged to a people at war with you, and he was a believer, the freeing of a believing slave (Is enough). If he belonged to a people with whom ye have treaty of Mutual alliance, compensation should be paid to his family, and a believing slave be freed. For those who find this beyond their means, (is prescribed) a fast for two months running: by way of repentance to Allah: for Allah hath all knowledge and all wisdom.\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-92)\nKilling somebody intentionally:\nIf somebody kills a person intentionally and the guilt has been proved in a court of law, then according to Islamic law, the murderer should be sentenced to death. In Islamic terminology this is called ‘Qisaas’. The Holy Quran says:\nيَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْقِصَاصُ فِي الْقَتْلَى\nO ye who believe! the law of equality is prescribed to you in cases of murder.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-178)\nWe understand from above that Islam considers human life very sacred. It does not allow it to be destroyed in any way. If somebody kills somebody without a valid reason, it is considered a grave sin. Stressing the sanctity of human life, the Holy Quran says that a person who kills one person without reason is like the one who has killed the entire humanity.\n(See:Quran, Surah-5, Al-Maaida, Verse-32)\nAnd if somebody kills a believer intentionally, then he will be punished in two ways. Firstly in this earthly life he will be punished according to the Islamic court of law(as described in Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-178) and secondly he will have to face the punishment in the Hereafter as the Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَمَن يَقْتُلْ مُؤْمِنًا مُّتَعَمِّدًا فَجَزَاؤُهُ جَهَنَّمُ خَالِدًا فِيهَا وَغَضِبَ اللَّـهُ عَلَيْهِ وَلَعَنَهُ وَأَعَدَّ لَهُ عَذَابًا عَظِيمًا ٩٣﴾\nIf a man kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell, to abide therein (For ever): And the wrath and the curse of Allah are upon him, and a dreadful penalty is prepared for him.\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-93)\nWe understand from above that while it is a grave sin to kill any human being whose punishment will have to be borne in this world, the killing of a believer is an even more serious offence whose punishment will have to be faced not only in this world but also in the Hereafter.\nIn the case of intentional murder, Islam provides a clause that the heir of the victim can take blood-money and pardon the killer.\nA third type of killing has been described in the hadith which is termed ‘Shibh Amad’. It means a murder which is similar to killing intentionally. For example a person hits somebody with a stick and he dies, somebody dies due to a slap or maybe a person frightens somebody sitting on a roof and the person falls to his death. In similar cases, the idea was not to kill and neither was a murder weapon used. So, the law in this case is similar to the law applicable in the case of accidental killing. It is important to note here that the Islamic court of law should decide the type of killing and the punishment which it entails and it is not the prerogative of any individual to decide these things.\nRevenge for some hurt or injury: It may be in the form of some injury, cutting off of some part of the body or making some organ useless for example loss of speech or smell, loss of fertility etc. In the above cases Qisaas is applicable except in the case where some organ was made useless because in the case of Qisaas, equality is compulsory and any excess will be a sin and in this case equality is impossible. So, the court will take a decision in this respect.\nThis is a brief description of the Islamic law pertaining to Qisaas which actually is a very important and vast subject. This is to safeguard the human life, property and human dignity."],[258,"§Qisas\nQisas is the plural of ‘Qissa’.\nAt various places in the Holy Quran, many ancient tribes have been described. The disbelievers of Makka termed these historical incidents as ancient stories and tried their best to turn people away from Quran. They also said that the stories of Rome and Iran were better than these. There were some foolish people who went to Iran and brought back the stories of Isfandayar etc. The Holy Quran describes these as follows:\n﴿وَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَن يَشْتَرِي لَهْوَ الْحَدِيثِ لِيُضِلَّ عَن سَبِيلِ اللَّـهِ بِغَيْرِ عِلْمٍ وَيَتَّخِذَهَا هُزُوًا ۚ أُولَـٰئِكَ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ مُّهِينٌ ٦ وَإِذَا تُتْلَىٰ عَلَيْهِ آيَاتُنَا وَلَّىٰ مُسْتَكْبِرًا كَأَن لَّمْ يَسْمَعْهَا كَأَنَّ فِي أُذُنَيْهِ وَقْرًا ۖ فَبَشِّرْهُ بِعَذَابٍ أَلِيمٍ ٧﴾\nBut there are, among men, those who purchase idle tales, without knowledge (or meaning), to mislead (men) from the Path of Allah and throw ridicule (on the Path): for such there will be a Humiliating Penalty. When Our Signs are rehearsed to such a one, he turns away in arrogance, as if he heard them not, as if there were deafness in both his ears: announce to him a grievous Penalty.\n(Quran, Surah-31, Luqman, Verses-6-7)\nThese people either do not know or do not accept that these are not ancient stories but the stories of the tribes who had rejected monotheism and practiced polytheism and so Allah(swt) sent various prophets for their guidance. But when they were arrogantly adamant and did not become believers, Allah(swt) seized them in a painful torment. Allah(swt) describes these incidents in various ways so that the people who had strayed from the right path take heed and mend their ways. These incidents are basically confrontations between truth and falsehood, with Allah(swt) and the prophets calling the people towards truth and paradise and the satan and his followers leading them astray and ultimately towards hell-fire. The final triumph will be of truth and justice.\nوَاللَّهُ يَدْعُو إِلَىٰ دَارِ السَّلَامِ\nBut Allah doth call to the Home of Peace.\n(Quran, Surah-10, Yunus, Verse-25)\nAfter he was bestowed with prophethood, the Holy Prophet(saws) stayed for about ten years in Makka and then migrated to Madina and then in about twelve years Islam had entered every house in Arabia. After the death of the Holy Prophet(saws), Islam spread to every corner of the world in just a few years.\nWe thus understand that the stories of the ancient tribes are in fact lessons to the people who oppose Islam that Islam cannot be stopped or wiped out."],[259,"§Qiyamat\nQiyamat is also called ‘Doomsday’. This is described in all religions in one way or the other. The last book of revelation, the Holy Quran describes this in great detail. The various signs and characteristics of Doomsday are described both in the Holy Quran and the sahih hadith and they can be classified into two groups:\nFirst: The major signs of Qiyamat\nThe advent of Prophet Muhammad(saws):\nThis is the greatest sign of the Doomsday being near. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿فَهَلْ يَنظُرُونَ إِلَّا السَّاعَةَ أَن تَأْتِيَهُم بَغْتَةً ۖ فَقَدْ جَاءَ أَشْرَاطُهَا ۚ فَأَنَّىٰ لَهُمْ إِذَا جَاءَتْهُمْ ذِكْرَاهُمْ ١٨﴾\nDo they then only wait for the Hour,- that it should come on them of a sudden? But already have come some tokens thereof, and when it (actually) is on them, how can they benefit then by their admonition?\n(Quran, Surah-47, Muhammad, Verse-18)\nThat is, Prophet Muhammad(saws) is the last prophet and no prophet will be sent down after him till the Doomsday. So, the advent of the Last Prophet(saws) means that Doomsday is near. It is narrated in one sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n“Qiyamat and me are like two fingers who are very close.”\n(Bukhari, 4936 and Muslim, 2950)\nThe second coming of Isa(as) to this earth:\nThe Holy Quran says:\n﴿بَل رَّفَعَهُ اللَّـهُ إِلَيْهِ ۚ وَكَانَ اللَّـهُ عَزِيزًا حَكِيمًا ١٥٨ وَإِن مِّنْ أَهْلِ الْكِتَابِ إِلَّا لَيُؤْمِنَنَّ بِهِ قَبْلَ مَوْتِهِ ۖ وَيَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ يَكُونُ عَلَيْهِمْ شَهِيدًا ١٥٩﴾\nNay, Allah raised him up unto Himself; and Allah is Exalted in Power, Wise;-\nAnd there is none of the People of the Book but must believe in him before his death; and on the Day of Judgment he will be a witness against them;-\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verses-158, 159)\nThat is, when Doomsday is near, Isa(as) will come down from the sky. Then, all ‘the people of the book’ will bear witness that he is a prophet.\nThe arrival of Gog and Magog:\nThe Holy Quran says:\n﴿حَتَّىٰ إِذَا فُتِحَتْ يَأْجُوجُ وَمَأْجُوجُ وَهُم مِّن كُلِّ حَدَبٍ يَنسِلُونَ ٩٦ وَاقْتَرَبَ الْوَعْدُ الْحَقُّ فَإِذَا هِيَ شَاخِصَةٌ أَبْصَارُ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا يَا وَيْلَنَا قَدْ كُنَّا فِي غَفْلَةٍ مِّنْ هَـٰذَا بَلْ كُنَّا ظَالِمِينَ ٩٧﴾\nUntil the Gog and Magog (people) are let through (their barrier), and they swiftly swarm from every hill. Then will the true promise draw nigh (of fulfilment): then behold! the eyes of the Unbelievers will fixedly stare in horror: \"Ah! Woe to us! we were indeed heedless of this; nay, we truly did wrong!\"\n(Quran, Surah-21, Al-Anbiya, Verses-96-97)\nFor more information on Gog and Magog see Gog-Magog.\nDaabba:\nThe meaning is ‘one who walks on earth’. When the Doomsday is near Allah(swt) will make an animal to appear which will talk to humans. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَإِذَا وَقَعَ الْقَوْلُ عَلَيْهِمْ أَخْرَجْنَا لَهُمْ دَابَّةً مِّنَ الْأَرْضِ تُكَلِّمُهُمْ أَنَّ النَّاسَ كَانُوا بِآيَاتِنَا لَا يُوقِنُونَ ٨٢﴾\nAnd when the Word is fulfilled against them (the unjust), we shall produce from the earth a beast to (face) them: He will speak to them, for that mankind did not believe with assurance in Our Signs.\n(Quran, Surah-27, An-Naml, Verse-82)\nSmoke will emanate from the sky:\n﴿فَارْتَقِبْ يَوْمَ تَأْتِي السَّمَاءُ بِدُخَانٍ مُّبِينٍ ١٠ يَغْشَى النَّاسَ ۖ هَـٰذَا عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ ١١﴾\nThen watch thou for the Day that the sky will bring forth a kind of smoke (or mist) plainly visible, Enveloping the people: this will be a Penalty Grievous.\n(Quran, Surah-44, Ad-Dukhaan, Verses-10,11)\nAmong the signs of the Doomsday which have been described in the sahih hadith, the appearance of smoke is one.\n(Sahih Muslim, 2901)\nBut we come to know from one hadith of sahih Bukhari that when the Holy Prophet(saws) cursed the people of Makka, there was a famine there and the people were writhing with the pangs of hunger. When they looked up towards the sky, they saw it enveloped in smoke. Then the above verses of surah-41, Ad-Dukhaan were revealed.(Bukhari, 4823)\nSo, it is the view of Abdullah-bin-Masood that of the five signs of Doomsday which have already occurred, the appearance of smoke from the sky is one.\n(Bukhari, 4820)\nThe scholars are of the opinion that both the views are true. That is, the event of the smoke has already occurred and will once again occur when Doomsday is near. The other five signs described in sahih Muslim are:\n1.Earthquakes in the eastern countries.\n2.Earthquakes in the western countries.\n3.Earthquakes in the deserts of Arabia.\n4.The rising of the sun from the west.\n5.The starting of a fire from the city of ‘Adan’ in Yemen and the fleeing of the people from it.\nSecond: The state of the world when Doomsday occurs\nWhen Doomsday occurs, this entire creation will be annihilated. The sun and the moon will clash with each other. Mountains will be flying around like cotton wool. Nobody will pay any heed to one another. This has been described vividly in the Holy Quran.\nThe state of the sun, moon and the stars:\n﴿إِذَا الشَّمْسُ كُوِّرَتْ ١ وَإِذَا النُّجُومُ انكَدَرَتْ ٢ وَإِذَا الْجِبَالُ سُيِّرَتْ ٣ وَإِذَا الْعِشَارُ عُطِّلَتْ ٤ وَإِذَا الْوُحُوشُ حُشِرَتْ ٥ وَإِذَا الْبِحَارُ سُجِّرَتْ ٦ وَإِذَا النُّفُوسُ زُوِّجَتْ ٧ وَإِذَا الْمَوْءُودَةُ سُئِلَتْ ٨ بِأَيِّ ذَنبٍ قُتِلَتْ ٩ وَإِذَا الصُّحُفُ نُشِرَتْ ١٠ وَإِذَا السَّمَاءُ كُشِطَتْ ١١ وَإِذَا الْجَحِيمُ سُعِّرَتْ ١٢ وَإِذَا الْجَنَّةُ أُزْلِفَتْ ١٣ عَلِمَتْ نَفْسٌ مَّا أَحْضَرَتْ ١٤﴾\nWhen the sun (with its spacious light) is folded up; When the stars fall, losing their lustre; When the mountains vanish (like a mirage); When the she-camels, ten months with young, are left untended; When the wild beasts are herded together (in the human habitations); When the oceans boil over with a swell; When the souls are sorted out, (being joined, like with like); When the female (infant), buried alive, is questioned - For what crime she was killed; When the scrolls are laid open; When the world on High is unveiled; When the Blazing Fire is kindled to fierce heat; And when the Garden is brought near;- (Then) shall each soul know what it has put forward.\n(Quran, Surah-81, At-Takwir, Verses-1-14)\nAt another place in the Holy Quran the description is as follows:\n﴿يَسْأَلُ أَيَّانَ يَوْمُ الْقِيَامَةِ ٦ فَإِذَا بَرِقَ الْبَصَرُ ٧ وَخَسَفَ الْقَمَرُ ٨ وَجُمِعَ الشَّمْسُ وَالْقَمَرُ ٩ يَقُولُ الْإِنسَانُ يَوْمَئِذٍ أَيْنَ الْمَفَرُّ ١٠ كَلَّا لَا وَزَرَ ١١ إِلَىٰ رَبِّكَ يَوْمَئِذٍ الْمُسْتَقَرُّ ١٢ يُنَبَّأُ الْإِنسَانُ يَوْمَئِذٍ بِمَا قَدَّمَ وَأَخَّرَ ١٣﴾\nHe questions: \"When is the Day of Resurrection?\" At length, when the sight is dazed, And the moon is buried in darkness. And the sun and moon are joined together,- That Day will Man say: \"Where is the refuge?\" By no means! No place of safety! Before thy Lord (alone), that Day will be the place of rest. That Day will Man be told (all) that he put forward, and all that he put back.\n(Quran, Surah-75, Al-Qiyaamah, Verses-6-13)\nThat is, on the day of Resurrection, an account will be taken of every person’s deeds and he will be put either in heaven or hell depending on what the final tally is. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿إِذَا السَّمَاءُ انفَطَرَتْ ١ وَإِذَا الْكَوَاكِبُ انتَثَرَتْ ٢ وَإِذَا الْبِحَارُ فُجِّرَتْ ٣ وَإِذَا الْقُبُورُ بُعْثِرَتْ ٤ عَلِمَتْ نَفْسٌ مَّا قَدَّمَتْ وَأَخَّرَتْ ٥ يَا أَيُّهَا الْإِنسَانُ مَا غَرَّكَ بِرَبِّكَ الْكَرِيمِ ٦ الَّذِي خَلَقَكَ فَسَوَّاكَ فَعَدَلَكَ ٧ فِي أَيِّ صُورَةٍ مَّا شَاءَ رَكَّبَكَ ٨ كَلَّا بَلْ تُكَذِّبُونَ بِالدِّينِ ٩﴾\nWhen the Sky is cleft asunder; When the Stars are scattered; When the Oceans are suffered to burst forth; And when the Graves are turned upside down;- (Then) shall each soul know what it hath sent forward and (what it hath) kept back. O man! What has seduced thee from thy Lord Most Beneficent?- Him Who created thee. Fashioned thee in due proportion, and gave thee a just bias; In whatever Form He wills, does He put thee together. Nay! But ye do reject Right and Judgment!\n(Quran, Surah-82, Al-Infitar, Verses-1-9)\nThe state of the earth and the sky:\nThe Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَمَا قَدَرُوا اللَّـهَ حَقَّ قَدْرِهِ وَالْأَرْضُ جَمِيعًا قَبْضَتُهُ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ وَالسَّمَاوَاتُ مَطْوِيَّاتٌ بِيَمِينِهِ ۚ سُبْحَانَهُ وَتَعَالَىٰ عَمَّا يُشْرِكُونَ ٦٧﴾\nNo just estimate have they made of Allah, such as is due to Him: On the Day of Judgment the whole of the earth will be but His handful, and the heavens will be rolled up in His right hand: Glory to Him! High is He above the Partners they attribute to Him!\n(Quran, Surah-39, Az-Zumar, Verse-67)\n﴿إِذَا زُلْزِلَتِ الْأَرْضُ زِلْزَالَهَا ١ وَأَخْرَجَتِ الْأَرْضُ أَثْقَالَهَا ٢ وَقَالَ الْإِنسَانُ مَا لَهَا ٣ يَوْمَئِذٍ تُحَدِّثُ أَخْبَارَهَا ٤ بِأَنَّ رَبَّكَ أَوْحَىٰ لَهَا ٥﴾\nWhen the earth is shaken to her (utmost) convulsion, And the earth throws up her burdens (from within), And man cries (distressed): 'What is the matter with her?'- On that Day will she declare her tidings: For that thy Lord will have given her inspiration.\n(Quran, Surah-99, Al-Zilzal, Verses-1-5)\nThe state of the mountains:\n﴿الْقَارِعَةُ ١ مَا الْقَارِعَةُ ٢ وَمَا أَدْرَاكَ مَا الْقَارِعَةُ ٣ يَوْمَ يَكُونُ النَّاسُ كَالْفَرَاشِ الْمَبْثُوثِ ٤ وَتَكُونُ الْجِبَالُ كَالْعِهْنِ الْمَنفُوشِ ٥﴾\nThe (Day) of Noise and Clamour: What is the (Day) of Noise and Clamour? And what will explain to thee what the (Day) of Noise and Clamour is? (It is) a Day whereon men will be like moths scattered about, And the mountains will be like carded wool.\n(Quran, Surah-101, Al-Qaari’a, Verses-1-5)\nIn this way the Holy Quran describes in great detail all the signs and occurrences on the day of Resurrection so that man takes heed of the warning and rectifies his book of deeds so that when it is presented to Allah(swt) on that day, the Almighty is pleased with him and he gets to lead an everlasting life of joy in paradise.\n﴿لَا أُقْسِمُ بِيَوْمِ الْقِيَامَةِ ١ وَلَا أُقْسِمُ بِالنَّفْسِ اللَّوَّامَةِ ٢ أَيَحْسَبُ الْإِنسَانُ أَلَّن نَّجْمَعَ عِظَامَهُ ٣ بَلَىٰ قَادِرِينَ عَلَىٰ أَن نُّسَوِّيَ بَنَانَهُ ٤﴾\nI do call to witness the Resurrection Day; And I do call to witness the self-reproaching spirit: (Eschew Evil). Does man think that We cannot assemble his bones? Nay, We are able to put together in perfect order the very tips of his fingers.\n(Quran, Surah-75, Al-Qiyaamah, Verses-1-4)\nThat is, Almighty Allah(swt) is All-Powerful. He(swt) can do anything He(swt) wishes. That is why on the day of Resurrection, He(swt) can re-assemble all the decayed bones of all mankind right up to their finger-tips and He(swt) shall make everybody stand in front of Him."],[260,"§Qula\nJust as a man can separate from his wife with the help of ‘Talaq’, a woman can separate from her husband with the help of ‘Qula’. And it is the greatness of Islam that it has given equal status to both men and women. Just as a man can get frustrated with the bad behaviour of his wife and not be able to live happily with her, a woman also can be fed up of the evil nature of her husband and not be able to live peacefully with him. Islam has given a woman the right to separate from her husband and this is ‘Qula’. The Holy Quran says:\nفَإِنْ خِفْتُمْ أَلَّا يُقِيمَا حُدُودَ اللَّهِ فَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْهِمَا فِيمَا افْتَدَتْ بِهِ ۗ\nIf ye (judges) do indeed fear that they would be unable to keep the limits ordained by Allah, there is no blame on either of them if she give something for her freedom.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-229)\nIn this verse, ‘to give something’ means the money spent for Meher and Nikah. Because the man has given ‘meher’ for marriage and has spent money for ‘valima’, it is only just that the wife return him his money and go away to her parents’ house because the man has to pay ‘meher’ again to remarry.\nThe scholars are of the opinion that demanding more money than the ‘meher’ is not right.\nIt is narrated in one sahih hadith that the wife of Saabit-bin-Qais came to the Holy Prophet(saws) and said, “O Prophet of Allah(swt), I have no problem with the religion or character of Saabit but in spite of being a Muslim I fear Kufr.” (that is I cannot live with him). Upon which the Holy Prophet(saws) asked, “Can you return him his orchard?” The lady replied, “Yes, I can.” So, the Holy Prophet(saws) ordered her to return the orchard and both the husband and wife were separated.” ( Sahih Bukhari 5273)\nIt is narrated in another hadith that she replied that she could return the orchard and also give some extra money. But this hadith is not reliable.\nMany scholars are of the opinion that ‘Qula’ is not ‘divorce’ but ‘Fisq’ as they have the following differences:\nTalaq has ‘turning back’ but not Qula.\nDivorce is done in a state of purity when there has been no intercourse. There is no such restriction in the case of Qula.\nIn the case of triple talaq it is necessary that the woman marries someone else and only after the other divorces her can she remarry the first husband. In the case of Qula, the woman can remarry the same person after accepting a new meher.\nThe iddat or the waiting period is three months in the case of talaq while it is one month in the case of Qula. Some scholars feel that the iddat is the same for both talaq and Qula. Due to these differences, it appears that Qula is not divorce but ‘Fisq’."],[261,"§Qummal\nIn the Holy Quran, the Qummal has been described only once:\n﴿فَأَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمُ الطُّوفَانَ وَالْجَرَادَ وَالْقُمَّلَ وَالضَّفَادِعَ وَالدَّمَ آيَاتٍ مُّفَصَّلَاتٍ فَاسْتَكْبَرُوا وَكَانُوا قَوْمًا مُّجْرِمِينَ ١٣٣﴾\nSo We sent upon them the flood and locusts and lice and frogs and blood as distinct signs, but they were arrogant and were a criminal people.\n(Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-133)\nIn the Arabic language, the word used is ‘Qummal’ which the majority of the commentators say is a small worm which lives as a parasite on the camels. So it has been called a louse but from the description in the Holy Quran it is possibly a small worm which eats up whatever is left over after the locusts have attacked. When the tribe of Pharaoh(Firaun) rejected the religion of Allah(swt) and His(swt) prophet Musa(as), Allah(swt) sent down upon them flood, locusts, small worms, frogs and blood and made their lives impossible."],[262,"§Quraish\nThis word occurs only once in the Holy Quran in Surah-Quraish:\n﴿لِإِيلَافِ قُرَيْشٍ ١ إِيلَافِهِمْ رِحْلَةَ الشِّتَاءِ وَالصَّيْفِ ٢ فَلْيَعْبُدُوا رَبَّ هَٰذَا الْبَيْتِ ٣ الَّذِي أَطْعَمَهُم مِّن جُوعٍ وَآمَنَهُم مِّنْ خَوْفٍ ٤﴾\nFor the covenants (of security and safeguard enjoyed) by the Quraish, Their covenants (covering) journeys by winter and summer,- Let them adore the Lord of this House, Who provides them with food against hunger, and with security against fear (of danger).\n(Quran, Surah-106, Al-Quraish, Verses-1-4)\nQuraish was the name of the best and most prominent tribe of Makka whose genealogy went up to ‘Fahar’ who was named ‘Quraish’ and Muhammad(saws) was from among his descendants. The genealogy from Muhammad(saws) to Fahar is as follows:\nMuhammad(saws) (bin) Abdullah (bin) Abdul Mutallib (bin)Hashim(bin) Abd Manaf(bin) Khusai(bin) Kilab (bin) Murra (bin) Ka’ab (bin) Lui (bin) Fahar. This is the same Fahar whose name was Quraish and the Quraish of Makka were his relatives and descendants.\nThe genealogy before Fahar is as follows:\nFahar(bin) Maalik (bin) Nazar (bin) Kinana (bin) Khuzaima (bin) Mudrika (bin) Iyas (bin) Nizar (bin) Ma’ad (bin) Adnan).\nAll the historians and scholars of hadith agree that Muhammad(saws) was from the descendants of this same Adnan and they also agree that the family tree of Adnan goes up to Ismael(as) the son of Ibraheem(as) who had settled down in Makka. But there is a difference of opinion pertaining to the genealogy from Ismael(as) to Adnan(as). It is as follows:\nAdnan (bin) Adh (bin) Yajid (bin) Yakdud (bin) Muqawwam (bin) Yasa (bin) Khedar (bin) Ismael(as).\nAllah(swt) chose Muhammad(saws) from the family of Ismael(as) as narrated in a sahih hadith:\n“Allah(swt) chose Kanana from the descendants of Ismael, and from Kanana He(swt) chose Quraish, and from Quraish He(swt) chose Banu-Hashim and me from Banu-Hashim.” ( Sahih Muslim, 2276)\nAllah(swt) gave the Quraish a lot of honour because they were the custodians of the Holy Kaaba. They had relations with all the tribes of Arab. They went on trade journeys to Yemen in winter and to Syria in summer and moreover all the people of Arab would come to Makka for the Haj. Due to this their relations with all the Arabs were further strengthened and thus Allah(swt) in His infinite wisdom made them secure from hunger forever when most of Makka is desert wasteland unfit for cultivation as is described in the Holy Quran(Surah-14, Ibraheem, Verse-37) And in the whole of Arabia, only Makka has been made the ‘city of peace’.\nAllah(swt) raised Muhammad(saws) from this tribe only. So, they should have been the first to accept the message of the Holy Prophet(saws), but they were the foremost on opposing him because they were scared of losing their leadership. So, they even engaged in wars with him in which they were the losers and they lost many of their chieftains. In 8 A.H, the disbelievers of Makka were finally defeated and the true religion Islam was established. Then, all the people of Quraish embraced Islam. They did not lose their power and respect but in fact became more strong and esteemed.\nAfter the Holy Prophet(saws), the four caliphs who succeeded him(saws) and were called ‘Khulfa-e-Rashideen’ meaning the ‘the pious caliphs’ were also from the tribe of Quraish. Their names were:\nAbu-Bakr Siddique, Umar Farooq, Usman Ghani and Ali (ra)."],[263,"§Quran\nQuran is the last divine book of revelation which was revealed to the Last Prophet Muhammad(saws) over a period of twenty three years. Firstly it would be instilled in the heart of the Holy Prophet(saws), then upon his reciting it, his companions would write it down on various things. Then, when Abu Bakr(ra) became the caliph, he collected all the material, divided it into parts and assembled it as a book. Then, when Usman(ra) became the caliph, he made many copies of this book and distributed them in the Islamic world. Till, today the Holy Quran is being published according to those copies. In this way Allah(swt) has ensured that the Holy Quran remains unchanged till Doomsday and has taken its responsibility. Allah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿إِنَّا نَحْنُ نَزَّلْنَا الذِّكْرَ وَإِنَّا لَهُ لَحَافِظُونَ ٩﴾\nWe have, without doubt, sent down the Message; and We will assuredly guard it (from corruption).\n(Quran, Surah-15, Al-Hijr, Verse-9)\nToday, the Holy Quran is the only divine book which has remained unchanged and will remain so till Doomsday. All the other divine books have undergone many changes down the ages.\nWhen the Holy Quran was first written, it did not have any signs because the Arabs did not find them necessary. But when Islam spread beyond the Arab world, the non-Arabs found it difficult to read the Holy Quran without them, so, when Abdul Malik-bin-Marwan became the caliph in 65 A.H, he ordered the linguist Abdul-Aswad Duvli (who died in 69 A.H.) to affix signs to the text in the Holy Quran so that people would not commit mistakes while reading the Holy Quran. In this way Allah(swt) ensured that the Holy Quran would not be recited wrongly. Then with the invention of the printing press, the Holy Quran started being published in every corner of the world. Today, the biggest printing press of the Holy Quran is in Madina. Its name is ‘Shah Fahd Quran Press Trust’ which was established on 30 October, 1984. From then to 2000 A.D, more than 1.5 crore copies of the Holy Quran have been published. In the same way, till 1999, the trust had printed the translations of the Holy Quran in the following 29 languages:\nUrdu, Spanish, Albanian, Indonesian, English, Anco, Uraami, Igaria, Barahoia, Pashto, Bengali, Bargi, Busti, Tamil, Thai, Turkish, Zulu, Somali, Chinese, Parsi, French, Kazachi, Kashmiri, Kori, Maqdooni, Malabari, Hosa, Purba and Greek.\nBefore judging a religious book and accepting it, it is necessary to understand what it says about itself. The Holy Quran says about itself:\n1.This has been sent down from Allah(swt):\nقُلِ اللَّهُ ۖ شَهِيدٌ بَيْنِي وَبَيْنَكُمْ ۚ وَأُوحِيَ إِلَيَّ هَٰذَا الْقُرْآنُ لِأُنذِرَكُم بِهِ وَمَن بَلَغَ ۚ أَئِنَّكُمْ لَتَشْهَدُونَ أَنَّ مَعَ اللَّهِ آلِهَةً أُخْرَىٰ\nSay: \"Allah is witness between me and you; This Qur'an hath been revealed to me by inspiration, that I may warn you and all whom it reaches. Can ye possibly bear witness that besides Allah there is another Allah?\"\n(Quran, Surah-6, Al-An’aam, Verse-19)\n﴿إِنَّا نَحْنُ نَزَّلْنَا عَلَيْكَ الْقُرْآنَ تَنزِيلًا ٢٣﴾\nIt is We Who have sent down the Qur'an to thee by stages.\n(Quran, Surah-76, Ad-Dahar, Verse-23)\n﴿أَوَلَمْ يَكْفِهِمْ أَنَّا أَنزَلْنَا عَلَيْكَ الْكِتَابَ يُتْلَىٰ عَلَيْهِمْ ۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَرَحْمَةً وَذِكْرَىٰ لِقَوْمٍ يُؤْمِنُونَ ٥١﴾\nAnd is it not enough for them that we have sent down to thee the Book which is rehearsed to them? Verily, in it is Mercy and a Reminder to those who believe.\n(Quran, Surah-29, Al-Ankaboot, Verse-51)\n﴿إِنَّا أَنزَلْنَا إِلَيْكَ الْكِتَابَ بِالْحَقِّ فَاعْبُدِ اللَّهَ مُخْلِصًا لَّهُ الدِّينَ ٢﴾\nVerily it is We Who have revealed the Book to thee in Truth: so serve Allah, offering Him sincere devotion.\n(Quran, Surah-39, Az-Zumar, Verse-2)\n﴿نَحْنُ نَقُصُّ عَلَيْكَ أَحْسَنَ الْقَصَصِ بِمَا أَوْحَيْنَا إِلَيْكَ هَٰذَا الْقُرْآنَ وَإِن كُنتَ مِن قَبْلِهِ لَمِنَ الْغَافِلِينَ ٣﴾\nWe do relate unto thee the most beautiful of stories, in that We reveal to thee this (portion of the) Qur'an: before this, thou too was among those who knew it not.\n(Quran, Surah-12, Yusuf, Verse-3)\nAnd We have bestowed upon thee the Seven Oft-repeated (verses) and the Grand Qur'an.\n﴿وَلَقَدْ آتَيْنَاكَ سَبْعًا مِّنَ الْمَثَانِي وَالْقُرْآنَ الْعَظِيمَ ٨٧﴾\n(Quran, Surah-15, Al-Hijr, Verse-87)\nAs to thee, the Qur'an is bestowed upon thee from the presence of one who is wise and all-knowing.\n﴿وَإِنَّكَ لَتُلَقَّى الْقُرْآنَ مِن لَّدُنْ حَكِيمٍ عَلِيمٍ ٦﴾\n(Quran, Surah-27, An-Naml, Verse-6)\nThus, we come to know that the Holy Quran is the book of Allah(swt). Other than the Holy Quran, there is no other religious book which categorically claims to be the book of Allah(swt). In fact Allah(swt) had warned the Holy Prophet(saws) that if he had attributed something of his own to the Holy Quran, then Allah(swt) would have seized his hand and cut off the artery of his heart. (See:Quran, Surah-69, Al-Haaqqa, Verse-45)\nWe come to know from this that the whole of the Holy Quran is from Allah(swt). In fact at one place, the Holy Quran claims that whatever the Holy Prophet(saws) says is only through revelation and not of his own desire.(See:Quran, Surah-53, An-Najm, Verse-3)\nQuran – a miracle\n2.The Holy Quran is such a miraculous book that the whole mankind combined cannot write a similar book:\n﴿قُل لَّئِنِ اجْتَمَعَتِ الْإِنسُ وَالْجِنُّ عَلَىٰ أَن يَأْتُوا بِمِثْلِ هَٰذَا الْقُرْآنِ لَا يَأْتُونَ بِمِثْلِهِ وَلَوْ كَانَ بَعْضُهُمْ لِبَعْضٍ ظَهِيرًا ٨٨﴾\nSay: \"If the whole of mankind and Jinns were to gather together to produce the like of this Qur'an, they could not produce the like thereof, even if they backed up each other with help and support.\n(Quran, Surah-17, Bani-Israel, Verse-88)\nThe Holy Quran posed this challenge to those people who considered themselves great scholars of Arabic. Compared to them the Holy Prophet(saws) was illiterate. Even then, they said that the Holy Prophet(saws) was reciting the verses on his own. So, the Holy Quran poses a challenge to all these proud disbelievers to bring forth along with the jinn another book like it? The answer is of course that they cannot.\nThen, the Holy Quran poses a challenge to bring forth at least ten verses similar to the ones in it:\n﴿أَمْ يَقُولُونَ افْتَرَاهُ ۖ قُلْ فَأْتُوا بِعَشْرِ سُوَرٍ مِّثْلِهِ مُفْتَرَيَاتٍ وَادْعُوا مَنِ اسْتَطَعْتُم مِّن دُونِ اللَّهِ إِن كُنتُمْ صَادِقِينَ ١٣﴾\nOr they may say, \"He forged it,\" Say, \"Bring ye then ten suras forged, like unto it, and call (to your aid) whomsoever ye can, other than Allah!- If ye speak the truth!\n(Quran, Surah-11, Hud, Verse-13)\nAnd when they failed to bring forth ten similar verses, then the Holy Quran challenged them to produce at least one such verse:\n﴿وَإِن كُنتُمْ فِي رَيْبٍ مِّمَّا نَزَّلْنَا عَلَىٰ عَبْدِنَا فَأْتُوا بِسُورَةٍ مِّن مِّثْلِهِ وَادْعُوا شُهَدَاءَكُم مِّن دُونِ اللَّهِ إِن كُنتُمْ صَادِقِينَ ٢٣﴾\nAnd if ye are in doubt as to what We have revealed from time to time to Our servant, then produce a Sura like thereunto; and call your witnesses or helpers (If there are any) besides Allah, if your (doubts) are true.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-23)\nBut the disbelievers could not produce a single verse similar to the ones in the Holy Quran and thus it was proved that the Holy Quran was indeed a miracle impossible to reproduce by mere creatures and can only be a revelation from Almighty Allah(swt).\nSpeciality of the Holy Quran:\n3.The Holy Quran has healing properties and is a mercy for mankind:\n﴿وَنُنَزِّلُ مِنَ الْقُرْآنِ مَا هُوَ شِفَاءٌ وَرَحْمَةٌ لِّلْمُؤْمِنِينَ ۙ وَلَا يَزِيدُ الظَّالِمِينَ إِلَّا خَسَارًا ٨٢﴾\nWe send down (stage by stage) in the Qur'an that which is a healing and a mercy to those who believe: to the unjust it causes nothing but loss after loss.\n(Quran, Surah-17, Bani-Israel, Verse-82)\nThat is, the Holy Quran provides healing for all the physical as well as mental afflictions. So, it is necessary that we completely believe in it, instill it firmly in our hearts and lead our lives under its holy guidance. As for the people who do not believe in it and do not consider it as the revelation of the Almighty Allah(swt), they are doubly the losers because neither can they benefit from it in this world nor in the Hereafter. That is, they can neither cure the disease of their heart nor of their body. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَإِذَا مَا أُنزِلَتْ سُورَةٌ فَمِنْهُم مَّن يَقُولُ أَيُّكُمْ زَادَتْهُ هَٰذِهِ إِيمَانًا ۚ فَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا فَزَادَتْهُمْ إِيمَانًا وَهُمْ يَسْتَبْشِرُونَ ١٢٤ وَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ فِي قُلُوبِهِم مَّرَضٌ فَزَادَتْهُمْ رِجْسًا إِلَىٰ رِجْسِهِمْ وَمَاتُوا وَهُمْ كَافِرُونَ ١٢٥﴾\nWhenever there cometh down a sura, some of them say: \"Which of you has had His faith increased by it?\" Yea, those who believe,- their faith is increased and they do rejoice. But those in whose hearts is a disease,- it will add doubt to their doubt, and they will die in a state of Unbelief.\n(Quran, Surah-9, At-Tawba, Verses-124-125)\nThe language of the Holy Quran:\n4.The Holy Quran was revealed by Allah(swt) in Arabic because it was first revealed to the Arabic speaking people and the people addressed also spoke Arabic. If it had been revealed in some other language, these people would have found it difficult to understand it:\nوَكَذَٰلِكَ أَوْحَيْنَا إِلَيْكَ قُرْآنًا عَرَبِيًّا\nThus have We sent by inspiration to thee an Arabic Qur'an\n(Quran, Surah-42, Ash-Shura, Verse-7)\nوَلَوْ جَعَلْنَاهُ قُرْآنًا أَعْجَمِيًّا لَّقَالُوا لَوْلَا فُصِّلَتْ آيَاتُهُ ۖ أَأَعْجَمِيٌّ وَعَرَبِيٌّ\nAnd if We had made it a non-Arabic Qur'an, they would have said, \"Why are its verses not explained in detail [in our language]? Is it a foreign [recitation] and an Arab [messenger]?\"\n(Quran, Surah-41, Fussilat, Verse-44)\nكِتَابٌ فُصِّلَتْ آيَاتُهُ قُرْآنًا عَرَبِيًّا لِّقَوْمٍ يَعْلَمُونَ ﴿٣\nA Book, whereof the verses are explained in detail;- a Qur'an in Arabic, for people who understand;-\n(Quran, Surah-41, Fussilat, Verse-3)\nOne more thing which is to be borne in mind is that all the previous prophets were given the religious books in the language with which they were familiar and so it is only logical that the Holy Prophet(saws) be given the Holy Quran in Arabic which was the language prevalent in those times in Makka and Madina.\nThe Greatness of the Holy Quran:\n5.The Holy Quran is the address of the Almighty Allah(swt) to the people of this world in which He(swt) has clearly explained the rights and duties of mankind so that they are successful both in this life and also in the Hereafter. But the people of this world are heedless of this priceless gift. The greatness and intensity of the Holy Quran is such that had it been revealed on a mountain (if it had life), then it would shudder and break into pieces with fear:\n﴿لَوْ أَنزَلْنَا هَـٰذَا الْقُرْآنَ عَلَىٰ جَبَلٍ لَّرَأَيْتَهُ خَاشِعًا مُّتَصَدِّعًا مِّنْ خَشْيَةِ اللَّـهِ ۚ وَتِلْكَ الْأَمْثَالُ نَضْرِبُهَا لِلنَّاسِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَفَكَّرُونَ ٢١﴾\nHad We sent down this Qur'an on a mountain, verily, thou wouldst have seen it humble itself and cleave asunder for fear of Allah. Such are the similitudes which We propound to men, that they may reflect.\n(Quran, Surah-59, Al-Hashr, Verse-21)\nThe mankind of today have not given the Holy Quran the honour it deserves and that is why the Holy Prophet(saws) will complain on the Day of Resurrection:\n﴿وَقَالَ الرَّسُولُ يَا رَبِّ إِنَّ قَوْمِي اتَّخَذُوا هَـٰذَا الْقُرْآنَ مَهْجُورًا ٣٠﴾\nThen the Messenger will say: \"O my Lord! Truly my people took this Qur'an for just foolish nonsense.\"\n(Quran, Surah-25, Al-Furqaan, Verse-30)\nThe Holy Quran is for everyone\n6.The speciality of the Holy Quran is that its teachings are for all the people living in this world. That is why again and again, the Holy Quran begins its addresses with, ‘O people’, ‘O man’:\nيَا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ اعْبُدُوا رَبَّكُمُ الَّذِي خَلَقَكُمْ وَالَّذِينَ مِن قَبْلِكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَّقُونَ ﴿٢١\nO ye people! Adore your Guardian-Lord, who created you and those who came before you, that ye may have the chance to learn righteousness;\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-21)\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الْإِنسَانُ مَا غَرَّكَ بِرَبِّكَ الْكَرِيمِ ٦﴾\nO man! What has seduced thee from thy Lord Most Beneficent?-\n(Quran, Surah-82, Al-Infitaar, Verse-6)\nToday, the Holy Quran is the only religious book which addresses the whole mankind and whose teachings are for the entire humanity. So, it is wrong to say that the Holy Quran is a book for one particular community. It is for every person who believes in it and accepts it.\nAllah(swt) has said very clearly in the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَمَا أَرْسَلْنَاكَ إِلَّا كَافَّةً لِّلنَّاسِ بَشِيرًا وَنَذِيرًا وَلَـٰكِنَّ أَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُونَ ٢٨﴾\nWe have not sent thee but as a universal (Messenger) to men, giving them glad tidings, and warning them (against sin), but most men understand not.\n(Quran, Surah-34, Saba, Verse-28)\nThe Holy Quran is a giver of glad tidings for the ones who follow its instructions and is a warning to those who pay no heed to it. It is not right to say that whatever the Holy Quran says does not apply to us. These are the people who do not understand the reality of the Holy Quran and for them is everlasting torment in hell while for the people who imbibe its teachings, there is everlasting joy in paradise.\nRecitation of the Holy Quran:\n7.The Holy Quran is such an excellent divine book that how many ever times we recite it, there is a novelty about it and we get the feeling that it has just been revealed. Its content is so instructive and heart-moving that we can seldom remain dry-eyed after reading it with concentration and understanding. We experience a divine peace and our senses feel calm and rested:\n﴿اللَّـهُ نَزَّلَ أَحْسَنَ الْحَدِيثِ كِتَابًا مُّتَشَابِهًا مَّثَانِيَ تَقْشَعِرُّ مِنْهُ جُلُودُ الَّذِينَ يَخْشَوْنَ رَبَّهُمْ ثُمَّ تَلِينُ جُلُودُهُمْ وَقُلُوبُهُمْ إِلَىٰ ذِكْرِ اللَّـهِ ۚ ذَٰلِكَ هُدَى اللَّـهِ يَهْدِي بِهِ مَن يَشَاءُ ۚ وَمَن يُضْلِلِ اللَّـهُ فَمَا لَهُ مِنْ هَادٍ ٢٣﴾\nAllah has revealed (from time to time) the most beautiful Message in the form of a Book, consistent with itself, (yet) repeating (its teaching in various aspects): the skins of those who fear their Lord tremble thereat; then their skins and their hearts do soften to the celebration of Allah's praises. Such is the guidance of Allah: He guides therewith whom He pleases, but such as Allah leaves to stray, can have none to guide.\n(Quran, Surah-39, Az-Zumar, Verse-23)\nAfter enumerating the above specialities of the Holy Quran, let us present a brief commentary. There are basically two means of understanding the Holy Quran:\nThe first means: The Holy Quran itself.\nThe second means: The books other than Quran like the Quran commentaries, Sahih Hadith etc.\nThe first means: The Holy Quran explains the same thing in many ways. So, if we desire to obtain complete knowledge about the Holy Quran, we should first begin by collecting all the different verses pertaining to one subject at one place and then arrange them according to their subject. In this way the central theme of the Holy Quran will become clear. The Holy Quran has referred to itself in many verses. Let us once again look at the 23rd verse of surah-39, Az-Zumar:\nاللَّهُ نَزَّلَ أَحْسَنَ الْحَدِيثِ كِتَابًا مُّتَشَابِهًا مَّثَانِيَ تَقْشَعِرُّ مِنْهُ\nAllah has revealed (from time to time) the most beautiful Message in the form of a Book, consistent with itself, (yet) repeating (its teaching in various aspects).\nIt says at another place:\n﴿وَلَقَدْ صَرَّفْنَا لِلنَّاسِ فِي هَـٰذَا الْقُرْآنِ مِن كُلِّ مَثَلٍ فَأَبَىٰ أَكْثَرُ النَّاسِ إِلَّا كُفُورًا ٨٩﴾\nAnd We have explained to man, in this Qur'an, every kind of similitude: yet the greater part of men refuse (to receive it) except with ingratitude!\n(Quran, Surah-17, Bani-Israel, Verse-89)\nFor detailed explanation see surah-18, Al-Kahf, Verse-54; surah-20, Ta-Ha, Verse-113; Surah-6, Al-An’aam, Verse-46.\nFor example let us look at how the Holy Quran guides us when we want to repent:\n﴿فَتَلَقَّىٰ آدَمُ مِن رَّبِّهِ كَلِمَاتٍ فَتَابَ عَلَيْهِ ۚ إِنَّهُ هُوَ التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيمُ ٣٧﴾\nThen learnt Adam from his Lord words of inspiration, and his Lord Turned towards him; for He is Oft-Returning, Most Merciful.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-37)\nWhat were the words which Adam(as) learnt in order to repent? Let us see how the Holy Quran has made them clear:\n﴿قَالَا رَبَّنَا ظَلَمْنَا أَنفُسَنَا وَإِن لَّمْ تَغْفِرْ لَنَا وَتَرْحَمْنَا لَنَكُونَنَّ مِنَ الْخَاسِرِينَ ٢٣﴾\nThey said: \"Our Lord! We have wronged our own souls: If thou forgive us not and bestow not upon us Thy Mercy, we shall certainly be lost.\"\n(Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raaf, Verse-23)\nSimilarly, the Holy Quran has described the stories of the different prophets, history of various tribes, their good deeds, their sins etc. at various places so that the people learn lessons from them.\nIf all the verses connected with the prophets are collected at one place, then we can learn a great deal about the various prophets. To explain the Holy Quran with its help, the renowned scholar Shaikh Muhammad Ameen Shanketi (expired in 1339 A.H.) has written the commentary ‘Azwaaul Bayaan’ which is published in eight volumes by the ‘Darul Fatwa’ of the Saudi Arab.\nTo completely understand the Holy Quran, a knowledge of Arabic is necessary. The various translations and commentaries are also very useful for this purpose.\nThe second means: The second means to understand the Holy Quran is to study the Sahih Hadith of the Holy Prophet(saws) and his life and behavior because nobody can understand the Holy Quran better than him because he was the one to whom the Holy Quran was revealed. So, the way the Holy Prophet(saws) performed an action and whatever he said is the real explanation of the Holy Quran. The Holy Quran says in this connection:\n﴿إِنَّا أَنزَلْنَا إِلَيْكَ الْكِتَابَ بِالْحَقِّ لِتَحْكُمَ بَيْنَ النَّاسِ بِمَا أَرَاكَ اللَّـهُ ۚ وَلَا تَكُن لِّلْخَائِنِينَ خَصِيمًا ١٠٥﴾\nWe have sent down to thee the Book in truth, that thou mightest judge between men, as guided by Allah: so be not (used) as an advocate by those who betray their trust;\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-105)\nAt another place, the Holy Quran says:\n﴿بِالْبَيِّنَاتِ وَالزُّبُرِ ۗ وَأَنزَلْنَا إِلَيْكَ الذِّكْرَ لِتُبَيِّنَ لِلنَّاسِ مَا نُزِّلَ إِلَيْهِمْ وَلَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَفَكَّرُونَ ٤٤﴾\n(We sent them) with Clear Signs and Books of dark prophecies; and We have sent down unto thee (also) the Message; that thou mayest explain clearly to men what is sent for them, and that they may give thought.\n(Quran, Surah-16, An-Nahl, Verse-44)\nAllah(swt) says:\n﴿وَمَا أَنزَلْنَا عَلَيْكَ الْكِتَابَ إِلَّا لِتُبَيِّنَ لَهُمُ الَّذِي اخْتَلَفُوا فِيهِ ۙ وَهُدًى وَرَحْمَةً لِّقَوْمٍ يُؤْمِنُونَ ٦٤﴾\nAnd We sent down the Book to thee for the express purpose, that thou shouldst make clear to them those things in which they differ, and that it should be a guide and a mercy to those who believe.\n(Quran, Surah-16, An-Nahl, Verse-64)\nIn the same way, according to a Sahih Hadith, the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n“I have been given the Quran, and the ‘sunan’ along with it.”\n(Abu Dawood, 4604 and Musnad Ahmad, 17174)\nThat is why the collectors of the Sahih Hadith, have also added the topic ‘explanation or commentary’ in their books of complete hadith which is nothing but ‘sunan’ or explanation of the Holy Quran. So, any commentary of the Holy Quran which goes against sahih sunan is not correct.\nSome people say that sometimes the sahih sunan clashes with the explanation of the Holy Quran, but this is not right because sahih hadith itself means that it does not go against the Holy Quran.\nWhile explaining the Holy Quran, if we do not understand something clearly either from the Holy Quran or from sahih hadith, then we should try to understand it from the sayings and opinions of the companions of the Holy Prophet(saws) because the Holy Quran was revealed before them and they were also well-acquainted with the hadith of the Holy Prophet(saws). While explaining the Holy Quran, we should give much importance to these companions and their opinions especially the four caliphs – Abu Bakr, Umar, Usman and Ali(ra). After them importance should be given to the Islamic scholars Abdullah-bin-Masood, Abdullah-bin-Abbas etc.\nThere is a very famous saying of Abdullah-bin-Masood which goes as:\n“I swear in the name of Allah(swt), who alone is worthy of worship that there is no verse in the Holy Quran about which I do not have knowledge as to whom it refers to and where it was revealed. If I come to know that there is somebody who has more knowledge than me, then I shall turn my mount towards him.”\nAccording to a sahih hadith, the Holy Prophet(saws) supplicated thus for Abdullah-bin-Abbas:\n“O Allah(swt), give him understanding in this religion and teach him the explanation of Quran.”\nThat is why he is known as ‘Tarjumanul Quran’ which means ‘great scholar of Quran’.\nIf while studying the Holy Quran, we cannot find the clear explanation of something in either the Quran, or the sahih hadith or even the interpretations of the sahabas (companions of the Holy Prophet(saws)), then we should turn to the explanations of the ‘taabayi’. ‘Taabayi’ is the one who has gained knowledge from the sahabas because he has taken the explanation of the Holy Quran from the sahabas. Prominent among these ‘taabiyas’ are Mujahid, Sayeed-bin-Zubair etc.\nCategorization of the teachings of the Holy Quran\nThe Holy Quran is an ocean of knowledge. It has many priceless gems and it is impossible to enumerate all of them:\n﴿قُل لَّوْ كَانَ الْبَحْرُ مِدَادًا لِّكَلِمَاتِ رَبِّي لَنَفِدَ الْبَحْرُ قَبْلَ أَن تَنفَدَ كَلِمَاتُ رَبِّي وَلَوْ جِئْنَا بِمِثْلِهِ مَدَدًا ١٠٩﴾\nSay: \"If the ocean were ink (wherewith to write out) the words of my Lord, sooner would the ocean be exhausted than would the words of my Lord, even if we added another ocean like it, for its aid.\"\n(Quran, Surah-18, Al-Kahf, Verse-109)\nWhich aspect of life is not covered in the Holy Quran? It contains teachings about everything necessary for mankind. In the past, scholars have tried to classify the Quranic teachings under various topics. According to me, the various teachings of the Holy Quran can be divided into five parts; but even then we cannot say for certain that all the topics have been covered:\n1.The explanation that Allah(swt) is One: Whether it is a matter of creation or a matter of worship, we can only perceive one Allah(swt) Who again and again challenges us that if there is anyone else who is worthy of worship, bring him along and see if he can create at least something as insignificant as a fly. So much so that all the supposed gods and goddesses together also cannot do so and moreover even if the fly flies away with something, they cannot get it back. This speciality of the Holy Quran makes it the best and unique book among all the other religious books as no other book so clearly explains that Allah(swt) is One and He(swt) alone is worthy of worship and the Creator of this entire universe.\n2.The description of those tribes who went astray and were thus seized by Allah(swt) in a painful punishment.\n3.The dialogues with those tribes which were present during the time of revelation of the Holy Quran. For e.g.: Jews, Christians, Polytheists, Majoosi etc.\n4.Description of deeds: Islam gives great importance to one’s deeds. The Holy Quran describes the importance of good deeds along with belief. That is why the scholars are of the opinion that good deeds are an important part of ‘Imaan’ or ‘faith’. Deeds decide the ultimate fate of a person. But along with good deeds, ‘Imaan’ is compulsory. In the sight of Almighty Allah(swt), good deeds without faith are insignificant.\nThe deeds of mankind can be divided into five types:\nObligatory: In the Islamic terminology they are termed ‘Farz’. On doing them, we are rewarded and not doing them entitles us to a painful punishment.\nMustahab: On doing these we are rewarded and on not doing them we do not have to face any punishment.\nHaraam: On doing these, we shall have to face a painful punishment.\nMakrooh: It is better not to do these even if we shall not be punished for doing them.\nMabah: It is the same whether we do them or do not do them.\n5.The description of the life of the Hereafter, the occurrence of Doomsday, judging of mankind by the Almighty Allah(swt) based on their deeds in this earthly life, awarding everlasting joy in paradise to the pious and everlasting torment in hell for the disbelievers and sinners. This is the speciality of the Holy Quran and we find these things mentioned in it again and again unlike in the other religious books which have little or no clear description of the Hereafter.\nExplanations of the Holy Quran\nWe can divide the explanations of the Holy Quran into two parts:\nFirst: ‘Tafseer Bilmasoor’ – it means the explanation based on the Holy Quran, sahih hadith and the sayings of the sahabas. This has already been explained above.\nImportant commentaries of ‘Tafseer Bilmasoor’ are:\n1.Ibn-Jareer Tabri(224-310 A.H): Its first edition is in six parts. Research for the second edition has been done by Ahmad Shakir and Mahmood Shakir. This edition has been published in 16 volumes. After further research, Dr. Abdullah Turkey has published it in 26 parts.\n2.Ibn-Kaseer(700-774 A.H): This is the most famous ‘Tafseer Bilmasoor’. This is in eight volumes and many editions have been published.\n3.The scholar, Shaik Muhammad-bin-Ali Shaukani (1173-1250 A.H) has authored more than a hundred books and among them tafseer ‘Fathul-Kadeer’ and the explanation of hadith ‘Nailul-Autaar’ are famous.\nSecond: ‘Tafseer Birraay’(that is, those commentaries which are based on one’s opinions). This does not mean that man does not contemplate on the Holy Quran. In fact the Holy Quran itself invites us to study it:\n﴿كِتَابٌ أَنزَلْنَاهُ إِلَيْكَ مُبَارَكٌ لِّيَدَّبَّرُوا آيَاتِهِ وَلِيَتَذَكَّرَ أُولُو الْأَلْبَابِ ٢٩﴾\n(Here is) a Book which We have sent down unto thee, full of blessings, that they may meditate on its Signs, and that men of understanding may receive admonition.\n(Quran, Surah-38, Saad, Verse-29)\n﴿أَمْ حَسِبَ الَّذِينَ فِي قُلُوبِهِم مَّرَضٌ أَن لَّن يُخْرِجَ اللَّـهُ أَضْغَانَهُمْ ٢٩﴾\nOr do those in whose hearts is a disease, think that Allah will not bring to light all their rancour?\n(Quran, Surah-47, Muhammad, Verse-29)\n‘Tafseer Birraay’ actually means that the commentator first creates his own opinions and then tries to fit in the teachings of the Holy Quran into his opinion-mould. That is why this has been criticized in one hadith as:\n‘Anyone who declares his opinions which are not based on the knowledge of the Quran is destined for the fire.’\nFamous commentaries of ‘Tafseer Birraay’:\n1.‘Kashaaf’ was written by Mahmood-bin-Umar Zamkhashri who was given the title ‘Jarullah’. He was born in 467 A.H and died in 538 A.H. He was a famous Muattazli and wrote the commentary upon the insistence of the other Muattazlis. He clearly employed ‘Tafseer Birraay’ and thus used hadith in a very few places.\n2.‘Mufatihul Ghaiyb’ was authored by Raazi (544-606 A.H). It is enough to say that it has everything but explanation. So, the scholars have not welcomed it. But Raazi has taken care that wherever Zamkhashri has described ‘Etizaal’, in his commentary, he has tried to condemn it. But even he has employed the principle of ‘Tafseer Birraay’.\nThere is a third interpretation of the Holy Quran which is the scientific approach. This concept originated in the eighteenth century A.D when Europe made great advances in science. The Muslim scientists started seeking the explanation of the scientific principles in the Holy Quran. The most famous commentary is the ‘Al-Jawahir Fi Tafseer Quran’ by the Egyptian scientist Shaikh Tantawi Johri who was born in 1870 A.D. The book was published in 26 volumes and according to him there are approximately 750 verses in the Holy Quran which are connected to science and astronomy. Muslims had never given a thought to this aspect of the Holy Quran and hence, he wrote this book. But it is not possible to completely agree with his opinions.\nThese are a few of the famous commentaries of the Holy Quran; but it is impossible to give the complete details of all the work done in this field. The Quran has been translated into more than a hundred languages. In the Arabic language alone, its commentaries have reached 6124, the details of which are given in the ‘List of Quran commentaries’ published by King Fahd Quran Publishing House."],[264,"§Quranic teachings about good behavior\nThe Holy Quran is an encyclopedia of good behavior and good character and it is impossible to try to enumerate them in a few pages. So, a few have been described here:\nLove and kindness:\n﴿وَمِنْ آيَاتِهِ أَنْ خَلَقَ لَكُم مِّنْ أَنفُسِكُمْ أَزْوَاجًا لِّتَسْكُنُوا إِلَيْهَا وَجَعَلَ بَيْنَكُم مَّوَدَّةً وَرَحْمَةً ۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَآيَاتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يَتَفَكَّرُونَ ٢١﴾\nAnd among His Signs is this, that He created for you mates from among yourselves, that ye may dwell in tranquillity with them, and He has put love and mercy between your (hearts): verily in that are Signs for those who reflect.\n(Quran, Surah-30, Ar-Room, Verse-21)\nHelp each other:\nوَلَا يَجْرِمَنَّكُمْ شَنَآنُ قَوْمٍ أَن صَدُّوكُمْ عَنِ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ أَن تَعْتَدُوا ۘ وَتَعَاوَنُوا عَلَى الْبِرِّ وَالتَّقْوَىٰ ۖ وَلَا تَعَاوَنُوا عَلَى الْإِثْمِ وَالْعُدْوَانِ ۚ وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ ۖ إِنَّ اللَّهَ شَدِيدُ الْعِقَابِ\nlet not the hatred of some people in (once) shutting you out of the Sacred Mosque lead you to transgression (and hostility on your part). Help ye one another in righteousness and piety, but help ye not one another in sin and rancour: fear Allah: for Allah is strict in punishment.\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Maaida, Verse-2)\nCommand to act justly:\n﴿إِنَّ اللَّـهَ يَأْمُرُ بِالْعَدْلِ وَالْإِحْسَانِ وَإِيتَاءِ ذِي الْقُرْبَىٰ وَيَنْهَىٰ عَنِ الْفَحْشَاءِ وَالْمُنكَرِ وَالْبَغْيِ ۚ يَعِظُكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَذَكَّرُونَ ٩٠﴾\nAllah commands justice, the doing of good, and liberality to kith and kin, and He forbids all shameful deeds, and injustice and rebellion: He instructs you, that ye may receive admonition.\n(Quran, Surah-16, An-Nahl, Verse-90)\nSpeak kindly and fairly to others\nSpeaking fairly to others was included in the covenant which Allah(swt) took from the Bani-Israel, but they broke it:\n﴿وَإِذْ أَخَذْنَا مِيثَاقَ بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ لَا تَعْبُدُونَ إِلَّا اللَّـهَ وَبِالْوَالِدَيْنِ إِحْسَانًا وَذِي الْقُرْبَىٰ وَالْيَتَامَىٰ وَالْمَسَاكِينِ وَقُولُوا لِلنَّاسِ حُسْنًا وَأَقِيمُوا الصَّلَاةَ وَآتُوا الزَّكَاةَ ثُمَّ تَوَلَّيْتُمْ إِلَّا قَلِيلًا مِّنكُمْ وَأَنتُم مُّعْرِضُونَ ٨٣﴾\nAnd remember We took a covenant from the Children of Israel (to this effect): Worship none but Allah; treat with kindness your parents and kindred, and orphans and those in need; speak fair to the people; be steadfast in prayer; and practise regular charity. Then did ye turn back, except a few among you, and ye backslide (even now).\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-83)\nReturn evil with good\n﴿وَلَا تَسْتَوِي الْحَسَنَةُ وَلَا السَّيِّئَةُ ۚ ادْفَعْ بِالَّتِي هِيَ أَحْسَنُ فَإِذَا الَّذِي بَيْنَكَ وَبَيْنَهُ عَدَاوَةٌ كَأَنَّهُ وَلِيٌّ حَمِيمٌ ٣٤ وَمَا يُلَقَّاهَا إِلَّا الَّذِينَ صَبَرُوا وَمَا يُلَقَّاهَا إِلَّا ذُو حَظٍّ عَظِيمٍ ٣٥ وَإِمَّا يَنزَغَنَّكَ مِنَ الشَّيْطَانِ نَزْغٌ فَاسْتَعِذْ بِاللَّـهِ ۖ إِنَّهُ هُوَ السَّمِيعُ الْعَلِيمُ ٣٦﴾\nNor can goodness and Evil be equal. Repel (Evil) with what is better: Then will he between whom and thee was hatred become as it were thy friend and intimate! And no one will be granted such goodness except those who exercise patience and self-restraint,- none but persons of the greatest good fortune. And if (at any time) an incitement to discord is made to thee by the Evil One, seek refuge in Allah. He is the One Who hears and knows all things.\n(Quran, Surah-41, Fussilat, Verses-34-36)\nSpeak the right and straight word\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اتَّقُوا اللَّـهَ وَقُولُوا قَوْلًا سَدِيدًا ٧٠ يُصْلِحْ لَكُمْ أَعْمَالَكُمْ وَيَغْفِرْ لَكُمْ ذُنُوبَكُمْ ۗ وَمَن يُطِعِ اللَّـهَ وَرَسُولَهُ فَقَدْ فَازَ فَوْزًا عَظِيمًا ٧١﴾\nO ye who believe! Fear Allah, and (always) say a word directed to the Right: That He may make your conduct whole and sound and forgive you your sins: He that obeys Allah and His Messenger, has already attained the highest achievement.\n(Quran, Surah-33, Al-Ahzab, Verses-70-71)\nThe qualities of the successful believers:\n﴿قَدْ أَفْلَحَ الْمُؤْمِنُونَ ١ الَّذِينَ هُمْ فِي صَلَاتِهِمْ خَاشِعُونَ ٢ وَالَّذِينَ هُمْ عَنِ اللَّغْوِ مُعْرِضُونَ ٣ وَالَّذِينَ هُمْ لِلزَّكَاةِ فَاعِلُونَ ٤ وَالَّذِينَ هُمْ لِفُرُوجِهِمْ حَافِظُونَ ٥ إِلَّا عَلَىٰ أَزْوَاجِهِمْ أَوْ مَا مَلَكَتْ أَيْمَانُهُمْ فَإِنَّهُمْ غَيْرُ مَلُومِينَ ٦ فَمَنِ ابْتَغَىٰ وَرَاءَ ذَٰلِكَ فَأُولَـٰئِكَ هُمُ الْعَادُونَ ٧ وَالَّذِينَ هُمْ لِأَمَانَاتِهِمْ وَعَهْدِهِمْ رَاعُونَ ٨ وَالَّذِينَ هُمْ عَلَىٰ صَلَوَاتِهِمْ يُحَافِظُونَ ٩ أُولَـٰئِكَ هُمُ الْوَارِثُونَ ١٠ الَّذِينَ يَرِثُونَ الْفِرْدَوْسَ هُمْ فِيهَا خَالِدُونَ ١١﴾\nCertainly will the believers have succeeded: They who are during their prayer humbly submissive. And they who turn away from ill speech. And they who are observant of zakah. And they who guard their private parts. Except from their wives or those their right hands possess, for indeed, they will not be blamed - But whoever seeks beyond that, then those are the transgressors - And they who are to their trusts and their promises attentive. And they who carefully maintain their prayers - Those are the inheritors. Who will inherit al-Firdaus. They will abide therein eternally.\n(Quran, Surah-23, Al-Muminoon, Verses-1-11)\nIf the debtor is in difficulties, give him some more time:\n﴿وَإِن كَانَ ذُو عُسْرَةٍ فَنَظِرَةٌ إِلَىٰ مَيْسَرَةٍ ۚ وَأَن تَصَدَّقُوا خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ ۖ إِن كُنتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ ٢٨٠﴾\nIf the debtor is in a difficulty, grant him time Till it is easy for him to repay. But if ye remit it by way of charity, that is best for you if ye only knew.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-280)\nThat is, if the debtor is unable to repay the loan on time, then we should grant him some more time and if we come to know that he will not be able to repay the loan, then we should forego it as a form of charity. This is a very good deed in the sight of Almighty Allah(swt).\nIn case of a difference of opinion, refer the matter to Allah(swt) and the Holy Prophet(saws):\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا أَطِيعُوا اللَّـهَ وَأَطِيعُوا الرَّسُولَ وَأُولِي الْأَمْرِ مِنكُمْ ۖ فَإِن تَنَازَعْتُمْ فِي شَيْءٍ فَرُدُّوهُ إِلَى اللَّـهِ وَالرَّسُولِ إِن كُنتُمْ تُؤْمِنُونَ بِاللَّـهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ ۚ ذَٰلِكَ خَيْرٌ وَأَحْسَنُ تَأْوِيلًا ٥٩﴾\nO ye who believe! Obey Allah, and obey the Messenger, and those charged with authority among you. If ye differ in anything among yourselves, refer it to Allah and His Messenger, if ye do believe in Allah and the Last Day: That is best, and most suitable for final determination.\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-59)\nThat is for the solution of any problem, we should seek the help of the book of Allah(swt), the Holy Quran and the narrations of the Holy Prophet(saws), the Sahih Hadith.\nMake room for others in an assembly:\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِذَا قِيلَ لَكُمْ تَفَسَّحُوا فِي الْمَجَالِسِ فَافْسَحُوا يَفْسَحِ اللَّـهُ لَكُمْ ۖ وَإِذَا قِيلَ انشُزُوا فَانشُزُوا يَرْفَعِ اللَّـهُ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا مِنكُمْ وَالَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْعِلْمَ دَرَجَاتٍ ۚ وَاللَّـهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ خَبِيرٌ ١١﴾\nO ye who believe! When ye are told to make room in the assemblies, (spread out and) make room: (ample) room will Allah provide for you. And when ye are told to rise up, rise up Allah will rise up, to (suitable) ranks (and degrees), those of you who believe and who have been granted (mystic) Knowledge. And Allah is well-acquainted with all ye do.\n(Quran, Surah-58, Al-Mujadila, Verse-11)\nThis means that when we sit in an assembly, we should do it in such a way that there is space for others also.\nLower your gaze:\n﴿قُل لِّلْمُؤْمِنِينَ يَغُضُّوا مِنْ أَبْصَارِهِمْ وَيَحْفَظُوا فُرُوجَهُمْ ۚ ذَٰلِكَ أَزْكَىٰ لَهُمْ ۗ إِنَّ اللَّهَ خَبِيرٌ بِمَا يَصْنَعُونَ ٣٠ وَقُل لِّلْمُؤْمِنَاتِ يَغْضُضْنَ مِنْ أَبْصَارِهِنَّ وَيَحْفَظْنَ فُرُوجَهُنَّ﴾\nSay to the believing men that they should lower their gaze and guard their modesty: that will make for greater purity for them: And Allah is well acquainted with all that they do. And say to the believing women that they should lower their gaze and guard their modesty.\n(Quran, Surah-24, An-Noor, Verses-30-31)\nKind words are better than charity followed by hurt:\n﴿قَوْلٌ مَّعْرُوفٌ وَمَغْفِرَةٌ خَيْرٌ مِّن صَدَقَةٍ يَتْبَعُهَا أَذًى ۗ وَاللَّـهُ غَنِيٌّ حَلِيمٌ ٢٦٣﴾\nKind words and the covering of faults are better than charity followed by injury. Allah is free of all wants, and He is Most-Forbearing.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-263)\nThat is after giving someone charity, if we try to belittle the receiver by boasting about it, it is equivalent to causing injury. Instead, it is better if we just speak a kind word.\nHelping the needy:\n﴿لِلْفُقَرَاءِ الَّذِينَ أُحْصِرُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّـهِ لَا يَسْتَطِيعُونَ ضَرْبًا فِي الْأَرْضِ يَحْسَبُهُمُ الْجَاهِلُ أَغْنِيَاءَ مِنَ التَّعَفُّفِ تَعْرِفُهُم بِسِيمَاهُمْ لَا يَسْأَلُونَ النَّاسَ إِلْحَافًا ۗ وَمَا تُنفِقُوا مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَإِنَّ اللَّـهَ بِهِ عَلِيمٌ ٢٧٣﴾\n(Charity is) for those in need, who, in Allah's cause are restricted (from travel), and cannot move about in the land, seeking (for trade or work): the ignorant man thinks, because of their modesty, that they are free from want. Thou shalt know them by their (unfailing) mark: They beg not importunately from all the sundry. And whatever of good ye give, be assured Allah knoweth it well.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-273)\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) even when he was extremely needy prayed to Allah(swt) that he should not be indebted to anybody:\n“O Allah(swt)! Except You, do not make me indebted to (in need of) anybody”\n(See: Tirmizi 3563 and Haakim 1:538)\nSucceeding through courage and perseverance:\n﴿وَاسْتَعِينُوا بِالصَّبْرِ وَالصَّلَاةِ ۚ وَإِنَّهَا لَكَبِيرَةٌ إِلَّا عَلَى الْخَاشِعِينَ ٤٥﴾\nNay, seek (Allah's) help with patient perseverance and prayer: It is indeed hard, except to those who bring a lowly spirit,-\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-45)\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اسْتَعِينُوا بِالصَّبْرِ وَالصَّلَاةِ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ مَعَ الصَّابِرِينَ ١٥٣﴾\nO ye who believe! seek help with patient perseverance and prayer; for Allah is with those who patiently persevere.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-153)\n﴿وَلَنَبْلُوَنَّكُم بِشَيْءٍ مِّنَ الْخَوْفِ وَالْجُوعِ وَنَقْصٍ مِّنَ الْأَمْوَالِ وَالْأَنفُسِ وَالثَّمَرَاتِ ۗ وَبَشِّرِ الصَّابِرِينَ ١٥٥ الَّذِينَ إِذَا أَصَابَتْهُم مُّصِيبَةٌ قَالُوا إِنَّا لِلَّـهِ وَإِنَّا إِلَيْهِ رَاجِعُونَ ١٥٦ أُولَـٰئِكَ عَلَيْهِمْ صَلَوَاتٌ مِّن رَّبِّهِمْ وَرَحْمَةٌ ۖ وَأُولَـٰئِكَ هُمُ الْمُهْتَدُونَ ١٥٧﴾\nBe sure we shall test you with something of fear and hunger, some loss in goods or lives or the fruits (of your toil), but give glad tidings to those who patiently persevere, Who say, when afflicted with calamity: \"To Allah We belong, and to Him is our return\":- They are those on whom (Descend) blessings from Allah, and Mercy, and they are the ones that receive guidance.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verses-155-157)\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اصْبِرُوا وَصَابِرُوا وَرَابِطُوا وَاتَّقُوا اللَّـهَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُونَ ٢٠٠﴾\nO ye who believe! Persevere in patience and constancy; vie in such perseverance; strengthen each other; and fear Allah; that ye may prosper.\n(Quran, Surah-3, Aali-Imran, Verse-200)\nReturning the things entrusted with us to their rightful owners:\n﴿إِنَّ اللَّـهَ يَأْمُرُكُمْ أَن تُؤَدُّوا الْأَمَانَاتِ إِلَىٰ أَهْلِهَا وَإِذَا حَكَمْتُم بَيْنَ النَّاسِ أَن تَحْكُمُوا بِالْعَدْلِ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ نِعِمَّا يَعِظُكُم بِهِ ۗ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ كَانَ سَمِيعًا بَصِيرًا ٥٨﴾\nAllah doth command you to render back your Trusts to those to whom they are due; And when ye judge between man and man, that ye judge with justice: Verily how excellent is the teaching which He giveth you! For Allah is He Who heareth and seeth all things.\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-58)\nTaking the just path:\n﴿لَّا يَنْهَاكُمُ اللَّـهُ عَنِ الَّذِينَ لَمْ يُقَاتِلُوكُمْ فِي الدِّينِ وَلَمْ يُخْرِجُوكُم مِّن دِيَارِكُمْ أَن تَبَرُّوهُمْ وَتُقْسِطُوا إِلَيْهِمْ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُقْسِطِينَ ٨ إِنَّمَا يَنْهَاكُمُ اللَّـهُ عَنِ الَّذِينَ قَاتَلُوكُمْ فِي الدِّينِ وَأَخْرَجُوكُم مِّن دِيَارِكُمْ وَظَاهَرُوا عَلَىٰ إِخْرَاجِكُمْ أَن تَوَلَّوْهُمْ ۚ وَمَن يَتَوَلَّهُمْ فَأُولَـٰئِكَ هُمُ الظَّالِمُونَ ﴿٩﴾\nAllah forbids you not, with regard to those who fight you not for (your) Faith nor drive you out of your homes, from dealing kindly and justly with them: for Allah loveth those who are just. Allah only forbids you, with regard to those who fight you for (your) Faith, and drive you out of your homes, and support (others) in driving you out, from turning to them (for friendship and protection). It is such as turn to them (in these circumstances), that do wrong.\n(Quran, Surah-60, Al-Mumtahana, Verses-8,9)\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا كُونُوا قَوَّامِينَ لِلَّـهِ شُهَدَاءَ بِالْقِسْطِ ۖ وَلَا يَجْرِمَنَّكُمْ شَنَآنُ قَوْمٍ عَلَىٰ أَلَّا تَعْدِلُوا ۚ اعْدِلُوا هُوَ أَقْرَبُ لِلتَّقْوَىٰ ۖ وَاتَّقُوا اللَّـهَ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ خَبِيرٌ بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ ٨﴾\nO ye who believe! stand out firmly for Allah, as witnesses to fair dealing, and let not the hatred of others to you make you swerve to wrong and depart from justice. Be just: that is next to piety: and fear Allah. For Allah is well-acquainted with all that ye do.\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Maaida, Verse-8)\nEverybody will get whatever he strove for:\n﴿وَأَن لَّيْسَ لِلْإِنسَانِ إِلَّا مَا سَعَىٰ ٣٩﴾\nThat man can have nothing but what he strives for;\n(Quran, Surah-53, An-Najm, Verse-39)\nSinner is responsible for his sins:\nوَمَن يَكْسِبْ إِثْمًا فَإِنَّمَا يَكْسِبُهُ عَلَىٰ نَفْسِهِ ۚ وَكَانَ اللَّـهُ عَلِيمًا حَكِيمًا ﴿١١١\nAnd if any one earns sin, he earns it against his own soul: for Allah is full of knowledge and wisdom.\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-111)\n﴿أَلَّا تَزِرُ وَازِرَةٌ وِزْرَ أُخْرَىٰ ٣٨﴾\nEvery soul draws the meed of its acts on none but itself: no bearer of burdens can bear the burden of another.\n(Quran, Surah-53, An-Najm, Verse-38)\nFulfil your promises:\nوَأَوْفُوا بِالْعَهْدِ ۖ إِنَّ الْعَهْدَ كَانَ مَسْئُولًا\nfulfil (every) engagement, for (every) engagement will be enquired into (on the Day of Reckoning).\n(Quran, Surah-17, Bani-Israel, Verse-34)\nEverybody has to taste the fruit of his good and bad deeds:\n﴿مَّنْ عَمِلَ صَالِحًا فَلِنَفْسِهِ ۖ وَمَنْ أَسَاءَ فَعَلَيْهَا ۗ وَمَا رَبُّكَ بِظَلَّامٍ لِّلْعَبِيدِ ٤٦﴾\nWhoever works righteousness benefits his own soul; whoever works evil, it is against his own soul: nor is thy Lord ever unjust (in the least) to His Servants.\n(Quran, Surah-41, Fussilat, Verse-46)\nPatience is better than revenge:\n﴿وَإِنْ عَاقَبْتُمْ فَعَاقِبُوا بِمِثْلِ مَا عُوقِبْتُم بِهِ ۖ وَلَئِن صَبَرْتُمْ لَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لِّلصَّابِرِينَ ١٢٦﴾\nAnd if ye do catch them out, catch them out no worse than they catch you out: But if ye show patience, that is indeed the best (course) for those who are patient.\n(Quran, Surah-16, An-Nahl, Verse-126)\nThose spending in the path of Allah(swt):\n﴿مَّثَلُ الَّذِينَ يُنفِقُونَ أَمْوَالَهُمْ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّـهِ كَمَثَلِ حَبَّةٍ أَنبَتَتْ سَبْعَ سَنَابِلَ فِي كُلِّ سُنبُلَةٍ مِّائَةُ حَبَّةٍ ۗ وَاللَّـهُ يُضَاعِفُ لِمَن يَشَاءُ ۗ وَاللَّـهُ وَاسِعٌ عَلِيمٌ ٢٦١﴾\nThe parable of those who spend their substance in the way of Allah is that of a grain of corn: it groweth seven ears, and each ear hath a hundred grains. Allah giveth manifold increase to whom He pleaseth: And Allah careth for all and He knoweth all things.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-261)\nA kind word is like a good tree:\n﴿أَلَمْ تَرَ كَيْفَ ضَرَبَ اللَّـهُ مَثَلًا كَلِمَةً طَيِّبَةً كَشَجَرَةٍ طَيِّبَةٍ أَصْلُهَا ثَابِتٌ وَفَرْعُهَا فِي السَّمَاءِ ٢٤ تُؤْتِي أُكُلَهَا كُلَّ حِينٍ بِإِذْنِ رَبِّهَا ۗ وَيَضْرِبُ اللَّـهُ الْأَمْثَالَ لِلنَّاسِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَذَكَّرُونَ ٢٥ وَمَثَلُ كَلِمَةٍ خَبِيثَةٍ كَشَجَرَةٍ خَبِيثَةٍ اجْتُثَّتْ مِن فَوْقِ الْأَرْضِ مَا لَهَا مِن قَرَارٍ ٢٦﴾\nSeest thou not how Allah sets forth a parable? - A goodly word like a goodly tree, whose root is firmly fixed, and its branches (reach) to the heavens,- of its Lord. So Allah sets forth parables for men, in order that they may receive admonition. It brings forth its fruit at all times, by the leave of its Lord. So Allah sets forth parables for men, in order that they may receive admonition. And the parable of an evil Word is that of an evil tree: It is torn up by the root from the surface of the earth: it has no stability.\n(Quran, Surah-14, Ibraheem, Verses-24-26)\nAllah(swt) commands good and forbids evil:\n﴿إِنَّ اللَّـهَ يَأْمُرُ بِالْعَدْلِ وَالْإِحْسَانِ وَإِيتَاءِ ذِي الْقُرْبَىٰ وَيَنْهَىٰ عَنِ الْفَحْشَاءِ وَالْمُنكَرِ وَالْبَغْيِ ۚ يَعِظُكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَذَكَّرُونَ ٩٠﴾\nAllah commands justice, the doing of good, and liberality to kith and kin, and He forbids all shameful deeds, and injustice and rebellion: He instructs you, that ye may receive admonition.\n(Quran, Surah-16, An-Nahl, Verse-90)\nBe kind to parents:\n﴿وَوَصَّيْنَا الْإِنسَانَ بِوَالِدَيْهِ حَمَلَتْهُ أُمُّهُ وَهْنًا عَلَىٰ وَهْنٍ وَفِصَالُهُ فِي عَامَيْنِ أَنِ اشْكُرْ لِي وَلِوَالِدَيْكَ إِلَيَّ الْمَصِيرُ ١٤ وَإِن جَاهَدَاكَ عَلَىٰ أَن تُشْرِكَ بِي مَا لَيْسَ لَكَ بِهِ عِلْمٌ فَلَا تُطِعْهُمَا ۖ وَصَاحِبْهُمَا فِي الدُّنْيَا مَعْرُوفًا ۖ وَاتَّبِعْ سَبِيلَ مَنْ أَنَابَ إِلَيَّ ۚ ثُمَّ إِلَيَّ مَرْجِعُكُمْ فَأُنَبِّئُكُم بِمَا كُنتُمْ تَعْمَلُونَ ١٥﴾\nAnd We have enjoined on man (to be good) to his parents: in travail upon travail did his mother bear him, and in years twain was his weaning: (hear the command), \"Show gratitude to Me and to thy parents: to Me is (thy final) Goal. But if they strive to make thee join in worship with Me things of which thou hast no knowledge, obey them not; yet bear them company in this life with justice (and consideration).\n(Quran, Surah-31, Luqman, Verses-14,15)\nIn this verse, a very highly commendable principle of Islam is explained. That is to obey, love and respect one’s parents in all aspects of this worldly life because it is through them that we are in this world. But if they ask us to commit shirk that is, associate somebody with Allah(swt), then we should and must disobey them. In return for the pains they have taken in bringing us up, we should help them in every way – physically as well as financially. This point can be underlined that Islam orders a Muslim son to take care of his non-Muslim parents in the very same way that a Muslim son takes care of his Muslim parents.\nDo not touch the wealth of an orphan:\nوَلَا تَقْرَبُوا مَالَ الْيَتِيمِ إِلَّا بِالَّتِي هِيَ أَحْسَنُ حَتَّىٰ يَبْلُغَ أَشُدَّهُ\nCome not nigh to the orphan's property except to improve it, until he attains the age of full strength.\n(Quran, Surah-17, Bani-Israel, Verse-34)\nThat is, invest the wealth of the orphan in some enterprise which is profitable and when he attains maturity, return it to him.\nWarning to those who do not give full measure:\n﴿وَيْلٌ لِّلْمُطَفِّفِينَ ١ الَّذِينَ إِذَا اكْتَالُوا عَلَى النَّاسِ يَسْتَوْفُونَ ٢ وَإِذَا كَالُوهُمْ أَو وَّزَنُوهُمْ يُخْسِرُونَ ٣ أَلَا يَظُنُّ أُولَـٰئِكَ أَنَّهُم مَّبْعُوثُونَ ٤ لِيَوْمٍ عَظِيمٍ ٥ يَوْمَ يَقُومُ النَّاسُ لِرَبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ ٦﴾\nWoe to those that deal in fraud,-\nThose who, when they have to receive by measure from men, exact full measure,\nBut when they have to give by measure or weight to men, give less than due.\nDo they not think that they will be called to account?-\nOn a Mighty Day,\nA Day when (all) mankind will stand before the Lord of the Worlds?\n(Quran, Surah-83, Mutaffifin, Verses-1-6)\nThat is why the Muslims have been commanded:\n﴿وَأَوْفُوا الْكَيْلَ إِذَا كِلْتُمْ وَزِنُوا بِالْقِسْطَاسِ الْمُسْتَقِيمِ ۚ ذَٰلِكَ خَيْرٌ وَأَحْسَنُ تَأْوِيلًا ٣٥﴾\nGive full measure when ye measure, and weigh with a balance that is straight: that is the most fitting and the most advantageous in the final determination.\n(Quran, Surah-17, Bani-Israel, Verse-35)\nShuaib(as) had also warned his tribe against not giving full measure:\n﴿وَيَا قَوْمِ أَوْفُوا الْمِكْيَالَ وَالْمِيزَانَ بِالْقِسْطِ ۖ وَلَا تَبْخَسُوا النَّاسَ أَشْيَاءَهُمْ وَلَا تَعْثَوْا فِي الْأَرْضِ مُفْسِدِينَ ٨٥ بَقِيَّتُ اللَّـهِ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ إِن كُنتُم مُّؤْمِنِينَ ۚ وَمَا أَنَا عَلَيْكُم بِحَفِيظٍ ٨٦﴾\n\"And O my people! give just measure and weight, nor withhold from the people the things that are their due: commit not evil in the land with intent to do mischief. \"That which is left you by Allah is best for you, if ye (but) believed! but I am not set over you to keep watch!\"\n(Quran, Surah-11, Hud, Verses-85-86)\nDo not turn away your faces from people:\n﴿وَلَا تُصَعِّرْ خَدَّكَ لِلنَّاسِ وَلَا تَمْشِ فِي الْأَرْضِ مَرَحًا ۖ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ لَا يُحِبُّ كُلَّ مُخْتَالٍ فَخُورٍ ١٨ وَاقْصِدْ فِي مَشْيِكَ وَاغْضُضْ مِن صَوْتِكَ ۚ إِنَّ أَنكَرَ الْأَصْوَاتِ لَصَوْتُ الْحَمِيرِ ١٩﴾\n\"And swell not thy cheek (for pride) at men, nor walk in insolence through the earth; for Allah loveth not any arrogant boaster\". And be moderate in thy pace, and lower thy voice; for the harshest of sounds without doubt is the braying of the ass.\"\n(Quran, Surah-31, Luqman, Verses-18,19)\nDo not enter somebody’s house without his permission:\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لَا تَدْخُلُوا بُيُوتًا غَيْرَ بُيُوتِكُمْ حَتَّىٰ تَسْتَأْنِسُوا وَتُسَلِّمُوا عَلَىٰ أَهْلِهَا ۚ ذَٰلِكُمْ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَذَكَّرُونَ ٢٧﴾\nO ye who believe! enter not houses other than your own, until ye have asked permission and saluted those in them: that is best for you, in order that ye may heed (what is seemly).\n(Quran, Surah-24, An-Noor, Verse-27)\nIf the person is not in a position to receive you, you should return:\n﴿فَإِن لَّمْ تَجِدُوا فِيهَا أَحَدًا فَلَا تَدْخُلُوهَا حَتَّىٰ يُؤْذَنَ لَكُمْ ۖ وَإِن قِيلَ لَكُمُ ارْجِعُوا فَارْجِعُوا ۖ هُوَ أَزْكَىٰ لَكُمْ ۚ وَاللَّـهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ عَلِيمٌ ٢٨﴾\nIf ye find no one in the house, enter not until permission is given to you: if ye are asked to go back, go back: that makes for greater purity for yourselves: and Allah knows well all that ye do.\n(Quran, Surah-24, An-Noor, Verse-28)\nKilling someone unjustly is like killing the whole humanity:\nThe first person to kill somebody unjustly was Cain who killed his brother Abel. Referring to this the Holy Quran says that killing somebody unjustly is like killing the whole of humanity:\n﴿وَاتْلُ عَلَيْهِمْ نَبَأَ ابْنَيْ آدَمَ بِالْحَقِّ إِذْ قَرَّبَا قُرْبَانًا فَتُقُبِّلَ مِنْ أَحَدِهِمَا وَلَمْ يُتَقَبَّلْ مِنَ الْآخَرِ قَالَ لَأَقْتُلَنَّكَ ۖ قَالَ إِنَّمَا يَتَقَبَّلُ اللَّـهُ مِنَ الْمُتَّقِينَ ٢٧ لَئِن بَسَطتَ إِلَيَّ يَدَكَ لِتَقْتُلَنِي مَا أَنَا بِبَاسِطٍ يَدِيَ إِلَيْكَ لِأَقْتُلَكَ ۖ إِنِّي أَخَافُ اللَّـهَ رَبَّ الْعَالَمِينَ ٢٨ إِنِّي أُرِيدُ أَن تَبُوءَ بِإِثْمِي وَإِثْمِكَ فَتَكُونَ مِنْ أَصْحَابِ النَّارِ ۚ وَذَٰلِكَ جَزَاءُ الظَّالِمِينَ ٢٩ فَطَوَّعَتْ لَهُ نَفْسُهُ قَتْلَ أَخِيهِ فَقَتَلَهُ فَأَصْبَحَ مِنَ الْخَاسِرِينَ ٣٠ فَبَعَثَ اللَّـهُ غُرَابًا يَبْحَثُ فِي الْأَرْضِ لِيُرِيَهُ كَيْفَ يُوَارِي سَوْءَةَ أَخِيهِ ۚ قَالَ يَا وَيْلَتَىٰ أَعَجَزْتُ أَنْ أَكُونَ مِثْلَ هَـٰذَا الْغُرَابِ فَأُوَارِيَ سَوْءَةَ أَخِي ۖ فَأَصْبَحَ مِنَ النَّادِمِينَ ٣١ مِنْ أَجْلِ ذَٰلِكَ كَتَبْنَا عَلَىٰ بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ أَنَّهُ مَن قَتَلَ نَفْسًا بِغَيْرِ نَفْسٍ أَوْ فَسَادٍ فِي الْأَرْضِ فَكَأَنَّمَا قَتَلَ النَّاسَ جَمِيعًا وَمَنْ أَحْيَاهَا فَكَأَنَّمَا أَحْيَا النَّاسَ جَمِيعًا ۚ وَلَقَدْ جَاءَتْهُمْ رُسُلُنَا بِالْبَيِّنَاتِ ثُمَّ إِنَّ كَثِيرًا مِّنْهُم بَعْدَ ذَٰلِكَ فِي الْأَرْضِ لَمُسْرِفُونَ ٣٢ إِنَّمَا جَزَاءُ الَّذِينَ يُحَارِبُونَ اللَّـهَ وَرَسُولَهُ وَيَسْعَوْنَ فِي الْأَرْضِ فَسَادًا أَن يُقَتَّلُوا أَوْ يُصَلَّبُوا أَوْ تُقَطَّعَ أَيْدِيهِمْ وَأَرْجُلُهُم مِّنْ خِلَافٍ أَوْ يُنفَوْا مِنَ الْأَرْضِ ۚ ذَٰلِكَ لَهُمْ خِزْيٌ فِي الدُّنْيَا ۖ وَلَهُمْ فِي الْآخِرَةِ عَذَابٌ عَظِيمٌ ٣٣﴾\nRecite to them the truth of the story of the two sons of Adam. Behold! they each presented a sacrifice (to Allah): It was accepted from one, but not from the other. Said the latter: \"Be sure I will slay thee.\" \"Surely,\" said the former, \"Allah doth accept of the sacrifice of those who are righteous. \"If thou dost stretch thy hand against me, to slay me, it is not for me to stretch my hand against thee to slay thee: for I do fear Allah, the cherisher of the worlds.\n\"For me, I intend to let thee draw on thyself my sin as well as thine, for thou wilt be among the companions of the fire, and that is the reward of those who do wrong.\" The (selfish) soul of the other led him to the murder of his brother: he murdered him, and became (himself) one of the lost ones. Then Allah sent a raven, who scratched the ground, to show him how to hide the shame of his brother. \"Woe is me!\" said he; \"Was I not even able to be as this raven, and to hide the shame of my brother?\" then he became full of regrets- On that account: We ordained for the Children of Israel that if any one slew a person - unless it be for murder or for spreading mischief in the land - it would be as if he slew the whole people: and if any one saved a life, it would be as if he saved the life of the whole people. Then although there came to them Our messengers with clear signs, yet, even after that, many of them continued to commit excesses in the land. The punishment of those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger, and strive with might and main for mischief through the land is: execution, or crucifixion, or the cutting off of hands and feet from opposite sides, or exile from the land: that is their disgrace in this world, and a heavy punishment is theirs in the Hereafter;\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Maaida, Verses-27-33)\nAllah(swt) has forbidden all shameful deeds:\n﴿قُلْ إِنَّمَا حَرَّمَ رَبِّيَ الْفَوَاحِشَ مَا ظَهَرَ مِنْهَا وَمَا بَطَنَ وَالْإِثْمَ وَالْبَغْيَ بِغَيْرِ الْحَقِّ وَأَن تُشْرِكُوا بِاللَّـهِ مَا لَمْ يُنَزِّلْ بِهِ سُلْطَانًا وَأَن تَقُولُوا عَلَى اللَّـهِ مَا لَا تَعْلَمُونَ ٣٣﴾\nSay: the things that my Lord hath indeed forbidden are: shameful deeds, whether open or secret; sins and trespasses against truth or reason; assigning of partners to Allah, for which He hath given no authority; and saying things about Allah of which ye have no knowledge.\n(Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raaf, Verse-33)\nAllah(swt) has forbidden suicide:\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لَا تَأْكُلُوا أَمْوَالَكُم بَيْنَكُم بِالْبَاطِلِ إِلَّا أَن تَكُونَ تِجَارَةً عَن تَرَاضٍ مِّنكُمْ ۚ وَلَا تَقْتُلُوا أَنفُسَكُمْ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ كَانَ بِكُمْ رَحِيمًا ٢٩﴾\nO ye who believe! Eat not up your property among yourselves in vanities: But let there be amongst you Traffic and trade by mutual good-will: Nor kill (or destroy) yourselves: for verily Allah hath been to you Most Merciful!\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-29)\nIt is a sin to call somebody by a bad name:\nوَلَا تَلْمِزُوا أَنفُسَكُمْ وَلَا تَنَابَزُوا بِالْأَلْقَابِ ۖ بِئْسَ الِاسْمُ الْفُسُوقُ بَعْدَ الْإِيمَانِ ۚ وَمَن لَّمْ يَتُبْ فَأُولَٰئِكَ هُمُ الظَّالِمُونَ\nNor defame nor be sarcastic to each other, nor call each other by (offensive) nicknames: Ill-seeming is a name connoting wickedness, (to be used of one) after he has believed: And those who do not desist are (indeed) doing wrong.\n(Quran, Surah-49, Al-Hujuraat, Verse-11)\nAllah(swt) does not love the arrogant:\nإِنَّ اللَّهَ لَا يُحِبُّ مَن كَانَ مُخْتَالًا فَخُورًا\nFor Allah loveth not the arrogant, the vainglorious;-\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-36)\n﴿وَلَا تُصَعِّرْ خَدَّكَ لِلنَّاسِ وَلَا تَمْشِ فِي الْأَرْضِ مَرَحًا ۖ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ لَا يُحِبُّ كُلَّ مُخْتَالٍ فَخُورٍ ١٨﴾\n\"And swell not thy cheek (for pride) at men, nor walk in insolence through the earth; for Allah loveth not any arrogant boaster.\n(Quran, Surah-31, Luqman, Verse-18)\nIt is not right to defame somebody in public:\n﴿لَّا يُحِبُّ اللَّـهُ الْجَهْرَ بِالسُّوءِ مِنَ الْقَوْلِ إِلَّا مَن ظُلِمَ ۚ وَكَانَ اللَّـهُ سَمِيعًا عَلِيمًا ١٤٨﴾\nAllah loveth not that evil should be noised abroad in public speech, except where injustice hath been done; for Allah is He who heareth and knoweth all things.\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-148)\nDo not say something and not do it:\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لِمَ تَقُولُونَ مَا لَا تَفْعَلُونَ ٢ كَبُرَ مَقْتًا عِندَ اللَّـهِ أَن تَقُولُوا مَا لَا تَفْعَلُونَ ٣﴾\nO ye who believe! Why say ye that which ye do not?\nGrievously odious is it in the sight of Allah that ye say that which ye do not.\n(Quran, Surah-61, As-Saff, Verses-2,3)\nDo not be miserly:\n﴿الَّذِينَ يَبْخَلُونَ وَيَأْمُرُونَ النَّاسَ بِالْبُخْلِ وَيَكْتُمُونَ مَا آتَاهُمُ اللَّـهُ مِن فَضْلِهِ ۗ وَأَعْتَدْنَا لِلْكَافِرِينَ عَذَابًا مُّهِينًا ٣٧﴾\n(Nor) those who are niggardly or enjoin niggardliness on others, or hide the bounties which Allah hath bestowed on them; for We have prepared, for those who resist Faith, a punishment that steeps them in contempt;-\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-37)\n﴿وَلَا يَحْسَبَنَّ الَّذِينَ يَبْخَلُونَ بِمَا آتَاهُمُ اللَّـهُ مِن فَضْلِهِ هُوَ خَيْرًا لَّهُم ۖ بَلْ هُوَ شَرٌّ لَّهُمْ ۖ سَيُطَوَّقُونَ مَا بَخِلُوا بِهِ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ ۗ وَلِلَّـهِ مِيرَاثُ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ ۗ وَاللَّـهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ خَبِيرٌ ١٨٠﴾\nAnd let not those who covetously withhold of the gifts which Allah hath given them of His Grace, think that it is good for them: Nay, it will be the worse for them: soon shall the things which they covetously withheld be tied to their necks like a twisted collar, on the Day of Judgment. To Allah belongs the heritage of the heavens and the earth; and Allah is well-acquainted with all that ye do.\n(Quran, Surah-3, Aali-Imran, Verse-180)\nIn the matter of spending, follow the middle path:\n﴿وَلَا تَجْعَلْ يَدَكَ مَغْلُولَةً إِلَىٰ عُنُقِكَ وَلَا تَبْسُطْهَا كُلَّ الْبَسْطِ فَتَقْعُدَ مَلُومًا مَّحْسُورًا ٢٩﴾\nMake not thy hand tied (like a niggard's) to thy neck, nor stretch it forth to its utmost reach, so that thou become blameworthy and destitute.\n(Quran, Surah-17, Bani-Israel, Verse-29)\nThat is employ the moderate path in matters of help and charity. Do not be so niggardly that you do not help anybody nor be so liberal that people rob you of everything and you are left in a state of regret.\nDo not waste or be a spendthrift:\n﴿يَا بَنِي آدَمَ خُذُوا زِينَتَكُمْ عِندَ كُلِّ مَسْجِدٍ وَكُلُوا وَاشْرَبُوا وَلَا تُسْرِفُوا ۚ إِنَّهُ لَا يُحِبُّ الْمُسْرِفِينَ ٣١﴾\nO Children of Adam! wear your beautiful apparel at every time and place of prayer: eat and drink: But waste not by excess, for Allah loveth not the wasters.\n(Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raaf, Verse-31)\nAscertain the truth of some information or accusation:\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِن جَاءَكُمْ فَاسِقٌ بِنَبَإٍ فَتَبَيَّنُوا أَن تُصِيبُوا قَوْمًا بِجَهَالَةٍ فَتُصْبِحُوا عَلَىٰ مَا فَعَلْتُمْ نَادِمِينَ ٦﴾\nO ye who believe! If a wicked person comes to you with any news, ascertain the truth, lest ye harm people unwittingly, and afterwards become full of repentance for what ye have done.\n(Quran, Surah-49, Al-Hujuraat, Verse-6)\n﴿وَمَن يَكْسِبْ خَطِيئَةً أَوْ إِثْمًا ثُمَّ يَرْمِ بِهِ بَرِيئًا فَقَدِ احْتَمَلَ بُهْتَانًا وَإِثْمًا مُّبِينًا ١١٢﴾\nBut if any one earns a fault or a sin and throws it on to one that is innocent, He carries (on himself) (Both) a falsehood and a flagrant sin.\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-112)\nMischief has spread on land and sea due to the misdeeds of men:\n﴿ظَهَرَ الْفَسَادُ فِي الْبَرِّ وَالْبَحْرِ بِمَا كَسَبَتْ أَيْدِي النَّاسِ لِيُذِيقَهُم بَعْضَ الَّذِي عَمِلُوا لَعَلَّهُمْ يَرْجِعُونَ ٤١﴾\nMischief has appeared on land and sea because of (the meed) that the hands of men have earned, that (Allah) may give them a taste of some of their deeds: in order that they may turn back (from Evil).\n(Quran, Surah-30, Ar-Room, Verse-41)\nDo not kill your children for fear of poverty:\n﴿وَلَا تَقْتُلُوا أَوْلَادَكُمْ خَشْيَةَ إِمْلَاقٍ ۖ نَّحْنُ نَرْزُقُهُمْ وَإِيَّاكُمْ ۚ إِنَّ قَتْلَهُمْ كَانَ خِطْئًا كَبِيرًا ٣١﴾\nKill not your children for fear of want: We shall provide sustenance for them as well as for you. Verily the killing of them is a great sin.\n(Quran, Surah-17, Bani-Israel, Verse-31)\nDo not commit adultery:\nوَلَا تَقْرَبُوا الزِّنَا ۖ إِنَّهُ كَانَ فَاحِشَةً وَسَاءَ سَبِيلًا\nNor come nigh to adultery: for it is a shameful (deed) and an evil, opening the road (to other evils).\n(Quran, Surah-17, Bani-Israel, Verse-32)\nThis means that we must avoid inter-mingling with the opposite sex as it may lead to temptation which is the handiwork of the Satan.\nConsuming somebody’s wealth without his permission is a sin:\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لَا تَأْكُلُوا أَمْوَالَكُم بَيْنَكُم بِالْبَاطِلِ إِلَّا أَن تَكُونَ تِجَارَةً عَن تَرَاضٍ مِّنكُمْ ۚ وَلَا تَقْتُلُوا أَنفُسَكُمْ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ كَانَ بِكُمْ رَحِيمًا ٢٩﴾\nO ye who believe! Eat not up your property among yourselves in vanities: But let there be amongst you Traffic and trade by mutual good-will.\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-29)\nWarning against flattery:\n﴿لَا تَحْسَبَنَّ الَّذِينَ يَفْرَحُونَ بِمَا أَتَوا وَّيُحِبُّونَ أَن يُحْمَدُوا بِمَا لَمْ يَفْعَلُوا فَلَا تَحْسَبَنَّهُم بِمَفَازَةٍ مِّنَ الْعَذَابِ ۖ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ ١٨٨﴾\nThink not that those who exult in what they have brought about, and love to be praised for what they have not done,- think escape the penalty. For them is a penalty grievous indeed.\n(Quran, Surah-3, Aali-Imran, Verse-188)\nDesiring what is right:\n﴿وَلَا تَتَمَنَّوْا مَا فَضَّلَ اللَّـهُ بِهِ بَعْضَكُمْ عَلَىٰ بَعْضٍ ۚ لِّلرِّجَالِ نَصِيبٌ مِّمَّا اكْتَسَبُوا ۖ وَلِلنِّسَاءِ نَصِيبٌ مِّمَّا اكْتَسَبْنَ ۚ وَاسْأَلُوا اللَّـهَ مِن فَضْلِهِ ۗ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ كَانَ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عَلِيمًا ٣٢﴾\nAnd in no wise covet those things in which Allah hath bestowed His gifts more freely on some of you than on others: To men is allotted what they earn, and to women what they earn: But ask Allah of His bounty. For Allah hath full knowledge of all things.\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-32)\nThis world is full of desires:\n﴿زُيِّنَ لِلنَّاسِ حُبُّ الشَّهَوَاتِ مِنَ النِّسَاءِ وَالْبَنِينَ وَالْقَنَاطِيرِ الْمُقَنطَرَةِ مِنَ الذَّهَبِ وَالْفِضَّةِ وَالْخَيْلِ الْمُسَوَّمَةِ وَالْأَنْعَامِ وَالْحَرْثِ ۗ ذَٰلِكَ مَتَاعُ الْحَيَاةِ الدُّنْيَا ۖ وَاللَّـهُ عِندَهُ حُسْنُ الْمَآبِ ١٤﴾\nFair in the eyes of men is the love of things they covet: Women and sons; Heaped-up hoards of gold and silver; horses branded (for blood and excellence); and (wealth of) cattle and well-tilled land. Such are the possessions of this world's life; but in nearness to Allah is the best of the goals (to return to).\n(Quran, Surah-3, Aali-Imran, Verse-14)\nThat is, use the things of this world according to one’s needs but always bear in mind that the ultimate return is to the Almighty Allah(swt).\nBelief and faith in Allah(swt) is the only way in which one can legitimately fulfil one’s desires. ‘Imaan’ is the way which neither throws us into the ditch of indulgence nor ordains a life of asceticism suppressing all our desires.\nThe life of this world is just play and amusement while the life of the Hereafter is everlasting:\n﴿وَمَا الْحَيَاةُ الدُّنْيَا إِلَّا لَعِبٌ وَلَهْوٌ ۖ وَلَلدَّارُ الْآخِرَةُ خَيْرٌ لِّلَّذِينَ يَتَّقُونَ ۗ أَفَلَا تَعْقِلُونَ ٣٢﴾\nWhat is the life of this world but play and amusement? But best is the home in the hereafter, for those who are righteous. Will ye not then understand?\n(Quran, Surah-6, Al-An’aam, Verse-32)\n﴿وَمَا هَـٰذِهِ الْحَيَاةُ الدُّنْيَا إِلَّا لَهْوٌ وَلَعِبٌ ۚ وَإِنَّ الدَّارَ الْآخِرَةَ لَهِيَ الْحَيَوَانُ ۚ لَوْ كَانُوا يَعْلَمُونَ ٦٤﴾\nWhat is the life of this world but amusement and play? but verily the Home in the Hereafter,- that is life indeed, if they but knew.\n(Quran, Surah-29, Al-Ankaboot, Verse-64)\nThe above are a few principles of good character and behaviour. But the whole Quran is full of such excellent teachings. According to a Sahih hadith, once Aisha(ra) was asked about the character of the Holy Prophet(saws). She replied, “His(saws) character is the Holy Quran.” We understand from this that not only is the Holy Quran an instruction of good character but that the Holy Prophet(saws) is the embodiment of it."],[265,"§Qurbani\nQurbani is a form of worship which is offered to Allah(swt). It was first offered by the two sons of Adam(as) as is described in the Holy Quran:\nوَاتْلُ عَلَيْهِمْ نَبَأَ ابْنَيْ آدَمَ بِالْحَقِّ إِذْ قَرَّبَا قُرْبَانًا فَتُقُبِّلَ مِنْ أَحَدِهِمَا وَلَمْ يُتَقَبَّلْ مِنَ الْآخَرِ\nRecite to them the truth of the story of the two sons of Adam. Behold! they each presented a sacrifice (to Allah): It was accepted from one, but not from the other.\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Maaida, Verse-27)\nThe scholars say that in the ancient times when somebody’s sacrifice was accepted, a fire from the sky would burn up the offering.\nThis incident is described in great detail in the book Genesis of the Bible; but the mode of acceptance is not specified.\n(See Genesis 4:1-7)\nThe Holy Quran says:\n﴿الَّذِينَ قَالُوا إِنَّ اللَّـهَ عَهِدَ إِلَيْنَا أَلَّا نُؤْمِنَ لِرَسُولٍ حَتَّىٰ يَأْتِيَنَا بِقُرْبَانٍ تَأْكُلُهُ النَّارُ ۗ قُلْ قَدْ جَاءَكُمْ رُسُلٌ مِّن قَبْلِي بِالْبَيِّنَاتِ وَبِالَّذِي قُلْتُمْ فَلِمَ قَتَلْتُمُوهُمْ إِن كُنتُمْ صَادِقِينَ ١٨٣﴾\n[They are] those who said, \"Indeed, Allah has taken our promise not to believe any messenger until he brings us an offering which fire [from heaven] will consume.\" Say, \"There have already come to you messengers before me with clear proofs and [even] that of which you speak. So why did you kill them, if you should be truthful?\"\n(Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-183)\nAs far as the custom of burning the sacrificial animal is concerned, Bible corroborates it. According to the Bible, sacrifice for Yehova is a pleasing, aromatic food offering (See Leviticus 1:9)\nBut Islam put an end to the custom of burning the sacrificial animal in the fire.\nIbraheem(as) also sacrificed his only son Ismael(as), which was replaced by a sheep. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَفَدَيْنَاهُ بِذِبْحٍ عَظِيمٍ ١٠٧﴾\nAnd We ransomed him with a momentous sacrifice.\n(Quran, Surah-37, As-Saffaat, Verse-107)\nCommemorating this sacrifice, the Holy Prophet(saws) sacrificed one hundred camels during Haj and distributed the flesh among his people. And till Doomsday, all the Muslims of this world will offer sacrifice commemorating the supreme sacrifice of Ibraheem(as). Calling it a momentous sacrifice, Allah(swt) is giving a message to His(swt) slaves that if they consider Ibraheem(as) to be a prophet, then if need be they should have the courage to sacrifice even their lives. Now it is not proper for anybody to sacrifice their sons as in the case of Ibraheem(as) because Ibraheem(as) was commanded in his dream by Allah(swt) to do so and the dreams of the prophets are true.\nRules concerning sacrifice\n1.Three types of animals can be sacrificed; namely camel, cow, goat etc. as has been described in Surah-22, Al-Hajj, Verse-34.\n2.One goat can be sacrificed for one family.\n3.In the case of camel or goat, seven families can take part.\n4.The correct time of sacrifice is after the Id-ul-Azha salah. If somebody offers the sacrifice before the namaz, it has to be offered again.\n5.It is best if the meat of the sacrificed animal is eaten by self and the friends and relatives and also the poor so that no one is hungry on this day. (See: Quran, Surah-22, Al-Hajj, Verse-28)\n6.Some of the meat may be stored in cold-storage or in a dried form for future use.\n7.The sacrificial animal should be plump, healthy, its nose, ears etc should not be cut, its horns should not be broken, it should not be lame; that is, it should be proper to look at.\n8. The person performing the sacrifice should not cut his hair or nails once the moon of Zil-Hijja is sighted; till he performs the sacrifice."],[266,"§Rasool\nThese are the slaves of Allah(swt) whom Allah(swt) has chosen to convey His message to the people so that the people do not say that the message of Allah(swt) has not reached them. (See: Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-165)\nAllah(swt) sent the prophets with clear proofs and also revealed divine books to them so that the people are rightly guided to the straight path. (See: Quran, Surah-57, Al-Hadid, Verse-25)\nThe Holy Quran describes in vivid detail how the people of their respective tribes treated their messengers and the aim is explained as follows:\nلَقَدْ كَانَ فِي قَصَصِهِمْ عِبْرَةٌ لِّأُولِي الْأَلْبَابِ ۗ\nThere was certainly in their stories a lesson for those of understanding.\n(Quran, Surah-12, Yusuf, Verse-111)\nA few principles in the Holy Quran about the messengers are as follows:\n1.Messengers have been sent to every tribe. (See: Quran, Surah-13, Ar-Ra’d, Verse-7)\n2.The messenger who was sent to a particular tribe spoke the language of those people. (See: Quran, Surah-14, Ibraheem, Verse-4)\n3.If Allah(swt) had willed it, He(swt) could have sent a messenger to every city. (See: Quran, Surah-25, Al-Furqan, Verse-51)\nBut it was not done because the people who disbelieved the messengers would not have believed even then.\n4.The core message of all the messengers was the same; to worship Allah(swt) alone and not to attribute partners to Him.\n(See: Quran, Surah-21, Al-Anbiya, Verse-25)\n5.Some messengers have been described in the Holy Quran but most of them haven’t been described. (See: Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-164)\n6.Choosing the messengers depends on Allah(swt). (See: Quran, Surah-22, Al-Hajj, Verse-75)\nThat is, no monk, rishi, peer, pious person, sanyasi, fakir etc. can become a messenger with the help of penance. Prophethood is a gift of Allah(swt). He(swt) makes whomever He(swt) wishes, His ‘Nabi’ or ‘Rasool’ or ‘Messenger’. Now that the chain of prophets has come to an end, anyone who claims prophethood is definitely a fraud.\nTwenty-four prophets have been described in the Holy Quran.\nHere are being mentioned the names of these twenty-four prophets, the period when they lived and the number of times they have been described in the Holy Quran. The period when they lived has been taken from the Bible and other books. It is difficult to be exact in the matter of a few prophets; especially Adam(as) whose period is more ancient than what has been mentioned in the Taurah.\nS.No.Name of the ProphetPeriodNo. of times described in the Holy Quran\n1.Adam(as)5872-4942 B.C.25 times\n2.Idris(as)4533-4188 B.C.2 times\n3.Nuh(as)3993-3043 B.C.43 times\n4.Hud(as)2450-2320 B.C.7 times\n5.Saleh(as)2150-2080 B.C.9 times\n6.Ibraheem(as)1997-1822 B.C.69 times\n7.Lut(as)1950-1870 B.C.27 times\n8.Ismael(as)1911-1774 B.C.12 times\n9.Ishaq(as)1897-1717 B.C.17 times\n10.Yaqub(as)1837-1690 B.C.16 times\n11.Yusuf(as)1745-1635 B.C.27 times\n12.Shuaib(as)1600-1490 B.C.11 times\n13.Ayyub(as)1540-1420 B.C.4 times\n14.Musa(as)1527-1407 B.C.136 times\n15.Haroon(as)1531-1408 B.C.19 times\n16.Dawood(as)1041-971 B.C.16 times\n17.Sulaiman(as)989-931 B.C.17 times\n18.Ilyas(as)910-850 B.C.3 times\n19.Al-Yasa(as)885-795 B.C.2 times\n20.Yunus(as)820-750 B.C.5 times\n21.Zakariya(as)91-31 B.C.8 times\n22.Yahya(as)1-31 B.C.4 times\n23.Isa(as)1-32 B.C.25 times\n24.Muhammad(saws)571-632 A.D.5 times using the name\n25.Zul-Kifl1500-1425 B.C.2 times\nThere is a difference of opinion among the scholars about whether Zul-Kifl was a prophet or not.\nThe Holy Quran does not confirm his prophethood. But, some scholars based on the Bible have said that he was a prophet. For a detailed account about these prophets, see under their respective topics.\nThe number of prophets:\nHere, only those prophets have been mentioned who have been mentioned in the Holy Quran. It is narrated in one hadith that the number of prophets who have not been mentioned in the Holy Quran is 316 while according to some other hadith the number is one lakh, twenty thousand. But these hadith are ‘Zaeef’."],[267,"§Red Lentil\nIn the desert of Sina, the Bani-Israel were fed up of eating just Manna and Salwa and so they went to Musa(as) and said:\nوَإِذْ قُلْتُمْ يَا مُوسَىٰ لَن نَّصْبِرَ عَلَىٰ طَعَامٍ وَاحِدٍ فَادْعُ لَنَا رَبَّكَ يُخْرِجْ لَنَا مِمَّا تُنبِتُ الْأَرْضُ مِن بَقْلِهَا وَقِثَّائِهَا وَفُومِهَا وَعَدَسِهَا وَبَصَلِهَا ۖ قَالَ أَتَسْتَبْدِلُونَ الَّذِي هُوَ أَدْنَىٰ بِالَّذِي هُوَ خَيْرٌ ۚ\n\"O Moses, we can never endure one [kind of] food. So call upon your Lord to bring forth for us from the earth its green herbs and its cucumbers and its garlic and its lentils and its onions.\" [Moses] said, \"Would you exchange what is better for what is less? Go into [any] settlement and indeed, you will have what you have asked.\"\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-61)\nThis was a sort of threat from Musa(as) that forgetting the main aim of coming out of Egypt, they were worried about eating and drinking. So, they could go to any place they wished and find the insignificant things they wished to have.\n﴿وَإِذْ قُلْتُمْ يَا مُوسَىٰ لَن نَّصْبِرَ عَلَىٰ طَعَامٍ وَاحِدٍ فَادْعُ لَنَا رَبَّكَ يُخْرِجْ لَنَا مِمَّا تُنبِتُ الْأَرْضُ مِن بَقْلِهَا وَقِثَّائِهَا وَفُومِهَا وَعَدَسِهَا وَبَصَلِهَا ۖ قَالَ أَتَسْتَبْدِلُونَ الَّذِي هُوَ أَدْنَىٰ بِالَّذِي هُوَ خَيْرٌ ۚ اهْبِطُوا مِصْرًا فَإِنَّ لَكُم مَّا سَأَلْتُمْ ۗ وَضُرِبَتْ عَلَيْهِمُ الذِّلَّةُ وَالْمَسْكَنَةُ وَبَاءُوا بِغَضَبٍ مِّنَ اللَّـهِ ۗ ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمْ كَانُوا يَكْفُرُونَ بِآيَاتِ اللَّـهِ وَيَقْتُلُونَ النَّبِيِّينَ بِغَيْرِ الْحَقِّ ۗ ذَٰلِكَ بِمَا عَصَوا وَّكَانُوا يَعْتَدُونَ ٦١﴾\nAnd they were covered with humiliation and poverty and returned with anger from Allah [upon them].\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-61)"],[268,"§Religious discussion\nThe word ‘Islam’ itself means peace. Hence, it advocates peace in its teachings. We get a glimpse of this in the religious discussions also. Addressing the Ahle-Kitab (Jews and the Christians), the Holy Quran says:\n﴿قُلْ يَا أَهْلَ الْكِتَابِ تَعَالَوْا إِلَىٰ كَلِمَةٍ سَوَاءٍ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَكُمْ أَلَّا نَعْبُدَ إِلَّا اللَّـهَ وَلَا نُشْرِكَ بِهِ شَيْئًا وَلَا يَتَّخِذَ بَعْضُنَا بَعْضًا أَرْبَابًا مِّن دُونِ اللَّـهِ ۚ فَإِن تَوَلَّوْا فَقُولُوا اشْهَدُوا بِأَنَّا مُسْلِمُونَ ٦٤﴾\nSay, \"O People of the Scripture, come to a word that is equitable between us and you - that we will not worship except Allah and not associate anything with Him and not take one another as lords instead of Allah.\" But if they turn away, then say, \"Bear witness that we are Muslims [submitting to Him].\"\n(Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-64)\n‘take one another as lords’ means giving the right of declaring something ‘halal’ or ‘haram’ to someone other than Allah(swt) as the Christians had empowered their priests and scholars:\n﴿اتَّخَذُوا أَحْبَارَهُمْ وَرُهْبَانَهُمْ أَرْبَابًا مِّن دُونِ اللَّـهِ وَالْمَسِيحَ ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ وَمَا أُمِرُوا إِلَّا لِيَعْبُدُوا إِلَـٰهًا وَاحِدًا ۖ لَّا إِلَـٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ ۚ سُبْحَانَهُ عَمَّا يُشْرِكُونَ ٣١﴾\nThey have taken their scholars and monks as lords besides Allah, and [also] the Messiah, the son of Mary. And they were not commanded except to worship one God; there is no deity except Him. Exalted is He above whatever they associate with Him.\n(Quran, Surah-9, At-Tawba, Verse-31)\nSometimes it so happens that even a clear thing is not understood by people. This is the result of their twisted minds. Even in these cases, Islam advocates good behavior and not force or compulsion:\nادْعُ إِلَىٰ سَبِيلِ رَبِّكَ بِالْحِكْمَةِ وَالْمَوْعِظَةِ الْحَسَنَةِ ۖ وَجَادِلْهُم بِالَّتِي هِيَ أَحْسَنُ ۚ إِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ أَعْلَمُ بِمَن ضَلَّ عَن سَبِيلِهِ ۖ وَهُوَ أَعْلَمُ بِالْمُهْتَدِينَ ﴿١٢٥\nInvite to the way of your Lord with wisdom and good instruction, and argue with them in a way that is best. Indeed, your Lord is most knowing of who has strayed from His way, and He is most knowing of who is [rightly] guided.\n(Quran, An-Nahl, Verse-125)\nAnd along with it, the Holy Quran makes the following declaration:\n﴿لَا إِكْرَاهَ فِي الدِّينِ ۖ قَد تَّبَيَّنَ الرُّشْدُ مِنَ الْغَيِّ ۚ فَمَن يَكْفُرْ بِالطَّاغُوتِ وَيُؤْمِن بِاللَّـهِ فَقَدِ اسْتَمْسَكَ بِالْعُرْوَةِ الْوُثْقَىٰ لَا انفِصَامَ لَهَا ۗ وَاللَّـهُ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٌ ٢٥٦﴾\nThere shall be no compulsion in [acceptance of] the religion. The right course has become clear from the wrong. So whoever disbelieves in Taghut and believes in Allah has grasped the most trustworthy handhold with no break in it. And Allah is Hearing and Knowing.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-256)\nThe gist of these verses is that there should be a discussion between the various religious heads. But these things should be borne in mind:\n1.Allah(swt), who is the Lord of everybody should be accepted as such; that is, no partners should be ascribed to Allah(swt).\n2.There should be no compulsion in the matter of religion.\n3. All religions should be respected. Nothing should be said which may hurt their religious sentiments. The Muslims have been given a clear instruction in this regard:\nوَلَا تَسُبُّوا الَّذِينَ يَدْعُونَ مِن دُونِ اللَّهِ فَيَسُبُّوا اللَّهَ عَدْوًا بِغَيْرِ عِلْمٍ\nAnd do not insult those they invoke other than Allah, lest they insult Allah in enmity without knowledge.\n(Quran, Surah-6, Al-An’am, Verse-108)\n4.Even if these religious discussions do not serve any purpose, there should not be any hurdles in the peaceful co-existence of the people belonging to different religions. Everybody together should strive for a fair and just and peaceful life in which there is no feeling of fear and everyone should have equal opportunities for earning their livelihood. This is what Islam teaches."],[269,"§Revenge\nSee: ‘Qisaas’."],[270,"§Riza’at\n‘Riza’at’ means a woman breastfeeding her child. We come to know from one verse that the period for which a woman is supposed to suckle her child is two years (See: Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-233), whether the mother feeds the child or some other woman. In the first case, a woman may either be with her husband or she may have been divorced from him. In case of separation, the Holy Quran says about the breastfeeding of the child:\n﴿وَالْوَالِدَاتُ يُرْضِعْنَ أَوْلَادَهُنَّ حَوْلَيْنِ كَامِلَيْنِ ۖ لِمَنْ أَرَادَ أَن يُتِمَّ الرَّضَاعَةَ ۚ وَعَلَى الْمَوْلُودِ لَهُ رِزْقُهُنَّ وَكِسْوَتُهُنَّ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ ۚ لَا تُكَلَّفُ نَفْسٌ إِلَّا وُسْعَهَا ۚ لَا تُضَارَّ وَالِدَةٌ بِوَلَدِهَا وَلَا مَوْلُودٌ لَّهُ بِوَلَدِهِ ۚ وَعَلَى الْوَارِثِ مِثْلُ ذَٰلِكَ ۗ فَإِنْ أَرَادَا فِصَالًا عَن تَرَاضٍ مِّنْهُمَا وَتَشَاوُرٍ فَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْهِمَا ۗ وَإِنْ أَرَدتُّمْ أَن تَسْتَرْضِعُوا أَوْلَادَكُمْ فَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْكُمْ إِذَا سَلَّمْتُم مَّا آتَيْتُم بِالْمَعْرُوفِ ۗ وَاتَّقُوا اللَّـهَ وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّ اللَّـهَ بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ بَصِيرٌ ٢٣٣﴾\nMothers may breastfeed their children two complete years for whoever wishes to complete the nursing [period]. Upon the father is the mothers' provision and their clothing according to what is acceptable. No person is charged with more than his capacity. No mother should be harmed through her child, and no father through his child. And upon the [father's] heir is [a duty] like that [of the father]. And if they both desire weaning through mutual consent from both of them and consultation, there is no blame upon either of them. And if you wish to have your children nursed by a substitute, there is no blame upon you as long as you give payment according to what is acceptable. And fear Allah and know that Allah is Seeing of what you do.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-233)\nIn this verse, some problems of ‘Riza’at’ have been highlighted which are as follows:\n1.If a woman has been separated from her husband, but her child is still taking her feed, then she has a greater right to breastfeed the child.\n2.If there is a difference of opinion between the mother and the father about the period of time for breastfeeding the child, then the maximum time for breastfeeding is two years.\n3.The Holy Quran says:\nوَحَمْلُهُ وَفِصَالُهُ ثَلَاثُونَ شَهْرًا ۚ\nHis gestation and weaning [period] is thirty months.\n(Quran, Surah-46, Al-Ahqaf, Verse-15)\nIf the breastfeeding period is two years (twenty-four months), then the gestation period becomes six months. That is, if a woman gives birth to a baby six months after marriage, then it is alright and the woman should not be considered unchaste.\n4.If before the completion of two years, both the mother and father decide to wean away the child by mutual consent, then it is allowed.\n5.If a woman breastfeeds some other woman’s child after the child has completed two years, then ‘Riza’at’ is not established. That is, the other woman’s children do not become the brother or sister of the breastfed child. It is narrated in a sahih hadith:\nMarriage is prohibited between persons having a foster suckling relationship corresponding to a blood relationship which renders marriage unlawful.\n(Sahih Bukhari, 2645 and Sahih Muslim, 1447)\nWhen people asked the Holy Prophet(saws) to marry the daughter of his paternal uncle Hamza, he(saws) replied:\n“She is my foster-niece (brother’s daughter).”\nShe was the daughter of Hamza and he(saws) and Hamza had been suckled by the same mother and hence marriage was unlawful with her and Hamza was his foster-brother. In the same one other incident is narrated. Umme-Habeeba, who was the wife of the Holy Prophet(saws), once told the Holy Prophet(saws), “O Apostle of Allah(swt)! Would you like to marry the daughter of Abu-Sufyan?” The Holy Prophet(saws) asked, “Do you wish it?” She replied, “Why not? I would like my sister also to be among your wives along with me.” The Holy Prophet(saws) replied, “It is unlawful for me.” (That is, it is forbidden in Islam to have two sisters as wives at the same time). She said, “I have heard that you are going to marry the daughter of Umme-Salma (who was the wife of the Holy Prophet(saws)).”\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) explained, “Even if the daughter of Umme-Salma had not been brought up in my lap (that is, hadn’t been a rabiba), she would be unlawful for me as she is the daughter of my foster-brother. Her father and myself were suckled by Subaiba.”\nThen the Holy Prophet(saws) said, “Do not give me the proposal of marriage of your daughters and sisters.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 5106 and Sahih Muslim, 1449)\nAs mentioned earlier, they should have been breastfed before turning two. If it is after two years of age, then ‘Riza’at’ is not established, that is they will not be foster-brothers or sisters. It is narrated in a sahih hadith:\n“The riza’at is only established when the milk comes out of the breast and goes directly into the stomach and this is before the weaning period.” (Tirmizi, 1152)\nThis is narrated by Umme-Salma; but Fatima-bint-Munzir did not hear anything from Umme-Salma because she was very young at the time. But after studying other similar hadith, it can be said that the above hadith is true. Most of the scholars are of the same opinion. There is an exception in one case. If a person has grown up but it has become difficult to observe ‘purdah’ in front of him, then according to some scholars like Shaikul-Islam Ibn-Taimiya, he can be fed some milk as a result of which the feeding woman becomes his mother and her children his siblings.\nAn incident is narrated in sahih hadith. The wife of Abu-Huzaifa(ra), Sahla-bint-Suhail came to the Holy Prophet(saws) and said, “O Apostle of Allah(swt)! My adopted son is now grown up and keeps coming to me as a result of which Abu-Huzaifa seems displeased.” So, the Holy Prophet(saws) replied:\n“Feed him your milk. She said, ”How should I feed him as he is grown up.” Upon this the Holy Prophet(saws) smiled and said, ”I know he is grown up.” (Sahih Muslim, 1453)\nThat is, collect the milk in a vessel and feed him. Sahla followed the advice of the Holy Prophet(saws) and Abu-Huzaifa was no longer displeased. But some scholars are of the opinion that this was a special concession only in this case and not for everyone.\n6.As is narrated in a sahih hadith (See: Sahih Muslim, 1450), riza’at is not established just by breastfeeding once or twice but should be done about five times or at least three times. It is narrated as such in Sahih Muslim, 1452. For this it is necessary that the child drinks milk from the breast of the foster mother. It is narrated in a sahih hadith:\n“Riza’at is established when the child is breastfed when it is hungry.” (so that he has his fill) (Sahih Bukhari, 2647 and Sahih Muslim, 1455)\n7.Just as a foster father cannot marry his foster daughter, the brother of the foster father also cannot marry his foster niece as he is her foster paternal uncle.\nIt is narrated in a sahih hadith that the wife of Abu Kuas had breastfed Aisha(ra). When Aflah, the brother of Abu Kuas came to Aisha(ra) she refused to come out in front of him before seeking the permission of the Holy Prophet(saws). When the Holy Prophet(saws) came home, she questioned him regarding this. The Holy Prophet(saws) replied:\n“He is your paternal uncle and there is nothing wrong if he comes to you.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 2644 and Sahih Muslim, 1445)\n8.If the woman is separated from her husband due to divorce or some other reason, then the husband should give her remuneration for feeding the child and also take care of her food, clothing and shelter during the period of feeding. The rule is that it should be in proportion to the husband’s wealth and capacity.\n9.It is forbidden for the mother and father to cause pain to each other regarding the child. For instance, a mother may want to feed her child but the father may not allow her to do so and this causes physical and mental pain to the mother.\nIn the same way, the father may want the child to be fed but the mother refuses to do so and the father is unable to find a wet nurse. If a woman is ready to take the amount offered, but still the father finds another woman to feed the child, then it is forbidden as it causes grief to the mother. Or maybe the father is ready to pay the amount but the mother just leaves the child with the father just to trouble him as a result of which the father may have to face a lot of problems. This is also forbidden.\n10.If the father of the child dies, then it is the duty of the guardians of the child to do what the father should have done as explained earlier so that both the mother and the guardians are satisfied with each other and neither causes the other any grief.\n11.If by mutual consent, the parents decide to wean the child before the completion of two years and start giving him other foods, then it is allowed. But if both are not in agreement, then it is forbidden to wean him away before the completion of two years.\n12.In the same way, if both the parents decide by mutual consent to employ a wet nurse to feed their baby especially in the case when the mother may have stopped lactating, then it is allowed. But the father must give remuneration to the mother for the period for which she has breastfed the baby.\nThe points mentioned in Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-233 have been explained above. It is imperative for the parents to keep these things in mind and with the fear of Allah(swt) in their hearts follow the injunctions and not cause grief to each other so that the rights of the child are not infringed upon."],[271,"§Rum\n‘Rum’ is the name of a surah in the Holy Quran which is the 30th surah. Along with other things, a prophecy has been made in this surah:\n﴿الم ١ غُلِبَتِ الرُّومُ ٢ فِي أَدْنَى الْأَرْضِ وَهُم مِّن بَعْدِ غَلَبِهِمْ سَيَغْلِبُونَ ٣ فِي بِضْعِ سِنِينَ ۗ لِلَّـهِ الْأَمْرُ مِن قَبْلُ وَمِن بَعْدُ ۚ وَيَوْمَئِذٍ يَفْرَحُ الْمُؤْمِنُونَ ٤﴾\nAlif, Lam, Meem. The Byzantines have been defeated. In the nearest land. But they, after their defeat, will overcome. Within three to nine years. To Allah belongs the command before and after. And that day the believers will rejoice.\n(Quran, Surah-30, Ar-Rum, Verses 1-4)\nTo understand these verses, let us take a look at the Roman reign.\nRome was the capital of the Roman empire whose foundation was laid in 753 B.C. and within just a short time, it had spread far and wide. It had spread from Italy to Jordan, Syria, Palestine and Turkey. Then later on it got divided into many parts. One was Western Rome which later on became Italy and the other was Eastern Rome which was spread to the north and east of the white sea and the capital of this was Constantinople.\nEight years after Muhammad(saws) was made a prophet, a war started between the Romans and the Persians. Thousands of people were killed. In this way, in 613 A.D the Persians conquered Damascus and in 614 A.D the Christians lost the Baitul-Muqaddas. 90 thousand Christians were killed and when this news reached the people of Makka, they were very happy. They thought that just as the Persian idol-worshippers had defeated the Christians, they would also defeat Muhammad(saws) and put an end to him and his religion because even the Christians spoke about divine revelations and monotheism just like Muhammad(saws).\nUnder these conditions the Surah-Rum was revealed which says that very soon the Romans would emerge victorious and the believers would be pleased with the help of Allah(swt).\nThe Holy Quran prophecies such a thing when it was simply unimaginable because the Romans were continuously being defeated and the Persians were simply forging ahead. That is why the disbelievers of Makka made fun of this prophecy, the Holy Quran and the Holy Prophet(saws). But the believers were convinced that the Romans would soon taste victory as Allah(swt) himself had said so in His divine book, the Holy Quran. That is why Abu-Bakr(ra) made a bet with Ubaiyy-bin-Khalaf that if the Romans did not emerge victorious then he would give him some camels and if the Romans did emerge victorious, then Ubaiyy-bin-Khalaf will have to give some camels to Abu-Bakr. (See: Sunan Tirmizi: 3193)\nThen the prophecy came true. The Holy Prophet(saws) migrated to Madina from Makka in 622 A.D. and in 624 A.D emperor Heraclius entered Azerbaijan and destroyed Clorumia, the birthplace of Zoroaster, and ravaged the principal fire temple of Iran. And the Jews were defeated. The king Parvez and his eighteen sons were killed. This was in the same year when 313 Muslims defeated a 1000 strong army of disbelievers. That is, within ten years of the prophecy in the Holy Quran, Romans defeated the Iranians and the Muslims defeated the disbelievers of Makkah in the battle of Badr:\n﴿وَيَوْمَئِذٍ يَفْرَحُ الْمُؤْمِنُونَ ٤ بِنَصْرِ اللَّـهِ ۚ﴾\nAnd that day the believers will rejoice. In the victory of Allah.\n(Quran, Surah-30, Ar-Rum, Verse-4,5)\nThis war started in 602 A.D. and ended in 615 A.D. with the defeat of the Persians. In this period the sacred place of the Romans, the Baitul-Muqaddas and their sacred cross were also destroyed. Under these conditions nobody could even imagine that the Romans in less than ten years would not only regain their kingdom but also gain complete victory over the Persians. In the same way, could anyone have imagined that the Muslims who were being tormented by the disbelievers of Makkah and had no huge army or weapons would in less than ten years defeat them. But the Most Powerful is Allah(swt). He(swt) gives victory to whomever He(swt) pleases and defeat to whomever He(swt) pleases. Can anything match this prophecy which proved a hundred percent correct. This is one of the miracles of the Holy Quran which shall be a guidance till Doomsday."],[272,"§Ruku\n‘Ruku’ means to bow down. In Arabic, when a weak person bows down in front of a strong person, it is termed ‘Ruku’. Islam advocates ‘monotheism’. Hence, it is forbidden to bow down before anyone other than Allah(swt). And this was the message and creed of all the true prophets. As mentioned again and again, the basic message of all the prophets was ‘monotheism’ or ‘tawheed’ and hence they bowed down to none but Allah(swt).\nAllah(swt) commanded Ibraheem(as) and Ismael(as):\nأَن طَهِّرَا بَيْتِيَ لِلطَّائِفِينَ وَالْعَاكِفِينَ وَالرُّكَّعِ السُّجُودِ\n\"Purify My House for those who perform Tawaf and those who are staying [there] for worship and those who bow and prostrate [in prayer].\"\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-125)\nThat is, never keep any idols in My house so that the people bow and prostrate before them when in fact ‘ruku’ and ‘sajda’ are for Me alone. It is also mentioned about Dawood(as) that when he came to know that he was being tested:\nوَظَنَّ دَاوُودُ أَنَّمَا فَتَنَّاهُ فَاسْتَغْفَرَ رَبَّهُ وَخَرَّ رَاكِعًا وَأَنَابَ\nAnd David became certain that We had tried him, and he asked forgiveness of his Lord and fell down bowing [in prostration] and turned in repentance [to Allah].\n(Quran, Surah-38, Sad, Verse-24)\nIn the same way Allah(swt) commanded Maryam, the mother of Isa(as):\n﴿يَا مَرْيَمُ اقْنُتِي لِرَبِّكِ وَاسْجُدِي وَارْكَعِي مَعَ الرَّاكِعِينَ ٤٣﴾\nO Mary, be devoutly obedient to your Lord and prostrate and bow with those who bow [in prayer].\"\n(Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-43)\nAllah(swt) has commanded the believers again and again:\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا ارْكَعُوا وَاسْجُدُوا وَاعْبُدُوا رَبَّكُمْ وَافْعَلُوا الْخَيْرَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُونَ ۩ ٧٧﴾\nO you who have believed, bow and prostrate and worship your Lord and do good - that you may succeed.\n(Quran, Surah-22, Al-Hajj, Verse-77)\nAllah(swt) mentions the characteristics of the companions of the Holy Prophet(saws):\nتَرَاهُمْ رُكَّعًا سُجَّدًا يَبْتَغُونَ فَضْلًا مِّنَ اللَّهِ وَرِضْوَانًا ۖ\nYou see them bowing and prostrating [in prayer], seeking bounty from Allah and [His] pleasure.\n(Quran, Surah-48, Al-Fath, Verse-29)\nAnd Allah(swt) says about the disbelievers:\n﴿وَإِذَا قِيلَ لَهُمُ ارْكَعُوا لَا يَرْكَعُونَ ٤٨﴾\nAnd when it is said to them, \"Bow [in prayer],\" they do not bow.\n(Quran, Surah-77, Al-Mursalat, Verse-48)\nThat is, they are proud.\nThe method of performing ‘Ruku’:\nHold both the knees firmly with both hands with the back completely straight. That is, neither the head nor the waist should be raised. Then remain in this state calmly for some time. ’Ruku’ is one of the pillars of salah without which the salah is not complete because while bowing down, the slave very humbly declares the Highness of Allah(swt) and that is why ‘ruku’ can only be done before Allah(swt). Islam forbids the bowing down in front of any king, emperor, holy person, grave, idol or anything or anybody other than Allah(swt). It is such a major sin to bow down before anyone other than Allah(swt), that the person doing so will no longer be in the fold of Islam."],[273,"§Ruler\nIslam is the code of rules sent down by Allah(swt) for the complete and successful life of man; from individual and social to political and financial matters, all are included in Islam. The establishment of a successful and peaceful society is dependent on the ruler of the state and therefore the Holy Quran says about a good ruler:\n﴿الَّذِينَ إِن مَّكَّنَّاهُمْ فِي الْأَرْضِ أَقَامُوا الصَّلَاةَ وَآتَوُا الزَّكَاةَ وَأَمَرُوا بِالْمَعْرُوفِ وَنَهَوْا عَنِ الْمُنكَرِ ۗ وَلِلَّـهِ عَاقِبَةُ الْأُمُورِ ٤١﴾\n[And they are] those who, if We give them authority in the land, establish prayer and give zakah and enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong. And to Allah belongs the outcome of [all] matters.\n(Quran, Surah-22, Al-Hajj, Verse-41)\nIn the above verse, three qualities of an Islamic ruler are being highlighted:\n1.Establishing the prayer: Prayer brings man closer to his Creator and purifies his soul.\n2.Giving the zakat: Zakat helps in removing poverty from the land because the ‘Baitul-Maal’ where the zakat is collected is used for buying supplies for the poor and needy.\n3.Enjoining what is right and forbidding what is wrong: By doing this evil can be abolished and good propagated so that a peaceful society is established.\nAn Islamic society based on the above principles can be nothing but the best and the most peaceful where both the Muslims and the non-Muslims co-exist peacefully.\nWhile the responsibility of establishing a peaceful society is that of the ruler, it is the duty of the subjects to be obedient to the ruler. The Holy Quran says:\nيَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا أَطِيعُوا اللَّهَ وَأَطِيعُوا الرَّسُولَ وَأُولِي الْأَمْرِ مِنكُمْ\nO you who have believed, obey Allah and obey the Messenger and those in authority among you.\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-59)\nObeying the ruler is one of the duties of a Muslim. Anyone who does not do so is a sinner and a rebel.\nEven in the sahih hadith, great importance has been given to obeying the commands of the ruler because this is how the society can tread the path to success. It is narrated in a sahih hadith:\nWhosoever obeys me obeys God, and whosoever disobeys me disobeys God. Whosoever obeys the commander obeys me, and whosoever disobeys the commander disobeys me.\n(Sahih Bukhari, 7137 and Sahih Muslim, 1835)\nIt is narrated in another sahih hadith:\n“It is compulsory for you to obey the command; whether you are poor or rich, whether you like it or not, even if others are given preference over you.”\n(Sahih Muslim, 1836)\nIt is narrated in another sahih hadith:\n“Obeying the command is compulsory for a Muslim whether he likes it or not.But if commanded to do bad deeds, then he should not.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 7144 and Sahih Muslim, 1839)\nIt is narrated in another sahih hadith:\n“If a person sees the ruler doing something which he may not like, then he should just bear it because if he rebels against the ruler even a little and dies in this state, then his death will be as the death in the days of ignorance (that is death as in the days before the advent of Islam). (Sahih Bukhari, 7053 and Sahih Muslim, 1849)\nIn this way there are many other hadith which enjoin the obeying of the ruler or commander. And this is part of the faith of Muslims. The companions, Taabiyeen and the other scholars after them are unanimous in their opinion that it is compulsory to obey the ruler. And the one who does not do so will be a rebel and has been criticized in the sahih hadith.\nImam Ahmad-bin-Hanbal has said that if he had a supplication which was sure to be accepted, then he would pray for the ruler because in the well-being of the ruler lies the well-being of the kingdom and subsequently that of the people."],[274,"§Sa’ibah\n‘Saibah’ is the name given to the camel who is left free in the name of some god. It is forbidden to ride it. The idol-worshippers of Arabia believed that because the camel was left free in the name of some god, only that god will ride it and hence it is forbidden for any human being to ride it.\nAll these were their innovations. Allah(swt) has not given any such command as it says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿مَا جَعَلَ اللَّـهُ مِن بَحِيرَةٍ وَلَا سَائِبَةٍ وَلَا وَصِيلَةٍ وَلَا حَامٍ ۙ وَلَـٰكِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا يَفْتَرُونَ عَلَى اللَّـهِ الْكَذِبَ ۖ وَأَكْثَرُهُمْ لَا يَعْقِلُونَ ١٠٣﴾\nAllah has not appointed [such innovations as] bahirah or sa'ibah or wasilah or ham. But those who disbelieve invent falsehood about Allah, and most of them do not reason.\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verse-103)\n\"I saw `Amr bin 'Amir Al-Khuza`i (in a dream) dragging his intestines in the Fire, and he was the first person to establish the tradition of setting free the animals (for the sake of their deities).\"\n(Sahih Bukhari, 4623 and Sahih Muslim, 2856)\nIt is shirk to free an animal in the name of some imagined god or goddess or to sacrifice animals in their names, or to make offerings to them etc and Amr bin Al-Khuza’I was the first to commit such shirk."],[275,"§Saa’\nThis is a unit to measure grain which is mentioned in the Holy Quran in the story of Yusuf(as) as follows:\n﴿قَالُوا نَفْقِدُ صُوَاعَ الْمَلِكِ وَلِمَن جَاءَ بِهِ حِمْلُ بَعِيرٍ وَأَنَا بِهِ زَعِيمٌ ٧٢﴾\nThey said, \"We are missing the measure of the king. And for he who produces it is [the reward of] a camel's load, and I am responsible for it.\"\n(Quran, Surah-12, Yusuf, Verse-72)\nThis was the same measure used during the time of the Holy Prophet(saws). This was the same measure used for giving Zakat-ul-Fitr (Sadaq-e-Fitr) or the charity of Fitr. This was used to measure the dates and determine the zakat. Regarding this measure the Holy Prophet(saws) had supplicated:\n“O Allah(swt), bless their Saa’ and Mudd.”\n(See: Sahih Bukhari, 2130 and Sahih Muslim, 1368)\nIn terms of the units of measure used today, one Saa’ is equal to three kilograms. Mudd is also one unit of measure, one Saa’ being equal to four Mudd and sixty Saa’ are equal to one Sak. These measures are described at various places in the Holy Quran."],[276,"§Saad\nSee ‘Alif-Laam-Meem’."],[277,"§Sabean\n‘Sabean’ ‘Saibeen’ is derived from the word ‘Sab’a’, which means to go to one side. In this way the meaning of ‘Saibeen’ would be the people who go to one side. It seems that these people were the followers of some prophet, but slowly they left the path of truth and started leaning towards falsehood. That is why some scholars have said that they were the followers of Nuh(as), but it is not possible to prove it. They are described only once in the Holy Quran:\n﴿إِنَّ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَالَّذِينَ هَادُوا وَالصَّابِئِينَ وَالنَّصَارَىٰ وَالْمَجُوسَ وَالَّذِينَ أَشْرَكُوا إِنَّ اللَّـهَ يَفْصِلُ بَيْنَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ شَهِيدٌ ١٧﴾\nIndeed, those who have believed and those who were Jews and the Sabeans and the Christians and the Magians and those who associated with Allah - Allah will judge between them on the Day of Resurrection. Indeed Allah is, over all things, Witness.\n(Quran, Surah-22, Al-Hajj, Verse-17)\nIt is proved from the Holy Quran that the Sabeans were present during the time of the Holy Prophet(saws). Some historians are of the opinion that these people inhabited Syria and because the people of Quraish would go there for trade, they had full knowledge about the Sabeans. When Islam spread to every house in Arabia, many Sabeans became Muslims and they came together in the city of Haraan in Syria. They even had a huge temple there where they worshipped the moon. They believed that the spirit or soul was very powerful and through it one could reach Allah(swt). Therefore by controlling and subjugating one’s senses, the power of the soul can be increased. They imbibed some of the teachings and principles of Islam like the namaz. They offered namaz three times a day and believed namaz to be the best way of reaching Allah(swt). They did not eat the flesh of swine, dog or any other unclean animal.\nThey achieved great success in the Islamic kingdom and were ministers of the Abbasi Khalifas. They were deeply influenced by the Islamic teachings and most of them embraced Islam. Today, some Sabeans are found in Iraq."]])